     1	# Phase 6.3 — Full bindings over the stable session API · Entry Plan
     2	
     3	**Status:** 🟡 DRAFT 2026-05-30 — for review (Codex gpt-5.5 xhigh, per the decision-lock discipline). Authored at engine HEAD `6c256608522` on `feat/quantbook-engine` (6.4B FULLY SHIPPED — the 6.4 Python-UDF wedge is closed).
     4	**Mandate:** decision-lock §2 item 8 — *"Full bindings (WASM/Node/C/Python) over the stable session API + parity golden matrix. The existing Node binding becomes an adapter to the stable session, not a separate semantic surface."*
     5	**Predecessor:** 6.4B closure (`docs/audits/2026-05-30-6-4b-udf-closure/`). The locked post-6.4B sequence is **6.3 → 6.2 → 6.5**.
     6	
     7	---
     8	
     9	## 1. What 6.3 is (and is NOT)
    10	
    11	6.1 built the binding-neutral `EngineSession` trait + versioned DTOs + the `EngineError` taxonomy, and bound a **first slice** over napi (Node) to drive the IDE. 6.4 added the UDF surface. **6.3 finishes the job**: every command the IDE/product needs is bound over a real binding, the existing Node path becomes a thin *adapter* to the stable contract (not a parallel semantic surface), and a **golden parity matrix** runs one canonical flow through the adapter(s) so a future binding cannot fork the semantics.
    12	
    13	6.3 is **breadth over a frozen contract**, not new engine semantics. The one place 6.3 *must* touch engine internals is the H3 spill-change-log prerequisite (below) — everything else is marshalling + the cross-cutting binding-layer machinery (panic boundary, versioning, event retention, cancellation honesty).
    14	
    15	**Strategic note:** the product wedge (Python-signal → pokeable-sheet) already has its *minimal* Python authoring bridge from 6.4A (UDF registration over the worker). 6.3 is what makes the contract real enough that Node/Python/(WASM/C) cannot drift — the decision-lock §5 risk #1 ("wrong 6.1 API lock → binding forks") is the thing 6.3 exists to retire.
    16	
    17	---
    18	
    19	## 2. The cut-line (source of truth: `EngineSession` = 51 methods)
    20	
    21	`crates/ql-session/src/session.rs:133-326` declares **51 trait methods**. `WorkbookSession` (`crates/ql-exec/src/session.rs`) implements **46** for real; **5** are honest `not_implemented_in_v1_core`. The napi `Session` class (`crates/ql-bindings-node/src/lib.rs`) currently binds **14** trait methods.
    22	
    23	### (a) Bound now over napi — 14 methods
    24	`add_sheet, set_value, set_formula, clear, recalc_dirty, recalc_all, snapshot, cell, list_sheets, close, register_function, unregister_function, list_functions, poll_events` (+ inherent `new` ctor and `set_udf_worker`).
    25	
    26	### (b) Implemented-but-UNBOUND — the 32-method "bind these in 6.3" set
    27	Grouped by binding cluster (sequencing in §5):
    28	
    29	- **Lifecycle / read (independent):** `lifecycle_state`, `validate_formula`, `query_range`, `mark_volatiles_dirty`
    30	- **Persistence:** `open`, `save`, `import`, `export` *(note: `export("xlsx")` needs the `xlsx-write` feature else `not_implemented`; `query_range` rejects `include_formulas/include_formats/include_rendered` with `not_implemented` — surface these as honest Capability errors at the binding)*
    31	- **Format:** `set_format`, `register_format`
    32	- **Structure:** `rename_sheet`, `delete_sheet`, `restore_sheet`, `move_sheet`, `set_name`
    33	- **Tables:** `create_table`, `rename_table`, `rename_column`, `resize_table`, `drop_table`
    34	- **Atomic groups:** `batch`, `begin_transaction`, `txn_add`, `commit_transaction`, `rollback_transaction`
    35	- **Live-grid cluster (H3-GATED — see §3):** `snapshot_delta`, `undo`, `redo`, `can_undo`, `can_redo`
    36	- **Operations (M2-related — see §4):** `cancel`, `operation_status`
    37	
    38	### (c) Deferred / not-implemented (out of v1 scope) — 5 methods
    39	`write_range, publish_dataset, bind_range, refresh_source, materialize_query` — the reserved bulk/SQL/AI surface (their DTO *shapes* are reserved in 6.1 so 6.5 extends, not forks). Bindings surface them as honest `Capability`/`not_implemented_in_v1_core`, never silent no-ops.
    40	
