quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:549:✅ **5.7 V3.6 PHASE TERMINATION CLEAN** (V3.6.0.1 LOCK + V3.6.0.2 D1 + V3.6.0.X AUDIT-CLOSURE + V3.6.0.3 D2 + V3.6.0.X AUDIT-OF-D2 + V3.6.0.4 D3 + V3.6.0.X AUDIT-OF-D3 + V3.6.0.5 D4 + V3.6.0.X AUDIT-OF-D4 + V3.6.0.6 D5 + V3.6.0.X AUDIT-OF-D5 + V3.6.0.7 D6 SPIKE + V3.6.0.8.1 D6 LOCK + V3.6.0.8.2 ENGINE PART 1 + V3.6.0.8.3 ENGINE PART 2 napi + V3.6.0.8.4 AUDIT-OF-D6 + 5 HIGH CLOSURES + BENCH + V3.6.0.8.5 MOCHA + V3.6.0.10 D8 Op::RestoreSheet + V3.6.0.10 DOCS MEGAUDIT + V3.6.0.11 D9 typing-stroke watchdog SHIPPED 2026-05-23 → 05-26)** -- 9 D-decisions per V3.5.0.X Opus § F V3.6 ENTRY READINESS packet.  Status: D1-D6 + D8 + D9 SHIPPED; only D7 (#REF! substitution at V3.6.0.9) remains conditional pending user signal.  D6 perf contract delivered with 46× headroom (1.08 ms at 100 new cells vs 246 ms full snapshot).  D9 typing-stroke watchdog closes R-V3.5-7 false-negative.  V3.6 phase-termination megaudit unblocked at V3.6.0.11 ship.  D1 (Loro UndoManager `set_on_push` + `set_on_pop` callback wiring, HIGH PRIORITY): closes V3.5.0.X conservative `pure_local_frontier` gate properly via Loro 1.12.0's verified API (`OnPop = Box<dyn Fn(UndoOrRedo, CounterSpan, UndoItemMeta) + Send + Sync>` at registry/loro-internal-1.12.0/src/undo.rs:199); REMOVES `pure_local_frontier` field in V3.6.0.2.  D2 (session-wide RegisterFormat FormatTable cache): new `format_table_cache: HashMap<FormatId, Arc<str>>` field + new `CacheEffect::RegisterFormat` variant + new `FormatDefJson` napi struct + `WorkbookSnapshotJson.formats` additive field; unblocks D4 format-aware rendering.  D3 (per-cell op-index): new `cell_op_index: HashMap<(SheetId, RowId, ColId), Vec<usize>>` field; closes V3.5.0.6 R-V3.5-2 perf gap (invalidate_cell O(N) -> O(ops-for-this-cell)).  D4 (format-aware buildHtml rendering): engine-side `format_value` reuse via Phase 4.6 D-1 FormatTable; new `rendered: Option<String>` field on CellSnapshotJson; new `dateSystem: String` field on WorkbookSnapshotJson ("Excel1900" | "Excel1904"; String chosen over wrapper struct for simplicity; napi-rs auto-camelCases at JS boundary); workbook.locale() passthrough + per-snapshot parsed-format cache + Pending-skip per V3.6.0.X audit-of-D4 closures; CSP-safe.  D5 (IDE-facing `appendPutFormula` napi, NEW): thin wrapper over existing `Op::PutFormula`; unblocks end-to-end repaired-formula integration tests (closes V3.5.0.X A-HIGH-2 IDE-level verification gap).  D6 (incremental WorkbookSnapshot deltas): DEFER pending V3.6.0.7 mid-cycle profiling spike; ship only if cost > 50ms/call.  D7 (#REF! substitution): DEFER until user signal.  D8 (Op::RestoreSheet): DEFER until user signal.  D9 (sheet-tabs UX + mid-edit-render guard typing-stroke watchdog): DEFER sheet-tabs to V3.6+ multi-tab redesign per Opus § G; ship typing-stroke watchdog as V3.6.0.10 only if surfaced.  V3.6 sub-step rollout (actual + planned): V3.6.0.1 docs-only LOCK ✅; V3.6.0.2-0.6 priority ship (D1-D5) ✅; V3.6.0.7 profiling spike ✅ (verdict: D6 SHIPS); V3.6.0.8.1-8.5 D6 arc COMPLETE ✅ (D6 perf contract delivered with 46× headroom); V3.6.0.9 D7 #REF! conditional (PENDING user signal); V3.6.0.10 D8 Op::RestoreSheet ✅ SHIPPED + V3.6.0.10 docs megaudit ✅ SHIPPED; V3.6.0.11 D9 typing-stroke watchdog conditional (PENDING user signal); V3.6.0.X parallel Codex+Opus phase-termination megaudit + closures (PENDING at V3.6.0.11 ship; ~6-8 sessions).  Total estimated V3.6 wall time: 14-20 sessions.  **18 risks documented in plan as R-V3.6-1..18 + R-V3.6-NEW (the V3.6.0.7-spike-discovered rebuild_workbook dominant-cost risk, CLOSED-AT-V3.6.0.8.1 via option (a) cache rebuilt+repaired Workbook + clone-and-apply-delta)**.  All non-conditional risks closed; conditionals tied to D7/D9 surfacing.  Plan at `.plans/_active.md`.  ✅ **V3.6.0.2 D1 SHIPPED** at engine `89f5a5f9e0b`: REMOVED `pure_local_frontier` field + dispatch gate; ADDED `pending_undo_cells: Arc<Mutex<Option<Vec<(u16, u32, u32)>>>>` field + on_push closure encoding cells as LoroValue::List<List<I64>> into UndoItemMeta::value; undo/redo use top_undo_meta/top_redo_meta + pre-stage cells for synthetic inverse op's on_push; 2 V3.5.0.X regression tests REWRITTEN to verify partial-invalidate FIRES correctly (not full-rebuild fallback).  ✅ **V3.6.0.X AUDIT-CLOSURE SHIPPED** at engine `(THIS commit)`: Codex Lane A `docs/audits/2026-05-24-phase-5-7-v3-6-0-2-codex.md` (FAIL: 1 HIGH + 1 LOW + 2 INFO); Opus Lane B inline audit (PASS-WITH-CONVERGENT-FINDING).  Convergent HIGH (CODEX-V3-6-0-2-HIGH-1): grouped-undo + merge-interval-undo lose cells because Loro's `push_with_merge` discards subsequent meta when merging spans -- only the FIRST push's meta survives.  Codex empirically verified with `codex_tmp_grouped_undo_cache_probe` (4 stale cells remained post-undo); Opus independently confirmed by reading loro-internal-1.12.0/src/undo.rs:389-396.  Closure: new `inside_group: bool` + `undo_merge_interval_ms: i64` fields on CollabSession; start/end_undo_group + set_undo_merge_interval maintain these; append_op gates partial-invalidate behind `!inside_group && undo_merge_interval_ms == 0` (conservative full-rebuild fallback matches V3.5.0.6 semantics for grouped undo).  Clean fix (`set_top_undo_meta` to union cells) BLOCKED: API exists on loro_internal but not exposed on public `loro::UndoManager`; deferred to V3.6+ pending upstream contribution.  +2 ql-collab regression tests: grouped_undo_clears_cache_for_all_cells_in_the_group + merge_interval_undo_clears_cache_for_all_cells_in_window.  CODEX-LOW-1 (coverage expansion) DEFERRED to V3.6.0.3+ backlog.  Rule 4 arc terminus HELD at 6 throughout V3.6.0.2 + V3.6.0.X (new fields all Copy+Send+Sync trivially; 0 new triggers).  Cumulative V3.6 cycle through V3.6.0.X audit: +2 ql-collab tests (115 -> 117), IDE mocha unchanged at 346.  Audit transcripts: 33 (was 32; +1 V3.6.0.2 Codex Lane A).  Cumulative findings closed across Phase 5.7: 19+ HIGH + 50+ MEDIUM (was 18+ HIGH + 49+ MEDIUM).  ✅ **V3.6.0.3 D2