-v3-6-0-3-codex.md` (0 HIGH + 3 MED + 4 LOW + 6 INFO).  Opus transcript: `docs/audits/2026-05-23-phase-5-7-v3-6-0-3-opus.md` (1 HIGH + 3 MED + 4 LOW + 4 INFO).  3 convergent findings closed in-cycle: **CONVERGENT-HIGH-1** (Opus HIGH-1 ≡ Codex MED-3): cache walker LWW (`insert`) -> first-write-wins (`entry().or_insert`) mirroring `FormatTable::register_at`'s IdCollision rejection at the cache layer; closes the V3.6.0.1 plan body § D2 line 133 locked decision violation.  **CONVERGENT-MED-1** (Codex MED-1 ≡ Opus MED-2): `workbook_snapshot.formats` sorted by FormatId via the engine's derived Ord (Builtin variants first per enum order, then Custom lexicographically by `(peer, counter)`) before returning -- pre-closure was raw HashMap iter which varied across consecutive calls due to per-instance random hasher.  **CONVERGENT-MED-2** (Codex MED-2 ≡ Opus MED-1+MED-3): `collect_cache_effects` drops Builtin variant `Op::RegisterFormat` payloads at the cache walker (matches "ONLY Custom" docstring claim); Workbook-side `FormatTable::register_at` still accepts in-range Builtins as Phase 4.6 D-1 backward-compat (deferred V3.7+).  Codex INFO-1 REFUTED suspected undo-of-Op::RegisterFormat staleness bug empirically (Probe 1: non-cell-keyed ops trigger full-rebuild fallback via the V3.6.0.X audit-closure gate).  +5 ql-collab regression tests (Opus H.1 + H.2 + H.3 + H.5 + H.7).  Opus LOW-1 (CacheBuckets refactor) DEFERRED to V3.6.0.4 D3 ship.  Opus LOW-3 (Builtin 0..=163 docstring drift; ~20 actually preloaded) folded into 4-site docstring sweep.  Cumulative V3.6 cycle (through V3.6.0.X audit-of-D2): +9 ql-collab (115 -> 124); IDE mocha 350/350 unchanged (sort change is deterministic across existing shape tests).  Audit transcripts: 35 (was 33; +2 V3.6.0.X audit-of-D2 Codex + Opus).  Cumulative findings closed across Phase 5.7: 20+ HIGH + 53+ MEDIUM (was 19+ HIGH + 50+ MEDIUM).  Rule 4 arc terminus HELD at 6 (no new fields/variants/structs in audit-of-D2; behavior-only closures: `entry/or_insert` + `sort_by_key` + Builtin early-return).  ✅ **V3.6.0.4 D3 SHIPPED** at engine `119df9b3826` (2026-05-23).  Per-cell + per-sheet op-log index closes V3.5.0.6 R-V3.5-2 perf gap.  Engine surface: new `cell_op_index: HashMap<(u16,u32,u32), Vec<usize>>` + `sheet_op_index: HashMap<u16, Vec<usize>>` fields on CollabSession; new `CacheBuckets<'a>` struct bundling 5 mutable refs (closes Opus LOW-1 from V3.6.0.X audit-of-D2); new `OpLog::get(index)` accessor on ql-oplog (random-access lookup); `apply_cache_effect` signature refactored to `(&mut CacheBuckets<'_>, CacheEffect, op_log_index: usize)`; new `rebuild_op_indices_only()` helper called by undo+redo BEFORE the per-cell invalidate loop (necessary because Loro's UndoManager retract COMPACTS the visible op list and shifts positional indices -- design discovery during V3.6.0.4 implementation; documented as R-V3.6-10).  `invalidate_cell` rewritten to walk via `cell_op_index ∪ sheet_op_index` instead of full log walk: O(ops-for-this-cell) typical 1-3 + O(removes-for-this-sheet) typical 0-1 vs pre-D3 O(N).  `force_clear_snapshot_cache` clears the new indices; new `cell_op_index_iter` + `sheet_op_index_iter` accessors.  +6 ql-collab regression tests (130/130 pass; +6 over V3.6.0.X audit-of-D2 124 baseline).  Rule 4 arc terminus HELD at 6 (2 new HashMap fields + 1 struct with 5 ref fields; all positive Send+Sync via composition; 0 new triggers).  This session counted 3 plan-implement-audit cycles (V3.6.0.X audit-of-D2 + closures + V3.6.0.4 D3 ship), 1 over the CLAUDE.md ≤2 guideline; user-directed exception via AskUserQuestion.  ✅ **V3.6.0.X AUDIT-OF-D3 SHIPPED** at engine (this commit) (2026-05-23).  Parallel Codex Lane A + Opus Lane B audit of V3.6.0.4 D3 surface; both PASS-WITH-FINDINGS.  Codex transcript: `docs/audits/2026-05-23-phase-5-7-v3-6-0-4-codex.md` (0 HIGH + 2 MED + 4 LOW + 5 INFO).  Opus transcript: `docs/audits/2026-05-23-phase-5-7-v3-6-0-4-opus.md` (1 HIGH + 2 MED + 4 LOW + 3 INFO).  4 in-cycle closures: **CONVERGENT-HIGH-1** (Opus HIGH-1 / Codex LOW-2): `invalidate_cell` atomic-swap (build-into-fresh; defer `self.last_snapshot.remove(target_key)` until AFTER all fallible `OpLog::get` calls succeed).  Pre-closure the unconditional `remove()` at entry + fallible mid-walk Err produced a torn-write hazard.  **CONVERGENT-MED-2** (Codex MED-2 / Opus MED-1): `rebuild_op_indices_only` rewritten to use `apply_cache_effect` (canonical walker) with throwaway snapshot/format_cache buckets + local tombstones tracker; gives tombstone-aware index parity with `rebuild_snapshot_cache`.  Also added `cell_op_index.retain(|(sheet,_,_),_| *sheet != id)` to RemoveSheet handler (mirrors `snapshot.retain`; prunes ghost index entries for cells on tombstoned sheets).  **Codex MED-1**: `poll_remote_with_limit` partial-error rebuild -- track first drain error in the loop; if `merged > 0` before propagating, run `rebuild_snapshot_cache` to keep cache + indices consistent with the committed log state.  **Codex LOW-1**: `OpLog::get` docstring corrected from "O(1)" to "O(log N) BTree lookup" per Loro 1.12.0's internal `LengthFinder`-over-`generic_btree::BTree` implementation; invalidate_cell docstring updated to reflect the honest O(ops-for-this-cell * log N) bound.  ide-consumer-contract.md sweep: V3.6.0.4 D3 SHIPPED inline + R-V3.5-2 marked CLOSED.  +4 ql-collab regression tests (134/134 pass; +4 over V3.6.0.4 D3 130 baseline).  Codex INFO-3 + INFO-5 noted for V3.7+ (long-term stable-op-ID migration design; OpLog::append stores JSON-only payload + would need wire-format extension).  Rule 4 arc terminus HELD at 6 (no new fields/structs in audit-of-D3; behavior-only closures).  Cumulative V3.6 cycle: +19 ql-collab tests (115 -> 134); IDE mocha 350/350 unchanged; audit transcripts: 37 (was 35; +2 V3.6.0.4 Codex + Opus).  Cumulative findings closed across Phase 5.7: 21+ HIGH + 55+ MEDIUM (was 20+ HIGH + 53+ MEDIUM).  This session counted **5 plan-implement-audit cycles** (V3.6.0.X audit-of-D2 + closures + V3.6.0.4 D3 ship + V3.6.0.X audit-of-D3 + closures), 3 over CLAUDE.md ≤2 guideline; user-directed exception via AskUserQuestion + "Proceed next" directives.  ✅ **V3.6.0.5 D4 SHIPPED** at engine (this commit) + IDE (this commit) (2026-05-23).  Format-aware buildHtml rendering via engine-side `ql_functions::format::render`.  Engine napi: new `CellSnapshotJson.rendered: Option<String>` additive field (populated when cell has format + value: format::parse the format-string -> render(value, fmt, eval_context) where eval_context.date_system = workbook.date_system() + locale = EnUs + now_provider = System).  Silent fallback to `None` on: no format / no value / format-id lookup miss / format-string parse error / wire-decode error.  New `WorkbookSnapshotJson.dateSystem: String` additive field ("Excel1900" | "Excel1904"; mapped from `ql_types::DateSystem`).  IDE: `types.ts` interfaces extended (CellSnapshotJson.rendered?: string + WorkbookSnapshotJson.dateSystem union); QuantbookCellSnapshot.entries[*].rendered passthrough; `extractSheetSnapshot` conditional include (only when rendered defined -- preserves exact-shape tests); `cellGridHtml::renderRows` + client-side `renderRowsClient` use `e.rendered ?? formatCellValue(e.value)` (escapeHtml covers both paths; CSP-safe).  +4 mocha shape tests (354/354 pass; +4 over V3.6.0.X audit-of-D3 350 baseline).  ql-collab 134/134 unchanged (no engine collab-side changes).  Rule 4 arc terminus HELD at 6 (1 new String field + 1 new Option<String> field on existing napi structs; 0 new triggers).  **mocha-test scope limitation**: full format::render integration tests (Op::RegisterFormat + Op::SetCellFormat + Op::PutValue -> rendered output) are deferred to V3.6.0.X audit-of-D4 -- the IDE napi at V3.6.0.5 D4 has no appendSetCellFormat / appendRegisterFormat method, so end-to-end mocha can only pin SHAPE.  Engine-side Rust integration tests TBD at audit-of-D4 closure.  Cumulative V3.6 cycle: ql-collab 134/134 + mocha 350 -> 354; audit transcripts still 37.  This session counted **6 plan-implement-audit cycles** (V3.6.0.X audit-of-D2 + closures + V3.6.0.4 D3 ship + V3.6.0.X audit-of-D3 + closures + V3.6.0.5 D4 ship), 4 over CLAUDE.md ≤2 guideline; user-directed exception via repeated "Proceed next" + "Ship D4 fully this session" AskUserQuestion answer.  ✅ **V3.6.0.X AUDIT-OF-D4 SHIPPED** at engine (this commit) + IDE (this commit) (2026-05-24).  Most serious audit verdict in V3.6 cycle: Codex Lane A FAIL (1 HIGH + 2 MED + 3 LOW + 4 INFO) + Opus Lane B FAIL (3 HIGH + 3 MED + 4 LOW + 3 INFO).  Transcripts: `docs/audits/2026-05-24-phase-5-7-v3-6-0-5-codex.md` + `docs/audits/2026-05-24-phase-5-7-v3-6-0-5-opus.md`.  Convergent + in-cycle closures: **CONVERGENT-HIGH-1** (both lanes empirically probed): new `Op::SetDateSystem` wire variant + `DateSystemWire` enum (mirrors LocaleWire pattern) + replay handler + `from_qbook` seeds the op when loaded workbook's date_system != default.  Pre-closure Excel1904 workbooks rendered with Excel1900 epoch (1462-day off-by-one).  R-V3.6-11 documented.  **OPUS-HIGH-2** (Codex missed): new IDE `data-raw-value` attribute carries parseable raw representation for click-to-edit; `beginEdit` reads it first (falls back to `data-original-text` for backward compat).  Pre-closure `parseCellRawInput` NaN'd on currency/percent/thousands/date format-rendered strings, breaking every formatted-cell edit.  R-V3.6-12 documented.  **CONVERGENT-HIGH-3** (Opus HIGH-3 / Codex MED-1): short-circuit pre-render when `wire_value.is_pending()`; preserves IDE "(pending)" fallback.  Pre-closure pending+format displayed as formatted zero (Value::Blank routed as 0.0).  R-V3.6-13 documented.  **CONVERGENT-MED-1**: thread `workbook.locale()` through EvalContext (prevents silent forward-compat regression at V3.6.1+).  **CONVERGENT-MED-2**: per-snapshot parsed-format cache (HashMap<FormatId, FormatString>; reuses parse result across cells sharing FormatId).  **CONVERGENT-MED-3**: ide-consumer-contract.md sweep (R-V3.5-4 marked CLOSED; D4 "deferred" updated to SHIPPED).  **OPUS-LOW-2 + LOW-3**: dropped `.to_string()` on lookup result + TS docstring `date_system` -> `dateSystem`.  +2 ql-collab regression tests (Op::SetDateSystem replay + unknown-wire error).  Rule 4 arc terminus HELD at 6 (new DateSystemWire enum + Op::SetDateSystem variant; both Send+Sync via primitive composition; 0 new triggers).  Cumulative V3.6 cycle: ql-collab 134 -> 136; IDE mocha 354/354 unchanged; audit transcripts: 39 (was 37; +2 V3.6.0.5 Codex + Opus).  Cumulative findings closed across Phase 5.7: 24+ HIGH + 58+ MEDIUM (was 21+ HIGH + 55+ MEDIUM).  This session counted **8 plan-implement-audit cycles** (audit-of-D2 + closures + D3 + audit-of-D3 + closures + D4 + audit-of-D4 + closures), 6 over CLAUDE.md ≤2 guideline; user-directed exception throughout via "Proceed next" chain + AskUserQuestion "Close all in-cycle".  **V3.6.0.6 D5 IDE-facing appendPutFormula napi** (Opus § F.5, ~1 session) is the next recommended sub-step.  Baselines tracked: ql-collab **136/136** + IDE mocha **354/354** + ql-collab-ws 40/40 + engine workspace all 30 suites pass.  ✅ **V3.6.0.6 D5 SHIPPED** at engine (this commit) + IDE (this commit) (2026-05-24).  Engine napi: new `CollabSession::appendPutFormula(sheet: u16, row: f64, col: f64, text: String) -> Result<()>` mirroring `appendPutValue` validation discipline (validate_u32_index on row/col + sheet u16 at FFI boundary); wraps existing `Op::PutFormula { sheet, row, col, text }` (shipping since Phase 4.6.x); no new wire variant; no new CacheEffect (the cell-keyed cache walker already handles PutFormula via `CacheEffect::Cell`).  IDE: `types.ts` adds `CollabSessionInstance.appendPutFormula(...)` + `QuantbookCellSnapshot.entries[*].formula?: string`; `session.ts` adds `appendPutFormulaValidated(session, sheet, row, col, text)` typed wrapper (validates sheet/row/col BEFORE the FFI ToUint32-coercion boundary; matches `appendPutValueValidated` pattern; text not validated since wire accepts any string); `extractSheetSnapshot` passes through `cell.formula` (additive; conditional-key discipline like `rendered` preserves V3.5.0.4b shape-stability tests); `cellGridHtml::renderRows` server-side emits `data-raw-formula="${escapeHtml(e.formula)}"` when entry has formula text; client-side `renderRowsClient` mirrors; **`beginEdit` precedence chain updated to `data-raw-formula > data-raw-value > data-original-text`** (extends V3.6.0.X audit-of-D4 OPUS-HIGH-2 § G.2 -- cells with both formula AND value have two raw representations; formula is the more-authoritative source for editing since it's what the user typed).  +19 mocha tests (354 -> **373**): 6 appendPutFormulaValidated input validation (negative sheet, sheet>u16, fractional row, oversize col, non-string text, accepts valid); 4 engine napi (opCount, fractional row reject, negative row reject, out-of-u32 col reject); 3 workbookSnapshot surface (formula-only cell -> formula property; rename-chain repair end-to-end; round-trip via to_qbook/from_qbook); 2 extractSheetSnapshot (formula+value pass-through; formula-absent shape stability); 4 buildHtml emit (with-formula attribute, without-formula td scope check, HTML-escape XSS, beginEdit precedence chain).  **V3.5.0.X A-HIGH-2 IDE-level verification gap CLOSED end-to-end** (engine-side Rust regression already verified the repair; now IDE-driven mocha verifies the rename-chain repair surfaces through napi `workbookSnapshot`).  Tests: ql-collab **136/136** unchanged (no engine collab-side changes); ql-oplog **67/67** unchanged; ql-collab-ws **42/42** unchanged (30 lib + 10 transport + 2 doctests); engine workspace **99 test-result lines pass**; IDE mocha **373/373** (+19 V3.6.0.6 D5 over V3.6.0.X audit-of-D4 354 baseline).  Rule 4 arc terminus HELD at 6 (napi method only; no new structs/fields/variants; 0 new triggers).  This session counted **1 plan-implement-audit cycle** (V3.6.0.6 D5 ship), WITHIN the CLAUDE.md ≤2 cycle guideline -- recovery from the V3.6.0.5 D4 / audit-of-D4 / docs-audit session's 9+ cycle bloat.
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:564:✅ **V3.6.0.8.1 D6 DESIGN LOCK SHIPPED** at engine (this commit) (2026-05-25).  Docs-only lock; no engine source modified.  Pattern mirrors V3.6.0.1 (the V3.6 phase-entry lock that landed all 9 D-decisions before V3.6.0.2 implementation).  Resolves the open R-V3.6-NEW question from V3.6.0.7 spike.  **Option (a) cache rebuilt+repaired Workbook + clone-and-apply-delta CHOSEN**; option (b) read-from-`last_snapshot`-and-skip-`rebuild_workbook` REJECTED because `last_snapshot.formula` carries PRE-rename-repair text (would silently regress V3.5.0.X A-HIGH-2 contract -- IDE would surface stale formula references after sheet rename); option (c) hybrid revalidate-changed-cells DEFERRED to V3.7+.  Locked napi surface: new `workbookSnapshotDelta(lastSeenVersion: Buffer) -> WorkbookSnapshotDeltaJson` method + new `WorkbookSnapshotDeltaJson { changedCells, removedCells, sheetsChanged, sheetsRemoved, formatsAdded, version, fullRebuildRequired }` interface.  Existing `workbookSnapshot()` retained for full-rebuild fallback (when `fullRebuildRequired=true`).  Two-call IDE discipline: empty `lastSeenVersion` Buffer returns `fullRebuildRequired=true`; IDE then calls `workbookSnapshot()` and caches the `version` token for subsequent delta calls.  Locked internal state on `CollabSession`: 2 new fields -- `last_snapshot_workbook: Option<Arc<Workbook>>` (post-repair) + `last_snapshot_oplog_vv: Option<VersionVector>`.  Both positive Send+Sync compositionally (`Workbook` auto-derives via field composition per `crates/ql-storage/src/workbook.rs:295-299`; `Arc<T>: Send+Sync` iff T; Loro `VersionVector` via `BTreeMap<PeerID, Counter>` [historical narrative; V3.6.0.8.4 OPUS-MED-1 corrected the actual type to `FxHashMap<PeerID, Counter>` per loro-internal-1.12.0/src/version.rs:29]).  **Rule 4 arc terminus stays at 6** -- no Rule 4 trigger.  Locked algorithm: 8-step body -- cache-miss + decode-VV + staleness-check + same-VV fast-path + op-enumeration-since-cached-VV + rename-detection branch + cell-only fast-path (Arc::make_mut clone + apply per-op + skip repair) OR rename-full-rebuild branch + JSON-delta-build.  Cell-only fast-path is steady-state IDE-editing happy path; any `Op::RenameSheet | RenameTable | RenameColumn` in the delta triggers full rebuild_workbook + repair walks (because repair touches ALL formula cells in the workbook, not just the renamed sheet -- verified at `crates/ql-collab/src/repair.rs:227-345`).  Locked invalidation triggers: `merge_bytes` + `discard_pending_ops` + `undo` + `redo` all call new `force_clear_workbook_cache()` helper; `append_op` does NOT invalidate (it's the cell-only fast-path target).  5 new risks documented R-V3.6-14..18 (cached-Workbook-stale-after-Loro-retract; VV-vs-op_count-drift; multi-peer-concurrent-rename-cell-edit; Workbook-clone-cost-may-exceed-20ms-at-100k-fallback-to-Arc-COW; apply_op-private-to-ql-oplog-prefer-new-`apply_ops_in_range(from, to)`-public-helper-on-OpLog).  R-V3.6-NEW (from V3.6.0.7 spike) closed as CLOSED-AT-V3.6.0.8.1.  Sub-step rollout: V3.6.0.8.1 ✅ docs-only lock; V3.6.0.8.2 = engine PART 1 (new fields + `force_clear_workbook_cache` + invalidation wiring at 4 callsites + new `apply_ops_in_range` helper on `OpLog` + ql-collab regression tests); V3.6.0.8.3 = engine PART 2 (`workbook_snapshot_delta` napi method + cell-only fast-path + rename-full-rebuild branch + staleness check + bench delta vs full snapshot at 100k cells + napi shape tests); V3.6.0.8.4 = V3.6.0.X audit-of-D6 (parallel Codex Lane A + Opus Lane B + closures).  D6 total arc estimate: 4 cycles across ≥2 sessions.  Files modified at V3.6.0.8.1: `.plans/_active.md` (V3.6.0.8.1 SHIPPED sub-section + frontmatter + R-V3.6-14..18 + R-V3.6-NEW resolution); this file (this paragraph); `docs/architecture/ide-consumer-contract.md § 4.1.z6` (D6 row + V3.6.0.8.1 sub-section preview with napi shape + IDE consumer protocol).  No engine source touched.  No new tests.  No IDE / mocha changes.  Tests baselines unchanged: ql-collab **136/136** + ql-oplog **67/67** + ql-collab-ws 40/40 (+2 ignored doctests) + IDE mocha **384/384**.  This session counted **1 plan-implement-audit cycle** (V3.6.0.8.1 docs lock), WITHIN the CLAUDE.md ≤2 cycle ceiling.
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:566:✅ **V3.6.0.8.2 D6 ENGINE PART 1 SHIPPED** at engine (this commit) (2026-05-25).  Lands the engine-side foundation for the V3.6.0.8.3 napi `workbook_snapshot_delta` per the V3.6.0.8.1 design lock; no new napi surface yet.  Two new fields on `CollabSession` -- `last_snapshot_workbook: Option<Arc<Workbook>>` (post-repair) + `last_snapshot_oplog_vv: Option<loro::VersionVector>` -- with `pub fn` accessors (`last_snapshot_workbook` / `last_snapshot_oplog_vv`) + setter (`set_workbook_cache(Arc<Workbook>, VersionVector)`) + invalidator (`force_clear_workbook_cache()` -- production, not test-gated).  Both fields default `None` in both `new` + `from_snapshot` constructors (per V3.6.0.8.1 lock: `from_snapshot` does NOT pre-populate the cache because rebuild_workbook + repair walks cost more than waiting until a consumer needs the result).  Invalidation wired at 4 production callsites: (1) `merge_bytes` (after rebuild_snapshot_cache; remote ops may shift LWW winners), (2) `discard_pending_ops` (after rebuild_snapshot_cache; fork_at_vv dropped ops), (3) `undo` (AT TOP, BEFORE Loro's undo per R-V3.6-14 -- retract may have included rename op whose effect would need un-repair), (4) `redo` (AT TOP, mirror of undo).  `append_op` does NOT invalidate (cell-only fast-path target; explicitly verified by `v3_6_0_8_2_append_op_does_NOT_invalidate_workbook_cache` regression test).  New public free function in ql-oplog: `pub fn apply_ops_in_range(log, workbook, from_index, to_index, registry) -> Result<usize, ReplayError>` (re-exported via `ql_oplog::apply_ops_in_range`; iterates `log.iter().skip(from).take(to-from)` and invokes the existing private `apply_op` per op; preserves `replay_into`'s from-empty contract; out-of-range to_index silently stops at log end; empty/inverted range = O(1) no-op returning 0).  V3.6.0.8.3 napi `workbook_snapshot_delta` will use this for the cell-only fast-path delta replay onto the cached Workbook clone.  `force_clear_snapshot_cache` test seam extended to clear the workbook cache too (cohesive test-state discipline).  +13 ql-collab regression tests (149/149 pass; +13 over V3.6.0.X audit-of-D5 136 baseline): 8 workbook cache invariants (fresh/from_snapshot empty; set populates atomic; force_clear resets atomic; merge_bytes/discard/undo/redo invalidate; append_op preserves; Arc identity preserved through setter) + 4 apply_ops_in_range correctness (empty noop; full-range matches replay_into; forward-from-partial composes correctly; oversized to_index saturates at log end) + 1 cache discipline (Arc ptr_eq through setter).  No new napi (V3.6.0.8.3 scope); no IDE / mocha changes (mocha baseline 384/384 unchanged); engine workspace release build clean.  Rule 4 arc terminus HELD at 6 (per the V3.6.0.8.1 lock: Workbook auto-derives Send+Sync via field composition at `crates/ql-storage/src/workbook.rs:295-299`; Arc<T>: Send+Sync iff T; VersionVector via Loro's `BTreeMap<PeerID, Counter>` [historical narrative; V3.6.0.8.4 OPUS-MED-1 corrected the actual type to `FxHashMap<PeerID, Counter>`]; Option<X>: Send+Sync iff X; 0 new triggers).  R-V3.6-14 (cached Workbook stale after Loro retract) CLOSURE LANDED via the undo + redo top-of-method clear discipline.  R-V3.6-15 (VV vs op_count drift) debug-assert deferred to V3.6.0.8.3 -- the invariant is "set together / clear together" not "monotonic drift" at this layer.  R-V3.6-17 (Workbook clone cost) profiled at V3.6.0.8.3.  R-V3.6-18 (apply_op private) CLOSED via the new `apply_ops_in_range` public helper.  This session counted **2 plan-implement-audit cycles** (V3.6.0.8.1 docs lock + V3.6.0.8.2 engine PART 1), AT the CLAUDE.md ≤2 cycle ceiling.
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:568:✅ **V3.6.0.8.3 D6 ENGINE PART 2 napi SHIPPED** at engine (this commit) + IDE (this commit) (2026-05-25; user-directed cycle-3 override of the CLAUDE.md ≤2 cycle ceiling).  Lands the napi surface for incremental WorkbookSnapshot deltas per the V3.6.0.8.1 design lock.  New `WorkbookSnapshotDeltaJson` napi struct (`changedCells: Vec<ChangedCellJson>` + `removedCells: Vec<RemovedCellJson>` + `sheetsChanged: Vec<SheetSnapshotJson>` + `sheetsRemoved: Vec<u32>` + `formatsAdded: Vec<FormatDefJson>` + `version: Buffer` + `fullRebuildRequired: bool`) + 2 helper structs `ChangedCellJson { sheet, cell: CellSnapshotJson }` + `RemovedCellJson { sheet, row, col }`.  New `#[napi(js_name = "workbookSnapshotDelta")] CollabSession::workbookSnapshotDelta(lastSeenVersion: Buffer)` method implementing the V3.6.0.8.1 8-step algorithm: cache-miss + decode-VV + staleness + same-VV-fast-path + op-enumeration + rename-detection + cell-only-fast-path (Arc-deref-clone + ql_oplog::apply_ops_in_range + skip repair walks) + JSON-delta-build.  Rename ops trigger fullRebuild fallback (locked at V3.6.0.8.1 -- the rename delta would degenerate to "all cells with formulas" anyway).  Existing `workbookSnapshot` napi now populates the cache via `set_workbook_cache(Arc::clone(&workbook), oplog_vv())` after `rebuild_workbook`; `workbook` wrapped in `Arc` BEFORE rendering so no double-clone (rendering reads through Arc::deref).  Added `last_snapshot_op_count: Option<usize>` 3rd cache field (revision to V3.6.0.8.2's 2-field cache invariants -- delta path derives the replay slice `[op_count, log.len())` without a VV->op_count walk; preserves the "all Some / all None" invariant); extended `set_workbook_cache` (pins op_count alongside VV) + `force_clear_workbook_cache` (clears all 3 fields) + new `last_snapshot_op_count()` accessor.  New `pub fn oplog_vv(&self)` + `pub fn log(&self) -> &OpLog` accessors on `CollabSession` so the napi can grab the VV at populate time + enumerate ops at delta time.  `loro::VersionVector` re-exported as `ql_oplog::VersionVector` for ergonomics (avoids a direct loro dep on ql-bindings-node).  New free fns `empty_delta` + `classify_delta_op` at file scope (helpers; `classify_delta_op` recurses into `Op::BatchCommit` mirroring V3.4.0.X HIGH-1 walker discipline).  IDE: types.ts adds `WorkbookSnapshotDeltaJson` + `ChangedCellJson` + `RemovedCellJson` interfaces + `CollabSessionInstance.workbookSnapshotDelta(lastSeenVersion: Buffer): WorkbookSnapshotDeltaJson` method.  +6 mocha shape tests (390/390 pass; +6 over V3.6.0.X audit-of-D5 live 384 baseline -- the 381 documented baseline was a 3-count undercount): empty Buffer + no-cache + same-VV fast-path + cell-only emits changes + rename triggers fullRebuild + undo invalidates cache.  Tests: ql-collab 149/149 unchanged (V3.6.0.8.2 baseline preserved; new op_count field naturally pinned by existing set_workbook_cache test calls) + ql-oplog 67/67 + IDE mocha **390/390** + engine workspace release build clean.  Rule 4 arc terminus HELD at 6 (all new napi struct fields + 1 new `last_snapshot_op_count: Option<usize>` cache field are positive Send+Sync composition; 0 new triggers).  V3.6.0.8.3 scope limitations: `removedCells` always empty (V3.7+); `sheetsChanged` always empty in cell-only path (cell ops don't change sheet metadata; full-rebuild paths return `fullRebuildRequired=true` instead); rename ops trigger fullRebuild rather than incremental rename delta.  Bench delta-vs-full at 100k cells DEFERRED to V3.6.0.8.4 audit-of-D6 (functional + regression test surface is complete at V3.6.0.8.3; perf verification + R-V3.6-15 full debug-assert + R-V3.6-17 clone-cost profile all naturally fit into V3.6.0.8.4's audit cycle).  This session counted **3 plan-implement-audit cycles** (V3.6.0.8.1 docs lock + V3.6.0.8.2 engine PART 1 + V3.6.0.8.3 napi), 1 over the CLAUDE.md ≤2 cycle ceiling; **user-directed exception** via AskUserQuestion at cycle 3 entry.
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:570:✅ **V3.6.0.8.4 D6 AUDIT-OF-D6 + CLOSURES + BENCH SHIPPED** at engine (this commit) + IDE (this commit) (2026-05-25; user-directed cycle-4 override, 2 over CLAUDE.md ≤2 ceiling).  Closes V3.6.0.8 D6 arc + ships the D6 perf contract.  Codex Lane A FAIL (3 HIGH + 1 LOW + 1 INFO) + Opus Lane B PASS-WITH-FINDINGS (3 HIGH + 5 MED + 3 LOW + 1 INFO) audit transcripts at `docs/audits/2026-05-25-phase-5-7-v3-6-0-8-{codex,opus}.md`; in-cycle closure summary at `docs/audits/2026-05-25-phase-5-7-v3-6-0-8-closures.md`.  **5 HIGH closed in-cycle**: (1) CONVERGENT-HIGH-1 (Codex-HIGH-2 ≡ Opus-HIGH-1) — `classify_delta_op` allowlist for metadata ops (silent data loss on AddSheet / MoveSheet / CreateTable / DropTable / ResizeTable / SetName / SetLocale / SetReferenceMode / SetDateSystem; pre-closure these were caught by `_=>{}` catch-all + ALSO advanced the cache token so IDE got empty delta + new version while engine had new sheets); (2) Codex-HIGH-1 — `poll_remote_with_limit` was a 5th log-mutation site missed by V3.6.0.8.2 invalidation discipline (force_clear_workbook_cache after rebuild_snapshot_cache in the `merged > 0` block); (3) Codex-HIGH-3 — new `pub fn snapshot_cell(sheet, row, col) -> Option<CellState>` O(1) HashMap.get accessor on CollabSession replacing the O(cells_in_sheet) `snapshot_cells(sheet).find()` per delta cell; (4) Opus-HIGH-2 — new `version: Buffer` field on `WorkbookSnapshotJson` napi struct (populated from `cache_vv.encode()`) + TS-optional in `WorkbookSnapshotJson` interface (so fixture-literal unit tests aren't forced to include opaque placeholders; napi-side always populated); (5) Opus-HIGH-3 — **the primary perf bug**: `OpLog::iter().skip(N).take(M)` was deserializing ALL N skipped ops on every delta call; fix is `for i in start..end { log.get(i)? }` (K * O(log N) BTree random-access).  Applied to both `apply_ops_in_range` (crates/ql-oplog/src/replay.rs) + the napi delta enumeration (crates/ql-bindings-node/src/lib.rs).  **4 of 5 MED closed in-cycle**: MED-1 BTreeMap → FxHashMap docstring drift (3 sites; actual Loro 1.12.0 type is `FxHashMap<PeerID, Counter>` per loro-internal-1.12.0/src/version.rs:29); MED-2 `formats_added` sort by full `FormatId` (engine-side derived Ord: Builtin first, then Custom by (peer, counter)) instead of just `kind` string; MED-3 `Arc::make_mut` docstring drift (V3.6.0.8.1 lock said make_mut; V3.6.0.8.3 ships `(*cached_arc).clone()` always-clone -- correct because cached_arc capture has strong_count >= 2 so make_mut would clone anyway); MED-4 `Workbook::clone()` cost profile via new `bench_workbook_clone` micro-bench (1k=7 μs / 10k=69 μs / 100k=692 μs; well under 20 ms threshold; R-V3.6-17 CLOSED).  Deferred to V3.6.0.8.5+: Opus-MED-5 comprehensive mocha coverage (multi-peer / undo / redo / AddSheet-in-delta / SetCellFormat-in-delta / BatchCommit-in-delta / chained-delta regressions); Opus-LOW-1 empty-stack undo/redo over-invalidation; Opus-LOW-2 per-accessor 3-field debug_assert (the primary R-V3.6-15 monotonicity assert ships at V3.6.0.8.4 lib.rs:2461-2475); Opus-LOW-3 `set_workbook_cache` API tightening (caller-supplied VV → method-read both atomically).  **R-V3.6-15 CLOSED** (monotonicity `debug_assert_eq!(new_ops.len(), current_op_count - cached_op_count)` after op enumeration).  **R-V3.6-17 CLOSED** (clone cost measured well under threshold).  Bench `crates/ql-bindings-node/benches/workbook_snapshot.rs` extended with `bench_workbook_snapshot_delta` (1 / 10 / 100 new cells × 100k initial workload) + `bench_workbook_clone` (1k / 10k / 100k cells).  **D6 perf contract achieved with 46× headroom**: 100 new cells delta median = **1.08 ms** vs full snapshot baseline 246 ms (228× faster than full; 46× under the 50 ms threshold).  1 new cell delta = 1.01 ms; 10 new cells = 1.00 ms.  Pre-closure 100 new cells = 741 ms (3× SLOWER than full snapshot); the Opus-HIGH-3 OpLog::get fix + Codex-HIGH-3 snapshot_cell fix together delivered the 230× improvement.  Tests: ql-collab **149/149** unchanged + ql-oplog **67/67** unchanged + ql-collab-ws **42/42** unchanged + IDE mocha **390/390** (2 shape-pinning tests updated to include the new `version` field; net delta 0) + engine workspace release build clean.  Rule 4 arc terminus HELD at 6 (the new `version: Buffer` field is positive Send+Sync via napi-rs's `Vec<u8>` wrapper composition; no new triggers).  **D6 ARC COMPLETE.**
