quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:643:   **V2.5 + V2.6 (cycle 5 combined)** — V8-block closure via Option A engine refactor. Engine `1b233af6150` → `81c66d02f9f`. IDE `c5997998741` → `8798349be6d`. Added `Transport::ack_handle(&self) -> Option<Box<dyn FlushAck + Send>>` default-None trait method + `WebSocketProgressAckHandle` (Codex M1 target snapshot AT call site, not at wait-start) + `CollabSession::flush_pending_handle(&self)` proxy. napi binding refactor: extract handle under session lock → drop lock → spawn_blocking wait without lock held. V2.6 added `BlockingTransport` test fixture behind `test-fixtures` Cargo feature + `BlockingTransportFixture` napi class to force deterministic contention for V2.5 contract testing. **V8-block VERIFIED CLOSED** by both audit lanes via source-walks. V2.5 contract test empirically passes: opCount() during 2000ms-blocked flushPending returns ~50ms. V2.5 audit verdicts: Codex 0H + 1M + 3L (M1 = production-cdylib DoS footgun, closed at binding via `block_ms > 0`); Opus 0H + 1M + 4L (Rule 4 #6 trigger: false `FlushAck: Send + !Sync` while impls Send + Sync; closed via positive Sync asserts).
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:645:   **V2.7 (cycle 7)** — structured `Error.code` discrimination. Engine `2a3e2ebcbfe` → `8f5b2e02ab7`. IDE `2a5619f9162` → `f9f98194958`. Closed the V2.1 Opus MEDIUM-3 carryforward (lossy `Display` projection of engine error variants; carried as V2.2 Opus MEDIUM-4 and re-flagged in V2.3 audit prep): every engine error enum got `kind() -> &'static str` accessors (TransportError, WebSocketError, CollabSessionError with Transport(inner) passthrough); napi binding got 3 helpers (`{collab_session,transport,websocket}_error_to_napi`) that prepend `[<kind>]` to Display strings; IDE got `parseQuantbookError(err) -> QuantbookErrorInfo` + `QuantbookErrorCode` union of 12 codes. V2.3 substring tests still pass (Display preserved after prefix). V2.7 audit: Codex 0H + 1L (all Q1-Q4 VERIFIED); Opus 0H + 3M + 4L (all required-walk VERIFIED). **0 Rule 4 triggers in V2.7**. Opus M2 (the big one) closed in-cycle: 14 napi-layer validation errors that silently bucketed under 'unknown' got the new `bad_argument` code prefix via `bad_argument_error(msg)` helper.
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:663:   - **V3.3.0.3 (cycle 3)** -- engine `exportSnapshot` incremental cache (engine `2bfba9b55ec`) closes V3.2.d Opus M4.  New field `last_snapshot: HashMap<(u16, u32, u32), CellWireValue>` on `CollabSession` with **Rule 4 per-field walk documented** (HashMap + tuple-of-primitives + CellWireValue all Send + Sync; inherits V2.4 Arc<Mutex<>> sync pinning; 0 new triggers).  5 op-mutation paths maintain the cache: `new` empty, `from_snapshot` rebuild, `append_op` O(1) incremental insert, `merge_bytes` full rebuild (causal-reorder safe), `discard_pending_ops` rebuild (log replaced), `poll_remote_with_limit` rebuild after drain.  napi `export_snapshot` refactored to read from cache via new `snapshot_cells()` accessor (O(cells-on-sheet) instead of O(N)).  **Regression caught + closed in-cycle**: `poll_remote_with_limit` bypassed `CollabSession::merge_bytes`; pre-fix V3.2.c.5 LWW loopback round-trip test FAILED; fixed by adding cache invalidation in the existing post-drain block.  4 new cache-invariant mocha tests (LWW / mergeBytes causal-reorder / pollRemote drain regression / fromSnapshot round-trip).  Mocha 145 -> 149.
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:675:   🚧 **V3.4 (undo + persistence + presence, 0.1-0.5 + 0.4a/b + 0.7 SHIPPED 2026-05-23)** -- 8 V3.4.0 sub-steps shipped; only 0.X audit remains.  Five locked D-decisions per V3.3.0.X Opus § V3.4 ENTRY READINESS: **D1 hybrid CellState cache** (unified `CellState{value, formula, ...}` for cell-keyed ops; non-cell ops stay on Workbook state); **D2 full-rebuild undo invalidation** (carries V3.3.0.X HIGH-1; partial-invalidate deferred to V3.5+); **D3 envelope-level persistence versioning** (V3.4.0.4a reuses existing v2 `workbook.toml.schema_version` from Phase 2A.8; no bump needed); **D4 boolean-flag race guard** (extends V3.3.0.4 `activeInput` pattern; R-V3.4-3 deferred at V3.4.0.5b implementation -- full HTML rebuild on every pollRemote merged tick handles regeneration); **D5 UUID-derived PeerId** -- **DEVIATED at V3.4.0.4b**: original lock specified persisted-per-workbook PeerId via envelope v3 / config file; implementation discovery showed two-windows-same-workspace collision; resolution is fresh-UUID-per-session via `crypto.randomUUID()` truncated to 64-bit BigInt, which is CRDT-correct + closes R-V3.3-5 fully (UUID 2^64 keyspace vs PID ~2^15 effective).  Cross-restart op-attribution continuity deferred to V3.4.1+ if user-facing feature surfaces.  Sub-steps shipped: 0.1 decision lock (engine `a87c31eed4f`); 0.2 hybrid CellState cache + 3 new ql-collab tests (engine `1ae59a1a1aa`); 0.3 undo/redo napi + Cmd-Z wiring + 13 mocha (engine `7d63ff53132` + IDE `673792af05f`); 0.4a engine .qbook napi (toQbook/fromQbook + `addSheet` REAL SEMANTIC GAP closure + 3 new napi-crate deps ql-io/ql-functions/ql-storage + persistence_error_to_napi + 5 mocha; engine `bef220d7d3c` + IDE `ec9b59db8a5`); 0.4b IDE Save As/Open + generateUuidPeerId + 4 mocha (engine `a1e2c673381` plan-only + IDE `fa7ec198cee`); 0.5a presence napi (5 wrappers + PresenceStateJson struct + 9 mocha; engine `5ce55f65739` + IDE `8ff2d81f1e4`); 0.5b IDE cell-grid presence integration (cell-grid-presence data block + .cell-peer-presence decoration + presenceUpdate envelope + R-V3.4-7 VOIDED + R-V3.4-3 DEFERRED + 16 mocha; engine `cd26a37b513` plan-only + IDE `1744cee11af`).  +47 cumulative V3.4-specific mocha tests (181 -> 228) + 3 new ql-collab tests (76 -> 79).  Rule 4 arc terminus held at 6 throughout (V3.4 surface adds one new Rust struct `PresenceStateJson` -- composition of u16/u32/bool primitives; trivially Send+Sync; 0 new triggers).  **0.6 mocha is EFFECTIVELY COMPLETE** via incremental per-sub-step coverage (47 V3.4-tests vs the plan's "~15 new" target).  **0.7 docs SHIPPED** at engine `fe10a245d07` (ide-consumer-contract.md § 4.1.z4 insertion; ~460 lines / file 837 -> 1280; covers full V3.4 napi surface + CellState cache + undo/redo + .qbook persistence + D5 DEVIATION + presence + 6 drift hazards + risk register R-V3.4-1..6 post-implementation reality + 12 out-of-scope items + steps 7-11 live smoke procedure extending V3.3.0.6).  Remaining: **0.X parallel Codex+Opus megaudit** (~4-6h cycle; sweeps V3.4.0.1-7 cumulatively).
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:710:**✅ DECISION-LOCKED 2026-05-26** (Codex-validated): authoritative locked decisions + sequence at `docs/phase6/decision-lock.md`. Lock = **wedge-first, staged**: 6.1A session-API contract → 6.1B owning `WorkbookSession` → 6.1C security audit → 6.4-0 function-metadata substrate → 6.4A MVP Python UDF + minimal `quantbook-py` authoring slice (proves the Month-6 kill gate) → 6.4B UDF hardening → 6.3 full bindings → 6.2 service (defer HTTP-vs-gRPC) → 6.5 SQL/connectors → 6.6 AI (sentinel; `=AI()` cell fn is v2-aligned) → 6.7 audit. Entry-readiness analysis: `docs/phase6/entry-plan.md`. Active plan: `.plans/_active.md`.
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:712:**✅ 6.1A + 6.1B inc.1/1b + inc.2a/2b/2c-1/2c-2 SHIPPED 2026-05-26.** Contract: `docs/api/session-api.md` v2 (API6-01/02/03; Codex gpt-5.5 xhigh REVISE → all 13 findings resolved; review `docs/api/codex-6-1a-review.md`). Contract crate: `ql-session` (`38108a5c8ef`) — complete type-level `EngineSession` trait + DTOs + EngineError + operation/lifecycle + table ops. **Owning `WorkbookSession` SHIPPED** in `crates/ql-exec/src/session.rs` `impl EngineSession` (`83b1b33bac2` PlanCache → `7335a5a1bfa` core → `993492b6f9b` validate_formula/query_range/`CellValue::Blank` → `2b5e7a13f5b` structure+table ops → `9f7a1645dbd` tombstone-read-consistency audit fix) — REAL: lifecycle + `{epoch,op_count}` 24-byte version token + single-cell mutations + add/rename/**delete/restore/move** sheet (fail-loud) + set_name + **table ops** (create/rename/rename_column/resize/drop) + recalc (Busy/op-registry, CellDiagnostic events) + read (snapshot/cell/list_sheets/query_range/validate_formula; tombstoned sheet = uniformly NotFound) + cancel/operation_status/poll_events; error mapping via free fns (orphan rules forbid `From<RuntimeError> for EngineError`). 17 session tests + 653 ql-exec lib green, clippy clean. Remaining trait methods surfaced `Capability/not_implemented_in_v1_core` (No-Fallbacks). Doc fix: ql-oplog::OpLog DOES expose a Loro VV (`oplog_vv`) — earlier "no VV" claim corrected; `{epoch,op_count}` is the deliberate v1 token. NEXT = 6.1B inc.2c-3 (snapshot_delta) → batch/txn/undo/redo/persistence → functions/bulk → Node smoke migration → 6.1C audit. **(Superseded — inc.2c-3 through inc.2c-8 all SHIPPED 2026-05-27; current NEXT = persistence; see the inc.2c-8 entry below + `docs/api/workbook-session-impl-plan.md` §0.)**
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:714:**✅ 6.1B inc.2 AUDIT (F3–F10) + inc.2c-3 snapshot_delta SHIPPED 2026-05-27.** Parallel Codex (gpt-5.5 xhigh) + Opus audit of `WorkbookSession` (synthesis `docs/audits/2026-05-27-inc2-session-audit/SYNTHESIS.md`; 10 distinct findings, all verified at source). **Audit-fix `879f3601747`**: F3 `with_runtime` FaultGuard (panic→Faulted, the in-engine half of the §8 boundary); F4 read-path coord bounds (query_range/cell/validate_formula → BadArgument, closes a u32 overflow); F5 tombstone op-log fidelity (double-delete = true no-op; restore-of-live = Conflict); F6 `require_live_sheet` on rename_sheet + create_table; F7 query_range include-options fail-loud (Capability); F8 Appendix-A honest mapping; F9 deleted-sheets-formula-readable doc; F10 corrected misleading tables.rs atomicity comment (the BatchCommit fix is TRACKED — pre-existing, near-zero reachability). **inc.2c-3 `20427b1c4c7`**: `snapshot_delta` via design (a) — a session change-log keyed by a monotonic **`state_seq`** that REPLACES `oplog.len()` as the token counter (advances on every committed mutation AND every recompute-with-changes + Blank-clear, so distinct states never share a token; closes Codex HIGH F1+F2-token-half). `RecomputeResult` gained `changed_cells`. §4.3 rules + fail-loud `invalid_version_token`; epoch-bump for delta-inexpressible states (move/restore sheet, table ops). **ql-exec lib 667/0, clippy clean, workspace `cargo check` green.** NEXT = batch/txn → undo/redo → persistence → functions/bulk → Node smoke → 6.1C audit. **(Superseded — see the inc.2c-8 entry below for current NEXT = persistence.)**
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:716:**✅ 6.1B inc.2c-4 `batch` SHIPPED 2026-05-27** (`58a55f4cfb8` + fix `9d471be3663`). `EngineSession::batch(ops, options)` via **option (a)**: validate-all up front → append ONE `Op::BatchCommit` before mutating → apply via a graph-maintaining runtime with the op-log DETACHED (new additive `WorkbookRuntime::with_session_state_no_oplog`, so workbook+calcgraph update but no second per-op append) → `record_changes` once. All four `SessionOp` variants (SetValue/SetFormula/Clear/SetFormat); validation-atomic; calcgraph stays live (proven by a batch→recalc_dirty test). **Built by a delegated Opus agent; a self-review caught + fixed a real latent replay-divergence** — same-cell value/formula ops in one batch (e.g. `[SetFormula A1, SetValue A1]`) built the log from pre-batch state but applied sequentially, and `Op::PutValue` replay does not clear a formula (`replay.rs:486-510`), so a replay would diverge; FIXED by rejecting >1 value/formula op per cell in a batch → `Conflict/conflicting_batch_ops` (`SetFormat` stays orthogonal). **ql-exec lib 681/0, clippy clean, workspace green.**
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:718:**✅ 6.1B inc.2c-5 transaction handle SHIPPED 2026-05-27.** The multi-call `EngineSession::begin_transaction`/`txn_add`/`commit_transaction`/`rollback_transaction`. Added the two `WorkbookSession` fields (`txns: HashMap<TransactionId, Vec<SessionOp>>`, `next_txn_id: u64`). The handle is a **pure `SessionOp` buffer holding no engine borrow**; `commit_transaction` drains it through the SAME `batch` machinery, inheriting validation-atomicity + graph consistency + one `Op::BatchCommit` + single `state_seq` tick + the same-cell value/formula conflict guard (`conflicting_batch_ops`). No lock between begin and commit → the buffer is validated at **commit time** (a sheet deleted after `txn_add` → `sheet_not_found` at commit). `begin`/`txn_add`/`commit` require `Ready`; `rollback` is ungated (cleanup); `close` drops all buffers. A **failed commit leaves the transaction open** (buffer restored — `batch` applied nothing). Unknown handle → fail-loud `NotFound`/`transaction_not_found`; id-space exhaustion → loud `Internal`/`transaction_id_exhausted` (`checked_add`, never wraps). 10 session tests. **Parallel Codex (gpt-5.5 xhigh) + Opus audit CLEAN** — no HIGH; both reviewers converged on 1 MED (gate `txn_add` on `ensure_ready` — APPLIED) + 2 LOW (`next_txn_id` `checked_add`, op-log-len test assertions — APPLIED). Synthesis `docs/audits/2026-05-27-inc2c5-txn-audit/SYNTHESIS.md`. **ql-exec lib 691/0, clippy clean, workspace green.** (superseded NEXT — see inc.2c-6/2c-7 below.)
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:722:**✅ 6.1B inc.2c-7 — undo/redo SHIPPED 2026-05-27** (`4f8e9858d77`). `undo`/`redo`/`can_undo`/`can_redo` via a long-lived `loro::UndoManager` field (built in `from_workbook`, `set_merge_interval(0)` → 1 Loro commit = 1 undo unit; every command emits exactly one commit except `rename_table`/`rename_column` which are wrapped in a `grouped()` Loro undo group — the F10 PutFormula loop). `rematerialize` after a Loro undo/redo: replay the (compacted) op-log onto a CLONE of the construction-time **baseline workbook** → `rebuild_from_workbook` → `recompute_all` with the op-log DETACHED → `bump_epoch` (outstanding `snapshot_delta` token → EpochMismatch full rebuild). Empty stack → `consumed:false`. Builds on inc.2c-6: undo of a Blank-clear restores the prior value. **Parallel Codex+Opus audit:** both verified the two load-bearing claims at source (1-command-1-undo-unit; linear-replay rename fidelity needs no ql-collab repair passes); both flagged ONE real bug — a populated-`from_workbook` session + undo silently dropped pre-loaded content (replayed from an empty workbook) — **FIXED via the `baseline: Workbook` field** (Codex HIGH / Opus M1). F10 table-rename append-atomicity was left tracked at this point, then CLOSED in its own increment inc.2c-8 (`dca5695549e`) — NOT folded into persistence; 100-step undo cap documented. Synthesis `docs/audits/2026-05-27-inc2c67-undo-audit/SYNTHESIS.md`. **ql-exec lib 709/0, clippy clean, workspace build green.** (superseded NEXT — see inc.2c-8 below.)
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:724:**✅ 6.1B inc.2c-8 — F10 atomic table-rename SHIPPED 2026-05-27** (`dca5695549e`). `rename_table`/`rename_column` previously appended `Op::RenameTable`/`RenameColumn` + one `Op::PutFormula` per rewritten formula cell as SEPARATE `oplog.append` calls interleaved with the `put_formula` mutations → a mid-loop append failure left a partial log + partially-rewritten workbook (the tracked F10 non-atomicity / Codex HIGH from the inc.2 audit; near-zero reachability — PutFormula serializes a String, only a Loro-internal/OOM failure triggers it). Fix: collect the rename op + all PutFormula rewrites into ONE `Op::BatchCommit` appended BEFORE any mutation, then apply — mirroring `rename_sheet`. Replay applies the inner ops in order ([Rename*, PutFormula*]); `apply_rename_table`/`apply_rename_column` only re-key metadata and rely on the explicit PutFormula ops for text → complementary, replay reproduces the identical end state. The undo `grouped()` wrapper is now defense-in-depth (single-commit by construction). **Focused Codex (gpt-5.5 xhigh) audit: no HIGH/MED** — atomicity + replay fidelity + op-equivalence verified at source; 2 LOW (stale docs, rename_table e2e coverage) APPLIED. `rename_table_emits_ops`/`rename_column_emits_ops` updated to assert the single-BatchCommit shape + new e2e `rename_table_op_log_replay_reconstructs_rename`. **ql-exec lib 709/0 + e2e 21/0, ql-oplog 70/0, clippy clean, workspace build green.** **NEXT = 6.1B persistence** (open/import/save/export via ql_io → adds PersistenceError to Appendix A). **DESIGN FORK to lock first: `open` adopts loaded state — Option 1 (baseline = loaded workbook + FRESH op-log; simple, always-correct, loses op-log history on resave) vs Option 2 (baseline = empty + adopt loaded op-log; preserves history but needs `loaded_wb == replay(loaded_oplog)`).** The inc.2c-7 baseline field is wired for Option 1. Then functions/bulk → Node smoke (+ `.node` rebuild + B#1/S2-01 mocha) → 6.1C audit. **(Superseded — inc.2c-9 below SHIPPED `.qbook` open/save with Option 1; current NEXT = import/export → functions/bulk.)**
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:726:**✅ 6.1B inc.2c-9 — `.qbook` `open`/`save` SHIPPED 2026-05-27.** Persistence round-trip on `WorkbookSession`. **DESIGN FORK LOCKED — Option 1** (user-confirmed): `open` reconstructs the workbook from the `.qbook` envelope via `ql_io::load_workbook_with_oplog` and adopts it with `*self = from_workbook(loaded_wb)` — a FRESH empty op-log + fresh `UndoManager` + `baseline = loaded_wb` + re-minted epoch (so any pre-open `snapshot_delta` token → EpochMismatch full rebuild) + reset state_seq/change_log/ops/events/txns, registry preserved — then recomputes with the op-log DETACHED (`with_runtime_no_oplog`; saved computed values may be stale, mirroring `loader.rs::load_workbook_and_recompute`), folding failures into `CellDiagnostic` events. The loaded op-log is **fully validated** (the snapshot framing by `load_workbook_with_oplog` PLUS its per-op payloads by an explicit `iter()` loop — Codex HIGH: framing-only validation would silently accept a payload-corrupt sidecar then mask it on the next save) then **discarded** (Option 1 trade-off: history not carried; re-save writes only this session's edits). `save(&self)` writes `&self.workbook` + `&self.oplog` via `ql_io::save_workbook_with_oplog`; the workbook name is derived from the path file-stem (no document-name metadata in v1; `None` → loud `BadArgument`). New `map_persistence_err` fills Appendix A (`Persistence`/`qbook_error`|`session_oplog`|`qbook_unsupported_version`|`qbook_truncated_header`; foreign `#[non_exhaustive]` wildcard → loud `Internal`/`unmapped_persistence_error`). `open` legal in `New`/`Ready` (re-open replaces the document) via a new `ensure_openable` gate; `save` uses `ensure_readable`. Option 2 (adopt the loaded op-log) rejected — needs `loaded_wb == replay(loaded_oplog)`, re-opening the data-loss bug class inc.2c-7 closed; revisit for collab-v1.5. `import`/`export` (xlsx/csv) stay honest `Capability/not_implemented_in_v1_core` — a follow-up sub-increment. **Parallel Codex(gpt-5.5 xhigh)+Opus audit:** 1 HIGH (sidecar payload-validation gap — FIXED + regression test) + 2 LOW docs/test-coverage (module-doc drift fixed; `can_undo`-false-after-open + save→open→re-save→open stability tests added) + INFO (Appendix-A variant-name spelling tidied); both verified the post-open undo invariant + open-failure atomicity + recompute op-log isolation at source. Synthesis `docs/audits/2026-05-27-inc2c9-persist-audit/`. **ql-exec lib 719/0 + e2e 21/0, clippy clean, workspace build green.** **(Superseded — inc.2c-10 below SHIPPED xlsx import; current NEXT = csv import + xlsx/csv export → functions.)**
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:728:**✅ 6.1B inc.2c-10 — xlsx `import` + `ql-io-xlsx` dependency inversion SHIPPED 2026-05-27.** `WorkbookSession::import("xlsx")` is live. **Root blocker:** `import` lives in `ql-exec`; the xlsx importer lives in `ql-io-xlsx`, which depended on `ql-exec` (only for formula recompute) — so `ql-exec → ql-io-xlsx` would be a cycle (`ql-io-xlsx` was a leaf crate, never wired into a consumer). **Fix — dependency inversion (chose A2 over A1-parse-only to preserve `ql-io-xlsx`'s tested recompute/Strict/`formula_failures` behavior):** new `pub trait XlsxRecomputer` in `ql-io-xlsx`; `import_xlsx_bytes`/`import_xlsx_path` gained a `recomputer: Option<&dyn XlsxRecomputer>` param (BestEffort/Strict require it → loud `XlsxError::Engine` if `None`; Skip ignores it); `recompute_loaded_workbook` deleted; `ql-exec` moved to `ql-io-xlsx`'s `[dev-dependencies]` (dev-dep cycles are allowed). `ql-exec` gained `ql-io-xlsx` as a normal dep + public `EngineXlsxRecomputer` (`src/xlsx_recompute.rs`, the moved recompute logic over `WorkbookRuntime::recompute_all`). `import("xlsx")` = parse via `import_xlsx_bytes(.., Some(&EngineXlsxRecomputer))` (recomputes during import) → **Option-1 adoption** (`*self = from_workbook`, registry preserved, epoch re-minted; NO second recompute) → `push_xlsx_import_diagnostics`. `"csv"` → honest `not_implemented` (net-new — no csv importer); unknown format → loud `BadArgument`. `map_xlsx_err` fills Appendix A (Io/Zip/Calamine/XmlParse/MalformedOoxml/UnsupportedFeature → Persistence; Export/Engine → Internal; foreign `#[non_exhaustive]` wildcard → loud `unmapped_xlsx_error`). **~90 `ql-io-xlsx` test call-sites migrated** (delegated to a fresh Opus agent, reviewed at source; 3 `src` lib-test sites use `None` — verified behavior-preserving since they fail before recompute or use Skip — because the dev-dep cycle puts two `ql_io_xlsx` crate instances in the lib-test graph, an E0277 the integration tests don't hit). **Parallel Codex(gpt-5.5 xhigh)+Opus audit, every finding verified at source:** 1 HIGH (both reviewers — `push_xlsx_import_diagnostics` dropped `report.feature_inventory.counts`, the PRIMARY dropped-feature channel: CF/DV/merged-cells/comments/drawings/protection/hidden-sheets → silent fidelity loss; FIXED + regression test) + 1 MEDIUM (Codex — recompute outside the `FaultGuard`; assessed NON-BUG: `import` replaces `self` atomically after a local-workbook recompute, so no torn state — documented, a guard would wrongly fault a healthy session) + INFO (docs). Both confirmed: no cycle, Option-1 atomicity, `map_xlsx_err` exhaustive, the 3 `None` sites sound. **Tracked follow-up:** `ql-exec` now transitively pulls the xlsx WRITER's heavy deps (umya-spreadsheet + image/rav1e/exr/tiff) — feature-gate the writer behind a `write` feature + depend `default-features = false` to keep the core engine + WASM/bindings lean (`ql-exec/Cargo.toml` tracks it). Spec: `docs/api/xlsx-import-integration-plan.md`; synthesis `docs/audits/2026-05-27-inc2c10-xlsx-import-audit/`. **ql-exec lib 723/0 + e2e 21/0, clippy clean; ql-io-xlsx green (lib 60 + calamine_smoke 49); workspace build green.** **(Superseded — inc.2c-11 below SHIPPED csv import/export; current NEXT = `export("xlsx")` + xlsx-writer feature-gate.)**
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:730:**✅ 6.1B inc.2c-11 — csv `import`/`export` SHIPPED 2026-05-27.** `WorkbookSession::import("csv")` + `export("csv")` are live. **New pure-I/O leaf crate `ql-io-csv`** (deps: `csv = "=1.3.1"` + `ql-storage` + `ql-types` + `thiserror` — deliberately NOT `ql-exec`; CSV has no formulas → no recompute injection, unlike the inc.2c-10 xlsx path, so it stays a true leaf with no cycle risk). Public surface: `import_csv_bytes(bytes, CsvImportOptions) -> Result<CsvImportResult{workbook, report}, CsvError>` + `export_csv_bytes(workbook, sheet_id, CsvExportOptions) -> Result<Vec<u8>, CsvError>` + `CsvError` (`#[non_exhaustive]`: Io/Parse/ExceedsSheetLimits/SheetNotFound). RFC 4180 via BurntSushi's `csv` crate (quoting/embedded-newlines) rather than a hand-rolled splitter. **Import:** `has_headers(false)` (row 0 is data), leading UTF-8 BOM stripped, UTF-8-strict (non-UTF-8 → loud `csv_parse`), type inference (empty→Blank skipped; `TRUE`/`FALSE`→Boolean; finite f64→Number, `inf`/`nan`→text; leading `=`→**text**, injection-safe; Excel-like lossy numeric coercion `00123`→123 documented), engine-row/col-limit guarded BEFORE `put_at` (never panics) → **Option-1 adoption** (`*self = from_workbook`, registry preserved, epoch re-minted; **NO recompute** — no formulas). **Export (`&self`):** single LIVE sheet only (`sheet_display_order` minus `is_sheet_removed`; 0→empty bytes, 1→serialise, >1→loud `BadArgument` — refuse rather than silently drop sheets, since `&self` has no warn channel); verbatim/value-only (cells via `ql_types::Value` `Display`; no formula-trigger escaping; uses the conservative `Sheet::bounds` used-range like the xlsx exporter + `.qbook` saver). `unknown` import/export format → loud `BadArgument`. New `map_csv_err` fills Appendix A (Io/Parse→Persistence `csv_io`/`csv_parse`; ExceedsSheetLimits→BadArgument `csv_exceeds_limits`; SheetNotFound→Internal `csv_sheet_not_found`; foreign `#[non_exhaustive]` wildcard → loud `unmapped_csv_error`). **Parallel Codex(gpt-5.5 xhigh)+Opus audit, every finding verified at source:** Codex **HIGH** (export over conservative `Sheet::bounds`, which `Sheet::put` grows even on a `Blank` write → a blank-inflated workbook could emit a giant rectangle) **assessed consistent-with-siblings + documented + tracked**: the IDENTICAL `for row in 0..bounds.row_extent` pattern is in the xlsx exporter (`umya_export.rs:424`) AND the `.qbook` saver (`qbook_format.rs:1422`), both shipped through prior audits — a CSV-only divergent fix would be worse engineering; the correct fix is a uniform storage-level effective-non-blank-value-extent API adopted by all three serializers (TRACKED cross-cutting follow-up; the common round-trip path is unaffected — import skips blanks). Codex MEDIUM (export doesn't escape formula-triggers) → kept **faithful/verbatim** export (silent `'`-prefixing would corrupt data + break round-trip + violate No-Fallbacks; matches Excel/Sheets export), doc claim scoped to import + future opt-in sanitiser noted. Opus INFO (leading UTF-8 BOM not stripped → corrupts cell (0,0)) **FIXED** + test. Codex LOW (numeric lexical fidelity) kept Excel-consistent + pinned with a test. Both confirmed: limit guards correct/no-panic, import adoption atomic-on-failure, no-recompute safe, multi-sheet refusal correct, `ql-io-csv` a genuine leaf, `map_csv_err` exhaustive. Synthesis `docs/audits/2026-05-27-inc2c11-csv-audit/`. **ql-exec lib 728/0 + e2e 21/0, clippy clean; ql-io-csv 11/0; ql-io-xlsx green; workspace build green.** **(Superseded — inc.2c-12 below SHIPPED `export("xlsx")` + the xlsx-writer feature-gate; current NEXT = functions 6.4-0/6.4.)**
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:732:**✅ 6.1B inc.2c-12 — xlsx `export` + xlsx-writer feature-gate SHIPPED 2026-05-27.** `WorkbookSession::export("xlsx")` is live (whole-workbook — xlsx is multi-sheet, unlike the single-sheet csv export), AND the tracked inc.2c-10 follow-up (ql-exec pulling the xlsx WRITER's heavy umya-spreadsheet + image/rav1e/exr/tiff codec tree for import-only use) is CLOSED. **In-memory writer (no tempfile):** umya 2.2.0 exposes `writer::xlsx::write_writer<W: io::Write>`, so a new `ql_io_xlsx::export_xlsx_bytes(workbook, registry, XlsxExportOptions) -> Result<(Vec<u8>, XlsxExportReport), XlsxError>` serialises straight into a `Vec<u8>`; the path exporter (`export_xlsx_path`/`export_new_workbook`) now delegates to a shared `export_new_workbook_to_bytes` core + one `atomic_write_to_path`, and `post_process_zip(path,…)` became the bytes-in/bytes-out `post_process_bytes(Vec<u8>,…)` — output is byte-identical (umya's path `write` and `write_writer` both go through `make_buffer`, verified at the registry source). `export_xlsx_bytes` is `NewWorkbook`-only (UpdateOriginal → loud `XlsxError::Export`, no silent downgrade); Strict drop-feature check kept (no file to remove). **Feature-gate:** ql-io-xlsx `umya-spreadsheet` is now `optional`; `[features] default = ["write"]`, `write = ["dep:umya-spreadsheet"]` gates `mod write` + `export_xlsx_path` + `export_xlsx_bytes`; the READER (calamine/zip/quick-xml + `import_xlsx_*` + `XlsxRecomputer`) is always compiled. `ql-exec` depends `default-features = false` (reader only) + `[features] xlsx-write = ["ql-io-xlsx/write"]`; `export("xlsx")` is real behind `#[cfg(feature = "xlsx-write")]`, else honest `Capability/not_implemented_in_v1_core` (No-Fallbacks — the writer's codec tree is opt-in, keeping the default ql-exec build + WASM/bindings lean). A `ql-exec` `[dev-dependencies]` re-enables `write` so the inc.2c-10 import round-trip test fixture (which calls `export_xlsx_path`) still compiles; workspace `resolver = "2"` keeps that dev-dep `write` out of the normal lib build. `export` is `&self` (no event channel), so the export report's fidelity caveats are dropped under the default Permissive policy — the same `&self` no-warning-channel limitation as csv export (documented). `export("xlsx")` errors route through the existing `map_xlsx_err` (Appendix A unchanged). **Parallel Codex(gpt-5.5 xhigh)+Opus audit: CLEAN — 0 HIGH/MED/LOW** (both verified the `write_writer ≡ write` byte-equivalence at the umya registry source + the feature graph via read-only `cargo tree`: umya absent from default ql-exec normal deps, present under `--features xlsx-write`; 1 doc-precision INFO applied; 1 pre-existing HashMap-ordered fresh-rels INFO folded into the cross-cutting tracker). Synthesis `docs/audits/2026-05-27-inc2c12-xlsx-export-audit/`. **ql-exec lib 729/0 (default + `--features xlsx-write`), clippy clean; ql-io-xlsx 60+49/0 (default), `--no-default-features` builds clean; workspace build green.** **NEXT = functions (6.4-0 metadata substrate then 6.4) + reserved bulk → Node smoke migration (+ `.node` rebuild + B#1/S2-01 mocha) → 6.1C security audit → 6.4 Python UDFs. Plus tracked cross-cutting: a storage-level effective-non-blank-value extent API for all serializers (csv/xlsx/.qbook).** **(Superseded — inc.2d below SHIPPED the engine-side Node-smoke enabler; the prior "functions-first" NEXT was reconciled to the canonical decision-lock §2: IDE-side Node smoke + mocha → 6.1C → 6.4-0 → 6.4.)**
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:734:**✅ 6.1B inc.2d — owning `WorkbookSession` over napi (engine-side Node-smoke enabler) SHIPPED 2026-05-28.** The Node binding `ql-bindings-node` now exposes the product-neutral owning session over FFI as a new **`Session`** `#[napi]` class wrapping `Arc<parking_lot::Mutex<ql_exec::WorkbookSession>>` — `new`/`addSheet`/`setValue`/`setFormula`/`clear`/`recalcDirty`/`recalcAll`/`snapshot`/`cell`/`listSheets`. This is decision-lock §2 item 3 ("migrate the Node smoke path onto the owning session") + risk-mitigation #1 ("migrate the Node path early to catch missing commands"). It does NOT touch the existing `CollabSession` CRDT façade (collab = v1.5). New `engine_error_to_napi` (mirrors `collab_session_error_to_napi`; `EngineError::Display = "[code] message"`) + free-fn DTO mappers reusing the existing `#[napi(object)]` shapes (`CellValueJson`/`CellSnapshotJson`/`SheetSnapshotJson`/`WorkbookSnapshotJson`/`FormatIdJson`/`FormatDefJson`) + a new `SheetInfoJson`; all index args are `f64`+`validate_u16/u32_index` (no JS `ToUint32` silent coercion); a positive `const _ASSERT_BINDING_SESSION_SEND` compile-proof confirms `WorkbookSession: Send` (so `Arc<Mutex<…>>` is `Send+Sync` — the owning session IS FFI-shareable, no contract finding). Deps added: `ql-exec` (NO default features → does NOT pull the umya xlsx-writer/image-codec tree) + `ql-session`. A plain-Node `process.dlopen` smoke (`crates/ql-bindings-node/tests/smoke_session.mjs`) PASSES edit→recalc→snapshot (B1==11), clear-preserves-value, setValue(blank)-clears, unknown-kind→`[bad_argument]`. **Parallel Codex(gpt-5.5 xhigh)+Opus audit: SHIP — 0 HIGH/MED**; 1 LOW (clear docstring overstated "value+formula" → FIXED to convert-to-literal) + deferred items (snapshot `formats` ordering non-deterministic at the `WorkbookSession::snapshot` source → 6.1C; `WorkbookSnapshotJson` omits `schema_version` → 6.3; no `catch_unwind` under `panic=abort`, identical to CollabSession → known). Synthesis `docs/audits/2026-05-28-inc2d-session-napi-audit/`. **Build green: `cargo build -p ql-bindings-node` (default; `--features test-fixtures` checks), `cargo check --workspace`; inc.2d code clippy-clean.** **⚠️ Pre-existing clippy debt surfaced (NOT this increment): `cargo clippy -p ql-bindings-node` is RED at HEAD (it has `#![deny(clippy::all)]`) due to the `rust-1.95.0` clippy bump — 4 deny-errors in pre-existing CollabSession-path code (`lib.rs:416/502/564/2788`) + workspace-wide warn-level `doc_lazy_continuation`/`type_complexity` (ql-storage/ql-oplog/ql-collab); needs a focused hygiene pass.** **NEXT (canonical decision-lock §2): IDE-side Node smoke wiring + mocha (drive `Session` through `loader.ts`, rebuild the `.node`, add B#1/S2-01 cross-window tests) — cross-repo (`feat/visualise-v1`) → 6.1C security/design audit → 6.4-0 function-metadata substrate → 6.4 Python UDFs. Plus the tracked serializer effective-extent API.** **(Superseded — the IDE Node migration below SHIPPED; current NEXT = 6.1C.)**
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:736:**✅ 6.1B IDE-side Node `Session` migration SHIPPED 2026-05-28 (cross-repo).** The VS Code fork (IDE repo, branch `feat/visualise-v1`, commit `c24222315ed`) now consumes the engine's owning `Session` napi class through its real Node load path — closing decision-lock §2 item 3 + risk-mit #1 (migrate the Node path early to catch missing commands). Engine code unchanged (still inc.2d `ea5987e4253`); the cdylib was REBUILT (`cargo build -p ql-bindings-node --release --features test-fixtures`), which also makes the previously SOURCE-ONLY `CollabSession` fixes **B#1** (`ff09a5e17a7`, `exportSnapshot` hides tombstoned-sheet cells) + **S2-01** (`7e536fc07b2`, `workbookSnapshotDelta` no prior-window tombstone leak) LIVE. IDE diff (5 files): `extensions/quantlab/src/quantbook/types.ts` (`SessionInstance`/`SessionConstructor` + `SheetInfoJson` + `SessionCellValueInput` incl `'blank'`; `Session` on `QuantbookNativeModule`), `…/loader.ts` (a `Session` constructor + 9-method prototype fail-at-boundary shape-check in `loadQuantbookEngine()`), `…/session.ts` (`createWorkbookSession()`), `test/quantbook-session.test.ts` (NEW — owning-Session smoke through the real loader + B#1 + S2-01 regressions), `test/quantbook-roundtrip.test.ts` (the V2.8 fixture-optionality fake module gains a `Session` stub). **Scope: types + loader + mocha proof, NO live-UI change** — the shipped collab `CellGridPanel` render path needs `workbookSnapshotDelta`/presence/transport, none of which `Session` exposes over napi yet (a later increment / 6.3). **Parallel Codex+Opus audit:** Opus SHIP; Codex 1 MED — the *cross-window* S2-01 test was vacuous as a filter regression (`mergeBytes` force-invalidates the delta cache → `workbookSnapshotDelta` returns `fullRebuildRequired=true`, never reaching the `changedCells` filter; a true two-peer fast-path delta is impossible), so it was **reframed honestly** (now deterministically asserts the full-rebuild fallback + end-to-end no-leak) while the **LOCAL** S2-01 test remains the genuine, non-vacuous filter regression (both lanes verified it hits the fix) — plus 1 pre-existing LOW (`WorkbookSnapshotJson.version` optional-in-TS vs always-present → 6.1C DTO fidelity) + 1 INFO (CI must build the cdylib or the skip-on-missing makes the proof vacuous). **Full IDE extension suite 1435 passing / 0 failing / 25 pending** (+11 new). Synthesis `docs/audits/2026-05-28-6-1b-ide-node-migration/`. **NEXT = 6.1C security/design audit** (best as a fresh dedicated multi-lane Codex+Opus megaudit; consumes the inc.2d-deferred findings: snapshot `formats` ordering, `schema_version` omission, no `catch_unwind` under `panic=abort`, the `version`-optionality DTO drift) → 6.4-0 function-metadata substrate → 6.4 Python UDFs.
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:738:**✅ 6.1C — Security/Design Audit SHIPPED 2026-05-28 (5-way parallel megaudit).** The mandatory audit before broader binding/service exposure (decision-lock §2 item 4) is complete — the Phase-6 exit-packet artifact lands at `docs/audits/2026-05-28-6-1c-megaudit/SYNTHESIS.md`. **Method:** 4 Codex (gpt-5.5 xhigh, `read-only`) lanes + 1 Opus agent + Opus synthesis (this 5-way pattern previously caught 22 HIGHs invisible per-batch at Phase 4.11+4.12 closure). Scope ≈9859 LoC: owning `WorkbookSession` (`session.rs` 5117) + `Session` napi class (`lib.rs:4276-4426` ~150) + the `ql-session` contract (~316) + the IDE TS consumer + shared `#[napi(object)]` DTOs. Lane briefs + orchestration committed at `c9297dff8ab` under `docs/phase6/6-1c-prep/`. **Verdict: SHIP-WITH-FIXES** — 3 HIGH (one fixed in audit-fix, two filed for 6.3 entry), 8 MED (two fixed in audit-fix, six filed for 6.3), 8 LOW + 6 INFO. **Foundation structurally sound:** Send/Sync compile-proven (audit rule 4); index validation exhaustive; error mapping consistent; lock discipline correct; lifecycle gates correct; `.qbook` open per-op `iter()` validation intact; F2/F10/undo all verified. **Audit-fix `6a14bd9075a`:** (1) **H2 deterministic ordering** — `snapshot.formats` + 5 `snapshot_delta` Vecs (`changed_cells`/`removed_cells`/`sheets_changed`/`sheets_removed`/`formats_added`) sorted by natural key, with `Ord`/`PartialOrd` added to `ql_session::FormatId` (additive trait, matches `ql_storage::FormatId`'s variant/field order so the wire-observable ordering is identical regardless of which side sorts); (2) **M8 `Session.close()`** bound over napi (5-line wrapper + a positive `[invalid_state]` smoke); (3) **M3 FaultGuard defense-in-depth** — lifted `FaultGuard` to module scope (eliminated the two inline duplicates in `with_runtime`/`with_runtime_no_oplog`) and wrapped `delete_sheet`/`restore_sheet`/`move_sheet`/`mark_volatiles_dirty` + `batch`'s Phase-2 op-log append so a panic mid-append/mutate seals →Faulted instead of leaving `state=Ready` with a torn op-log; (4) **L1 / seed input #5 closed** — `EngineSession::clear` trait doc tightened to "convert-to-literal; for delete-contents call `set_value(.., Blank)`" (verified at `cells.rs::set_value` Blank arm: emits `ClearValue + ClearFormula` atomically when a formula was present; the gap was docs-only, NO need for a separate `delete_cell` command); (5) **A-INFO/L-E6** — corrected the misleading `session.rs:332` docstring (Cargo default is `unwind`, NOT `abort`; the operational panic→host-abort is via napi-derive's no-`catch_unwind`-by-default behavior, which `#[napi(catch_unwind)]` would fix — tracked 6.3 M1); (6) **M6 partial** — `next_op_id` uses `checked_add` matching `next_txn_id`. **Tracked for 6.3-entry (block-on-6.3):** H1 (cross-repo IDE `parseQuantbookError` allowlist covers ~15 codes, engine `Session` emits ~40 — IDE-side commit on `feat/visualise-v1`), H3 (`snapshot_delta` under-reports spill changes — touches `WorkbookRuntime` return signature, too invasive for the audit-fix cycle; binding `snapshot_delta` over napi must wait for the engine fix). **Filed for 6.3:** M1 (`#[napi(catch_unwind)]` boundary), M2 (recalc cancel honesty — `run_recalc` allocates the op-id internally and never checks the registry, so even "pre-start cancel" is non-functional in v1), M5 (`schema_version` dropped at napi DTO boundary), M6 (events/ops bounded retention; needs event-ring infrastructure per contract §9), M7 (storage-level effective-non-blank-value extent cross-cutting). **Over-napi cut-line decision:** at 6.1C `Session` binds 11 methods (the existing 10 + `close`). `snapshotDelta`/`undo`/`redo`/`import`/`export`/`open`/`save`/`validateFormula`/`pollEvents`/`lifecycleState`/`operationStatus`/`cancel` all DEFER to 6.3; table/transaction/batch defer to 6.3; `register_function`/`unregister_function`/`list_functions` defer to 6.4 (function-metadata substrate prerequisite). Cycle-budget discipline (≤2 plan-implement-audit cycles per session) — megaudit cycle 1, audit-fix cycle 2, doc-sync separate. **Verification (focused re-verify of affected lanes):** `cargo build -p ql-exec -p ql-session -p ql-bindings-node` clean; `cargo test -p ql-exec --lib` 732/0 default + `--features xlsx-write` (+3 new H2 tests vs the 729 baseline); `cargo clippy -p ql-exec -p ql-session -p ql-bindings-node --all-targets` clean for edits; `node crates/ql-bindings-node/tests/smoke_session.mjs` PASS including the new post-close `[invalid_state]` + idempotent re-close assertions. **NEXT (canonical decision-lock §2 item 5): 6.4-0 function-metadata substrate** (replace the hardcoded `is_volatile_function` + `is_address_only_reference_fn` whitelists at `calcgraph_session.rs:149-164/:201-203` with first-class per-function metadata + `functions_used` reverse index → unblocks UDFs not bypassing the graph). Then 6.4 Python UDFs.
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:740:**✅ 6.4-2 — Engine trait wiring + napi DTO surface SHIPPED 2026-05-28 (parallel 2-way audit).** Decision-lock §2 item 6 (continued). Wires the three previously-stubbed `EngineSession` trait methods to real implementations over the substrate (`register_function` / `unregister_function` / `list_functions`) and surfaces them over napi to the IDE. **CODE commits:** `3bf0d4fcbef` (cycle-2 audit-fix) ← `f8eeaaeadfe` (cycle-1 code; +1477/-27 across 5 files in 4 crates) + IDE `739b625b4fd` on `feat/visualise-v1` (allowlist +2 codes). **Cycle 1 in 4 components:** (A) **registry substrate** — new `udf_handles: HashMap<String, FunctionImplHandle>` field on `FunctionRegistry` parallel to `metadata` (UDF-only; built-ins dispatch through `fns`) + `register_udf(meta, handle)` combined method (atomic: `register_metadata` first, handle insert on success, single `fn_gen` bump) + `udf_handle(name)` reader + `unregister_metadata` extended to symmetrically clear `udf_handles[name]` on success; (B) **engine trait wiring** (`session.rs`) — register/unregister wrapped in `FaultGuard` (6.1C M3 pattern) with explicit disarm-on-Err (legitimate Conflict/NotFound MUST NOT seal Faulted); `ensure_ready` for mutators, `ensure_readable` for the read; `Arc::make_mut(&mut self.registry)` (strong-count 1 in the normal flow — no stored clone, calcgraph borrows `&FunctionRegistry`); `map_function_registry_err` `#[allow(dead_code)]` removed; (C) **napi DTO surface** (`lib.rs`) — `FunctionMetadataJson` `#[napi(object)]` + nested `ArityJson` tagged-union + 6 enum-string mapper pairs (unknown JS string → `[bad_argument]`, No-Fallbacks) + 3 `#[napi]` methods with BigInt sign+losslessness validation for `implHandle`; (D) **cross-repo IDE** — `function_exists` / `function_not_found` added to both `KNOWN_QUANTBOOK_ERROR_CODE_RECORD` + the `QuantbookErrorCode` union (V2.9 compile-time Record invariant intact). **Parallel Codex (gpt-5.5 xhigh) + fresh-context Opus reviewer audit; reconciled verdict SHIP-WITH-FIXES after 2 HIGHs.** The 2-way INVERTED the usual pattern this cycle: **H1** (bad-name FFI panic) found by BOTH lanes — Opus added the decisive detail that the panic fires while the `FaultGuard` is armed → permanently seals the session, and empirically confirmed it via a `catch_unwind` probe; **F2** (open/import rebuild the graph against a fresh UDF-free registry) found by **CODEX ONLY** (Opus graded the `Arc::make_mut` question clean and didn't examine the `from_workbook` adoption path). Neither lane alone caught both. **Audit-fix `3bf0d4fcbef`:** (H1) `register_function` now VALIDATES the canonical name (non-empty + ASCII-upper-case) BEFORE touching the registry / arming the FaultGuard, returning `[bad_argument]` instead of letting `register_metadata`'s `assert!`s (`registry.rs:357,:361`) panic across the catch_unwind-free napi boundary; docstring corrected. (F2) new `from_workbook_with_registry(workbook, Arc<FunctionRegistry>)` builds the graph against the caller-provided registry; `from_workbook` delegates with a fresh default; all 3 adoption sites (`open`, xlsx `import`, csv `import`) adopt via it (live divergence was xlsx-import, which doesn't recompute post-swap; `open` self-healed via its post-swap `recompute_all`). (F3) `ArityJson` made a strict tagged union (reject extraneous fields + `max<min`). (M1/L1) `register_function_dirties_dependent_formulas` strengthened — was a false-positive (`#NAME?` before AND after); now asserts `fn_generation()` bumped once through the trait + `dirty_formulas()` grew. (M2) aggregate test pins `Compute/formula_bind` + `NamedRangeInScalarContext`. (M3) duplicate test asserts `udf_handle` directly. (F4) `ArityJson` doc: optional fields OMITTED/undefined, never `null`. **Verified CLEAN by the Opus lane** (re-confirmed): Arc::make_mut soundness, register_udf atomicity, FaultGuard happy/Conflict path, lifecycle gates, symmetric handle clearing, enum-mapper exhaustiveness, IDE cross-repo allowlist (no IDE change needed at audit-fix). Synthesis + lanes `docs/audits/2026-05-28-6-4-2-trait-wiring-audit/`. **Cycle budget honored:** Cycle 1 (prev session) = code; cycle 2 (this session) = audit + audit-fix; doc-sync separate. **Verification (all green):** `cargo check --workspace` clean; `cargo test -p ql-exec --lib` **755/0** default + `--features xlsx-write` (753 + 2 new); `cargo test -p ql-exec --tests` all 18 integration suites green; `cargo test -p ql-functions --lib` **1824/0** (unchanged); clippy clean for edits; `node smoke_session.mjs` PASS through fresh-built cdylib. **Still filed (non-blocking):** L2-OPUS `DepShape::LazyShape` `#[serde(alias)]` (6.4-3); I2-OPUS Phase-1.5 overlap `debug_assert` (6.4-3); L3-OPUS walker hot-path 2x HashMap-lookup (6.4 perf backlog). **NEXT: 6.4-3 — Python worker + Arrow exchange + debugpy** (the substantial sub-increment; 3-way audit), then 6.4-4 exit tests + closure megaudit (5-way).
