    41	
    42	## 1. Design principles
    43	
    44	1. **One contract, many transports.** The session is a Rust trait (`EngineSession`) + versioned DTOs.
    45	   Bindings (Node/WASM/C/Python) and the service (HTTP/gRPC) are thin adapters marshalling the same
    46	   DTOs and mapping the same `EngineError`. No binding invents its own command/error/event semantics.
    47	2. **Transport-neutral** (decision-lock §1 D2): no napi-only/HTTP-only/gRPC-only assumption. IDs,
    48	   version tokens, cancellation handles, error envelopes are plain owned data. The HTTP-vs-gRPC pick
    49	   is deferred to 6.2.
    50	3. **Opaque handles, owned results.** FFI holds an opaque session handle. **No borrowed Rust ref
    51	   crosses FFI** (this is why §3.4 uses an opaque transaction *handle*, not an RAII scope). Results are
    52	   owned snapshots/buffers/Arrow handles with explicit release; version tokens + operation IDs are
    53	   opaque blobs the caller round-trips without interpreting.
    54	4. **Bottom-up, then trimmed** — extracted from the IDE-exercised napi workflows, generalized, and
    55	   extended with the cancellation/diagnostics/function-metadata machinery v1 product surfaces need.
    56	5. **Errors are visible, never swallowed** (project No-Fallbacks rule): every fallible command returns
    57	   `Result<_, EngineError>`. The **only** structured "recovery" signal is `full_rebuild_required`, and
    58	   it is locked to an enumerated set of legitimate delta-cache states (§4.3) — a *malformed* token is a
    59	   **fail-loud `Protocol` error**, never a silent resync (MED-2).
    60	6. **Shape the future now** (decision-lock §5): event/diagnostic/provenance/operation-state DTOs +
    61	   the bulk publish/bind/materialize command *shapes* (§3.5) are versioned and reserved in 6.1 so
    62	   UDF/SQL/AI extend an existing contract rather than fork it.
    63	
    64	---
    65	
    66	## 2. Ownership & lifetime model
    67	
    68	### 2.1 The owning session (`WorkbookSession`)
    69	
    70	The engine already anticipates this consolidation — `crates/ql-exec/src/calcgraph_session.rs:69-71`:
    71	
    72	> *"Phase 6.1 `WorkbookSession` will absorb Workbook + OpLog + CalcgraphSession + PlanCache +
    73	> FunctionRegistry into ONE owning struct that the binding crate can wrap cleanly (per GAP-PS-09)."*
    74	
    75	`WorkbookSession` (built in 6.1B) **owns**:
    76	
    77	| Owned component | Source today | Role |
    78	|-----------------|--------------|------|
    79	| `Workbook` | `ql-storage` | Cell/sheet/table/name/format storage |
    80	| `OpLog` (**mandatory, single-writer** — §4.0) | `ql-oplog` | Edit history → version token, undo/redo, save/load |
    81	| `CalcgraphSession` | `ql-exec/src/calcgraph_session.rs` | Dependency graph + dirty propagation |
    82	| `PlanCache` | `ql-exec` | Compiled formula plans — **see LOW-1 below** |
    83	| `FunctionRegistry` (+ `FunctionMetadata`, §10) | `ql-functions/src/registry.rs` | Built-in + custom (UDF) dispatch + metadata |
    84	| **Cancellation registry** *(new)* | — | op-id → token/deadline/terminal-state (§6) |
    85	| **Event queue** *(new)* | — | structured diagnostics/events (§9) |
    86	
    87	Today these are constructed per-edit via `WorkbookRuntime::with_oplog_and_graph(...)` (a per-edit
    88	borrow window). 6.1B inverts it: the session owns them; the per-edit `WorkbookRuntime` borrow is
    89	constructed *internally* so it never crosses FFI.
    90	
    91	**LOW-1 — `PlanCache` is an explicit 6.1B refactor, not free.** `WorkbookRuntime::new` /
    92	`with_oplog_and_graph` (`workbook_runtime/mod.rs:140/162/225`) each allocate a *fresh private*
    93	`plan_cache`. Constructing a runtime per command would reset the cache and make `cache_stats`
    94	meaningless. 6.1B MUST refactor `WorkbookRuntime` to borrow a **session-owned** `PlanCache` (or move
    95	the runtime methods onto `WorkbookSession`). This is flagged work, not an emergent property.
    96	
    97	### 2.2 FFI handle contract
    98	
    99	- A binding holds an **opaque handle** to a `WorkbookSession` (Node: `#[napi]` over
   100	  `Arc<Mutex<WorkbookSession>>`; C: opaque ptr + `qb_session_free`; WASM: JS handle; Python: PyO3
   101	  class). **No method returns a borrowed Rust ref across FFI.** Tabular results are owned buffers or
   102	  Arrow `RecordBatch` handles with explicit release (C: `qb_release_*`; managed: GC).
   103	  - **✅ Node realized (6.1B inc.2d, 2026-05-28):** `ql-bindings-node` exposes the **`Session`** `#[napi]`
   104	    class over `Arc<parking_lot::Mutex<ql_exec::WorkbookSession>>` (the smoke surface: `new`/`addSheet`/
