   115	    `loadQuantbookEngine()`. The rebuilt cdylib also made the source-only `CollabSession` fixes B#1 +
   116	    S2-01 live, now backed by regression tests. Full IDE suite 1435/0/25. Synthesis
   117	    `docs/audits/2026-05-28-6-1b-ide-node-migration/`. **Driving the live `CellGridPanel` off `Session`
   118	    stays deferred** (the panel needs `workbookSnapshotDelta`/presence/transport, none yet on `Session`).
   119	- Long-running / multi-call state (transactions §3.4, operations §6) is referenced by **opaque IDs**,
   120	  never by a borrowed runtime object.
   121	
   122	### 2.3 Lifecycle states
   123	
   124	```
   125	New ──open/import──▶ Ready ──(edit/recalc/query)──▶ Ready
   126	  │                    │  ╲
   127	  │                    │   ╲──start long op──▶ Busy ──(complete/cancel)──▶ Ready
   128	  │                    ├──save/export──▶ Ready (persisted)
   129	  │                    └──close────────▶ Closed (terminal)
   130	  └──(error before Ready)──▶ Faulted (terminal; only diagnostics + close)
   131	```
   132	
   133	- **`Busy`** *(new — HIGH-1)*: the session is executing a long operation that owns mutable engine
   134	  state (in-engine recalc, a staged op). Commands that mutate or recalc are rejected with
   135	  `EngineError{class:Lifecycle, code:"session_busy", details:{op_id}}`; read-only snapshot/query of the
   136	  *last committed* state and `cancel(op_id)`/`operation_status(op_id)` remain legal. This is what makes
   137	  the cancellation/lock story implementable over the synchronous compute core (§6/§7).
   138	- **`Closed`/`Faulted`** are terminal. Illegal-state calls return `Lifecycle`/`invalid_state`, never panic.
