   174	| `add_sheet(name, chunk_rows)` | v1 | `addSheet` | duplicate name → `Conflict`; invalid `chunk_rows` → `BadArgument` |
   175	| `rename_sheet(id, name)` | v1 | `renameSheet` | unknown id → `NotFound`; duplicate name → `Conflict` |
   176	| `delete_sheet(id)` | v1 | `deleteSheet` | unknown id → **`NotFound`** (storage `remove_sheet` `workbook.rs:749` silently no-ops — 6.1B MUST wrap fail-loud). Deletion is a **tombstone** (preserves cells for restore); document refs-to-deleted-sheet behavior (`#REF!` vs preserved) as a locked decision in 6.1B. |
   177	| `restore_sheet(id)` | v1 | `restoreSheet` | not-tombstoned / unknown id → `NotFound`/`Conflict` (storage `restore_sheet` `:781` silently no-ops — wrap fail-loud) |
   178	| `move_sheet(id, index)` | v1 | `moveSheet` | unknown id → `NotFound`; out-of-range index → **`BadArgument`** (storage `move_sheet` `:809` silently clamps — wrap fail-loud, do not inherit clamp) |
   179	| `set_name(name, target)` | v1 | `SetName` / names | redefinition policy locked in 6.1B |
   180	| table ops `create/rename/rename_column/resize/drop_table` | v1 (single-writer) | `workbook_runtime/tables.rs` | **single-writer only**; collaborative table-merge DEFERRED (Phase 5 EC#2 — no collaborative producer; a future one MUST land conflict-resolution + `removed_cells`) |
   181	
   182	### 3.4 Batch / transaction (HIGH-3 — transport-neutral; atomicity defined per layer)
   183	| Command | Tier | Backed by | Notes |
   184	|---------|------|-----------|-------|
   185	| `batch(ops, options) -> BatchResult` | v1 | `WorkbookTransaction` + `Op::BatchCommit` | **Request-scoped, single call.** `options` = `{undo_group_id?, undo_label?}`. The whole batch is one undo unit. |
   186	| `begin_transaction() -> txn_id` / `txn_add(txn_id, op)` / `commit_transaction(txn_id) -> result` / `rollback_transaction(txn_id)` | v1 | opaque handle owning **buffered DTOs** | For multi-call grouping. The handle owns buffered ops + an undo-group + optional deadline — **never** a borrowed `WorkbookTransaction<'_>` (`transaction.rs:80` holds `&mut Workbook`, which cannot cross FFI). |
   187	
   188	**Atomicity, defined per layer (the word "atomic" was conflated):**
   189	- **Validation + local commit:** all-or-nothing. The producer validates/buffers, appends
   190	  `Op::BatchCommit` *before* mutating the workbook (`transaction.rs:293`), so an append/validation
   191	  failure leaves the workbook unchanged. ✅ atomic.
   192	- **Op-log append:** the `BatchCommit` op is a single atomic log entry. ✅ atomic.
   193	- **Replay from a persisted log:** **NOT rollback-atomic.** `Op::BatchCommit` replay applies inner ops
   194	  sequentially and returns on the first inner failure with no rollback of earlier inner effects
   195	  (`crates/ql-oplog/src/replay.rs:889-895`). The contract states this **honestly**: replay is
   196	  *fail-loud but not transactional*. (Making replay rollback-atomic requires staged/clone replay —
   197	  out of v1 scope; tracked for the collaborative producer work.)
   198	- **Undo grouping:** the batch is one undo unit.
   199	
   200	**Multi-call transaction handle — v1 implementation (inc.2c-5, `WorkbookSession`):**
   201	- The handle is a **pure `SessionOp` buffer holding NO engine borrow** (`txns:
   202	  HashMap<TransactionId, Vec<SessionOp>>`). `begin_transaction` allocates an empty
   203	  buffer; `txn_add` appends; `commit_transaction` drains it through the **same**
   204	  `batch` machinery (so a transaction inherits batch's validation-atomicity, graph
   205	  consistency, one `Op::BatchCommit`, single state tick, and the same-cell
   206	  value/formula conflict guard — two value/formula ops on one cell →
   207	  `conflicting_batch_ops` at commit); `rollback_transaction` drops the buffer.
   208	- **No lock between `begin` and `commit`:** interleaved single edits / other
   209	  transactions are permitted; the buffer is validated against the workbook state
   210	  **at commit time** (a sheet deleted after `txn_add` → `sheet_not_found` at commit),
   211	  not at add time. This is the no-borrow-across-FFI consequence (a borrowed
   212	  `WorkbookTransaction<'_>` cannot cross FFI).
   213	- **Lifecycle:** `begin`/`txn_add`/`commit` require `Ready` (forward progress →
   214	  `invalid_state` on Busy/terminal). `rollback` is ungated (cleanup is always
   215	  permitted). `close` drops all open buffers.
   216	- **Failed commit leaves the transaction OPEN** (the buffer is restored): `batch`
   217	  is validation-atomic, so a rejected commit applied nothing — the caller may
   218	  fix-and-retry or `rollback`. A successful commit consumes the handle. Unknown
   219	  handle → fail-loud `NotFound`/`transaction_not_found` (never a silent no-op).
   220	- **v1 limitations:** `txns` grows unbounded if callers `begin` without

