   430	"compute on a clone, swap atomically" and "discard partial results mid-flight" are **not available in
   431	v1** without a compute-core refactor. The contract is scoped to what is implementable:
   432	
   433	### 6.1 Universal: every long op has an identity
   434	`recalc_*`, `query_range` over large ranges, UDF (6.4), SQL (6.5), AI (6.6) return an **operation ID**
   435	and register `{optional deadline, cancel token, terminal state}`. `OperationState`: `Running` →
   436	`Completed | Canceled | Failed(EngineError)` (terminal, immutable). The session is `Busy` (§2.3) while
   437	an op owns mutable engine state.
   438	
   439	### 6.2 Out-of-process work: hard no-late-commit (UDF/SQL/AI)
   440	A canceled/timed-out **UDF** is hard-canceled by **killing the worker process** (decision-lock §5.2);
   441	its result is discarded and the cell gets a deterministic `Canceled` diagnostic. The same applies to
   442	SQL/AI (cancel the outstanding request). **No late commit** — guaranteed because the work is off-engine.
   443	
   444	### 6.3 Staged in-engine work (future): commit-once
   445	When a staged-recalc protocol lands (compute into a write-set, check the token before a single commit),
   446	in-engine recalc also gets hard mid-flight cancel + no-late-commit. This requires the compute-core
   447	refactor and is **explicitly post-6.1** (a `recompute_into(write_set)` API + a `Clone`/snapshot of
   448	`CalcgraphSession`).
   449	
   450	### 6.4 In-engine recalc TODAY: pre-start cancel only (v1 guarantee)
   451	For `recalc_dirty`/`recalc_all` in v1: `cancel(op_id)` **before execution begins** prevents the run;
   452	**once running, the synchronous pass completes** (it is fast — incremental dirty recalc is the common
   453	path) and commits, then transitions to `Completed`. The contract does **not** promise mid-flight
   454	abort or partial-result rollback for in-engine recalc in v1, and bindings MUST NOT claim it (this is
   455	the exact wording that prevents the binding fork). Sync FFI: `start→poll/wait/cancel`; async bindings
   456	`await` the same op; both surface `Canceled` identically when the pre-start cancel wins.
   457	
   458	---
   459	
   460	## 7. Sync/async & concurrency discipline
   461	
   462	**Rule: locks guard state transitions, not arbitrary waiting** (decision-lock §3.5). Canonical lesson:
   463	`flushPendingToTransport` (`lib.rs:~3421-3445`) extracts the ack handle *under* the lock, **drops the
   464	lock**, then `spawn_blocking(|| handle.wait_for_drain())`. Obligations:
   465	
   466	1. A binding wraps the session in its lock (`Arc<Mutex<..>>` Node; GIL-aware Python). Mutating/querying
   467	   commands hold the lock for the **state transition only**.
   468	2. No command holds the session lock across a blocking wait, an `await`, or a round-trip into user code
   469	   (UDF/AI). Long ops use the §2.3 `Busy` state: acquire lock → mark `Busy` + register op → **release
   470	   lock** → execute → re-acquire to commit + clear `Busy`. (For v1 in-engine recalc the execute step is
   471	   the synchronous pass per §6.4; for UDF/SQL it is genuinely off-lock.)
   472	3. Soundness closures carried forward: V2.4 (no `&mut self` UB across napi) + V2.5 (no event-loop
   473	   block). New long-op surfaces replicate the detach-then-off-lock shape.
   474	
   475	---
   476	
   477	## 8. Panic & validation boundary
   478	
   479	1. **Validation at the boundary** before engine work (NaN/Inf/negative/fractional coords, oversize
   480	   indices, bad UTF-8) → `EngineError{class:BadArgument}` (generalizes today's `appendPut*` validation
   481	   + `[bad_argument]`). Lives once in the common layer.
   482	2. **Panic catch** (LOW-2 specifics): FFI crates MUST build with **`panic = "unwind"`** (else abort
   483	   remains possible and this guarantee is void). A single shared `catch_unwind` wraps the common
   484	   command dispatcher **before** any FFI boundary observes unwinding, converting a panic to
   485	   `EngineError{class:Internal, code:"panic"}`. Because the Node wrapper uses `parking_lot::Mutex`
   486	   (no poisoning, `lib.rs:1121`), the conservative rule is: **any panic during a mutating command marks
   487	   the session `Faulted`**; read-only command panics are surfaced as `Internal` without faulting (the
   488	   committed state is intact). A panic is never a silent crash, never a swallowed fallback.
   489	3. C ABI: no `panic` unwinds across `extern "C"` (UB) — verified by BND-6-02.
   490	
   491	---
   492	
   493	## 9. Event & diagnostic stream (MED-5: cursor + backpressure locked)
   494	
   495	- **`Event`** (versioned union): `RecalcProgress{op_id,done,total}`,
   496	  `CellDiagnostic{addr,severity,code,message}`, `OperationCompleted{op_id,state}`,
   497	  `Provenance{addr,source}` (shaped now for UDF/SQL/AI), `StructureChanged{kind,target}`.
   498	- **Queue model (locked):** a single **append-only ring** with a **monotonic global cursor**.
   499	  `poll_events(cursor) -> EventPage{events[], next_cursor, dropped?}` **reads** (does not drain) from
   500	  the cursor — so pull pollers and push subscribers never starve each other. Retention is a bounded
   501	  window; if a consumer falls behind the horizon, the page carries `dropped:true` + a
   502	  `FullResyncRequired` event (the consumer reseeds via `snapshot()`), rather than silently losing
   503	  events. Ordering: an `OperationCompleted{op_id}` event never precedes the events produced by that op.
   504	- `Diagnostic` is the same DTO whether returned synchronously (`validate_formula`) or via the stream.
   505	
   506	---
   507	
   508	## 10. Function metadata & graph-invalidation contract (R-P6-4 / 6.4-0)
   509	
   510	### 10.1 The gap (CLOSED by 6.4-0 substrate + 6.4-1 substrate-completion, 2026-05-28; commits `ac20a432c63` + audit-fix `63592126afe` + `1a7dfee12b0` + audit-fix `befcd0d34cc`)
   511	**Pre-substrate (historical):** `FunctionRegistry` (`ql-functions/src/registry.rs`) stored **dispatch only**.
   512	Volatility + reference-shape lived in **two hardcoded whitelists** in `calcgraph_session.rs`
   513	(`is_volatile_function` `:149-164`; `is_address_only_reference_fn` `:201-203`); `FormulaDeps`
   514	had no `functions_used` reverse index. A Python UDF couldn't be added to a hardcoded match,
   515	and a registration/metadata change couldn't dirty its callers → silent graph bypass.
   516	
   517	**Post-substrate (6.4-0 SHIPPED 2026-05-28):**
   518	- `FunctionRegistry` carries a first-class `metadata: HashMap<String, FunctionMetadata>` keyed by
   519	  canonical (ASCII-uppercase) name; populated for every builtin via `register_builtin_metadata`
   520	  at `default_registry()` tail. Public API: `metadata(name)` / `register_metadata(meta)` /

