    50	### Known v1 limitations (documented, not bugs — revisit when relevant)
    51	- **Version token = `{epoch, state_seq}`** (inc.2c-3): `state_seq` (NOT `oplog.len()`) advances on every
    52	  committed mutation + every recompute-with-changes, so the token is a true *state* token for delta.
    53	- **`snapshot_delta` = change-log design (a)** keyed by `state_seq` (bounded `CHANGE_LOG_CAP`); §4.3
    54	  rules implemented (empty→NoPriorVersion, epoch→EpochMismatch, future→fail-loud `invalid_version_token`,
    55	  `seq<floor`→StaleHorizon). **Epoch-bump (forces full rebuild) for states the delta DTO can't express:**
    56	  `move_sheet` (reorder), `restore_sheet` (reappears at an unconveyable position), all table ops (rewrite
    57	  arbitrary formula cells). `set_name` is delta-invisible (no names field in the snapshot DTO).
    58	- A tombstoned sheet is uniformly `NotFound` for reads + cell/structure edits (`require_live_sheet`,
    59	  incl. rename_sheet + create_table per F6); delete/restore use a tombstone pre-check (F5: double-delete
    60	  = true no-op; restore-of-live = `Conflict/sheet_not_deleted`). Formula EVAL still reads tombstoned
    61	  sheets (deliberate v1 semantic, F9 — no `#REF!` until v1.5 D7).
    62	- `ops` HashMap + `events` Vec grow **unbounded** (no retention horizon yet); `change_log` IS bounded.
    63	  The Loro undo stack is capped at **100 steps** (Loro default; inc.2c-7 L1) — oldest unit silently
    64	  dropped past 100 undoable commands (bounded retention, intentional v1).
    65	- ✅ **F2 CLOSED (inc.2c-6, `d8d22a04248`):** `set_value(Blank)` (+ batch/transaction Blank-clears) now
    66	  emit a replayable **`Op::ClearValue`** → durable on save/load AND on undo's replay re-materialization.
    67	  `clear_formula` deliberately unchanged (preserves values — Excel convert-to-literal).
    68	- **undo/redo (inc.2c-7):** Loro `UndoManager` field (`set_merge_interval(0)`) → 1 command = 1 undo unit
    69	  (every command = one Loro commit; `rename_table`/`rename_column` wrapped in `grouped()` since they emit
    70	  N+1 commits via the F10 loop). `rematerialize` = replay the post-undo op-log onto a CLONE of the
    71	  construction-time **baseline workbook** (NOT a fresh empty one — closes the Codex-HIGH populated-
    72	  `from_workbook` data-loss path) → `rebuild_from_workbook` → `recompute_all` (op-log detached) →
    73	  `bump_epoch`. Empty stack → `consumed:false`. Linear single-writer replay reproduces renames without
    74	  the ql-collab repair passes (concurrency-only).
    75	- ✅ **F10 CLOSED (inc.2c-8, `dca5695549e`): table rename/rename_column are now append-before-mutate
    76	  atomic** — `rename_table`/`rename_column` collect the rename op + all `PutFormula` rewrites into ONE
    77	  `Op::BatchCommit` appended before any mutation (mirroring `rename_sheet`). Replay applies the inner ops
    78	  in order (re-key, then rewrite text — complementary). Focused Codex audit clean (no HIGH/MED). The undo
    79	  `grouped()` wrapper is now defense-in-depth (the renames are single-commit by construction).
