   562	- The contract (`session-api.md` §4.0) + the `SessionVersion` doc comment in `dto.rs` already reflect this.
   563	
   564	---
   565	
   566	## 5. Method-by-method implementation map
   567	
   568	Build a per-edit runtime with `WorkbookRuntime::with_session_state(&mut self.workbook, &self.registry,
   569	&mut self.oplog, &mut self.graph, &mut self.plan_cache)` then call the existing mutator. Group order:
   570	
   571	| Trait method | Implement via | Notes |
   572	|--------------|---------------|-------|
   573	| `set_value` | `WorkbookRuntime::set_value` | map `CellValue` → `ql_types::Value`; `Pending` is invalid as *input* → `BadArgument` |
   574	| `set_formula` | `set_formula` | parse/bind err → `Compute` `EngineError` (or `Diagnostic`); §5.5 |
   575	| `clear` | `clear_formula` | |
   576	| `validate_formula` | `validate_formula` (no mutation) | returns `Vec<Diagnostic>` |
   577	| `set_format`/`register_format` | format-table ops | |
   578	| `add_sheet`/`rename_sheet` | `WorkbookRuntime` sheet ops (`sheets.rs`) | duplicate→`Conflict`, unknown→`NotFound` |
   579	| `delete_sheet`/`restore_sheet`/`move_sheet` | **NEW fail-loud wrappers** (MED-3) | `ql-storage::Workbook::{remove,restore,move}_sheet` silently no-op/clamp (`workbook.rs:749/781/809`) — wrap: check existence/range FIRST, return `NotFound`/`BadArgument`, then call |
   580	| `set_name` | names (`names.rs`) | |
   581	| `create_table`/`rename_table`/`rename_column`/`resize_table`/`drop_table` | `workbook_runtime/tables.rs` | name-keyed; `TableSpec` → `create_table(name, sheet, top_row, top_col, rows, cols, has_header, has_totals, column_names)` |
   582	| `batch` | buffer ops → one `Op::BatchCommit` via `WorkbookTransaction` (`transaction.rs`) | atomicity per §3.4 (validation+local-commit atomic; replay NOT rollback-atomic — honest) |
   583	| `begin/txn_add/commit/rollback_transaction` | `txns` map of buffered `SessionOp` → commit builds a `batch` | opaque handle, no borrowed runtime |
   584	| `recalc_dirty`/`recalc_all` | `recompute_dirty`/`recompute_all` | return `op_id`; **pre-start cancel only** (§6 / HIGH-1); set `Busy` around the call |
   585	| `mark_volatiles_dirty` | volatile pass | |
   586	| `query_range` | iterate owned `Workbook` cells in range → columnar `RangeResult` | batch-shaped |
   587	| `snapshot` | iterate owned `Workbook` (sheets/cells/formats) → `WorkbookSnapshot` + `{epoch,op_count}` token | **no replay** — single-writer owns a live workbook (unlike the collab `rebuild_workbook` path). Mirror the napi `workbook_snapshot` builder (`lib.rs:2141+`) but read the live workbook. |
   588	| `snapshot_delta` | §4 token logic + walk new ops | |
   589	| `cell` | `Workbook` cell lookup | |
   590	| `list_sheets` | `Workbook` sheets (skip tombstoned) | |
   591	| `undo`/`redo`/`can_undo`/`can_redo` | op-log/undo machinery | empty stack → `consumed:false`; bump `epoch` (clears delta cache) |
   592	| `register_function`/`unregister_function`/`list_functions` | `FunctionRegistry` + §10 metadata | collision→`Conflict` (not panic); functions_used invalidation is 6.4-0 |
   593	| `cancel`/`operation_status` | `ops` registry | |
   594	| `poll_events` | `events` ring read-from-cursor (no drain) | |
   595	| `write_range`/`publish_dataset`/`bind_range`/`refresh_source`/`materialize_query` | **reserved** | return `EngineError{class:Capability, code:"not_implemented_in_v1_core"}` until 6.4/6.5 — an explicit, surfaced "not yet", NOT a silent fallback |
   596	
   597	---
   598	
   599	## 6. The hard parts (concrete approaches)
   600	
   601	- **Cancellation / `Busy` (HIGH-1):** `recompute_*` are synchronous `&mut self` commit-as-you-go loops
   602	  (`recompute.rs:61/153/252/445`); `CalcgraphSession` is not `Clone`. So v1 = **pre-start cancel only**:
   603	  `recalc_*` registers an op, sets `state = Busy`, checks the cancel token *before* invoking the synchronous
   604	  pass; if canceled pre-start → `OperationState::Canceled`, no recompute; else run to completion, commit,
   605	  `state = Ready`, emit `OperationCompleted`. Do **not** promise mid-flight abort. Hard mid-flight cancel
   606	  (staged recalc) + out-of-process UDF worker-kill are later (§6.3 of the contract). While `Busy`, mutating/
   607	  recalc commands return `session_busy`; read-only snapshot of the last committed state stays legal.
   608	- **Fail-loud sheet ops (MED-3):** wrap the storage no-op/clamp methods — validate first, return
   609	  `NotFound`/`BadArgument`, then mutate.
   610	- **`EngineError` Appendix A (MED-1):** implement `From<RuntimeError>`, `From<ReplayError>`,
