   991	
   992	    /// **6.4B (item H):** the operation-level UDF time budget for ONE recompute
   993	    /// pass — `Some(now + UDF_OP_BUDGET)` iff a worker is attached, else `None`.
   994	    /// With no worker, UDFs are `#CALC!` no-worker and never block, so a budget
   995	    /// would be meaningless and the `None` path keeps non-UDF recompute byte-for-byte
   996	    /// unchanged. EVERY full-pass recompute that can dispatch a UDF must arm this so
   997	    /// the aggregate stall is bounded (not just the explicit `recalc_*` paths):
   998	    /// [`run_recalc`], [`rematerialize`] (undo/redo), and the `open` load path all
   999	    /// route through it (6.4B closure-audit MED — the budget was previously armed
