quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:744:**✅ 6.4-0 — Function-metadata substrate SHIPPED 2026-05-28 (parallel 2-way audit).** Decision-lock §2 item 5; the prerequisite for 6.4 Python UDFs and for contract §10.3 registration-invalidation. Replaces the two hardcoded whitelists in `ql-exec::calcgraph_session` (`is_volatile_function` `:149-164`, `is_address_only_reference_fn` `:201-203`) with first-class `FunctionMetadata` stored on `FunctionRegistry`, and adds a `functions_used: HashMap<Arc<str>, HashSet<NodeId>>` reverse index on `CalcgraphSession` + two hooks `on_function_registered` / `on_function_unregistered`. **LAST CODE commits:** `63592126afe` (audit-fix; H2 production registry threading + 5 new substrate tests + 3 polish items) ← `ac20a432c63` (substrate; +1071/-117 across 8 files). **Substrate in 4 phases (each cleanly green):** (1) `ql-functions::FunctionRegistry` gains `metadata: HashMap<String, FunctionMetadata>` field + 5 public methods (`metadata` / `register_metadata` / `unregister_metadata` / `iter_metadata` / `metadata_count`) + a `FunctionRegistryError` enum (Conflict / NotFound); `default_registry()` runs a new `register_builtin_metadata` pass (Phase 1 explicit overrides match the prior whitelists byte-for-byte: NOW/TODAY/RAND/RANDBETWEEN/RANDARRAY → `Volatility::Volatile`; INDIRECT/OFFSET/INFO/CELL → `Volatility::Dynamic`; ROW/COLUMN/ROWS/COLUMNS/ISREF → `DepShape::AddressOnly`; Phase 2 defaults for every other dispatched builtin via `r.fns.keys()`); boot-time `assert!`-driven migration-shim invariant ("every dispatched fn has metadata"); `ql-functions` gains a one-way dep on `ql-session` (no cycle). (2) `FormulaDeps` gains `pub functions_used: Vec<Arc<str>>`; walker pushes at the TOP of the `ExprPlan::Function` arm BEFORE any routing decision, so ROW / ISREF / nested-fn paths all participate uniformly. (3) Walker signature `walk_plan_for_deps(plan, deps, registry)` + `walk_plan_for_address_only_deps` parallel; `is_volatile_function(registry, name)` reads `metadata.volatility ∈ {Volatile, Dynamic}` (migration-preserving); `is_address_only_reference_fn(registry, name)` reads `metadata.dep_shape == AddressOnly`; `rebuild_from_workbook(wb)` keeps its zero-arg public signature (constructs `default_registry()` internally) + new `rebuild_from_workbook_with_registry(wb, registry)` for production callers that own a session-scoped registry; 4 production call sites in `workbook_runtime/{cells, recompute, tables}.rs` thread `self.registry`; 53 test sites sed-batched. (4) `CalcgraphSession.functions_used` reverse-index field mirrors `name_to_formulas` pattern (populate at `extract_and_register_deps` after dedupe, cleanup at `remove_formula_deps`); storage gate widened from `!deps.is_empty() || deps.is_volatile` to also include `!deps.functions_used.is_empty() || !deps.names.is_empty() || !deps.tables.is_empty()` — closes a latent `ROW(MyName)` cleanup bug where the address-only walker's `names` push (without `named_ranges`) caused `name_to_formulas[MYNAME]` to leak on rebind; two new hooks return the dirtied-count, mirror `on_set_name`'s transitive BFS-fanout (Phase 3.10 H2 semantics) via `mark_dirty_from_cell_write`, bump new `HookCounts.function_registered` / `function_unregistered` counters; `functions_used_for(name)` read-only inspector. **Parallel Codex (gpt-5.5 xhigh) + Opus reviewer audit; verdict SHIP-WITH-FIXES** — 3 HIGH (1 fixed in audit-fix, 2 filed for 6.4 entry-plan), 5 MED (2 closed in audit-fix or by H3 disposition, 3 filed for 6.4), 4 LOW (all 4 closed in audit-fix), 5 INFO. Synthesis `docs/audits/2026-05-28-6-4-0-substrate-audit/SYNTHESIS.md`. **Audit-fix `63592126afe`:** (1) **H2 (HIGH)** — `WorkbookRuntime::recompute_all`'s cycle pre-pass at `workbook_runtime/recompute.rs:111` was building an ephemeral session via the zero-arg `rebuild_from_workbook(wb)`, silently falling back to `default_registry()` (benign today; silent divergence at 6.4 with UDFs); swapped to `_with_registry(self.workbook, self.registry)`. (2) **Codex A LOW** — `unregister_metadata` could remove builtin metadata (leaving dispatch present + metadata absent = silent walker regression); audit-fix guards via `if self.fns.contains_key(upper) → Conflict`. (3) **Opus L2** — `debug_assert!` migration-shim invariant upgraded to `assert!` (release builds now fail loud at boot rather than ship with silent unknown-fn fallback). (4) **Opus L3** — `HookCounts` gains `function_registered` / `function_unregistered` fields for parity. (5) **Opus M4 + Codex D LOW** — 5 new substrate tests pin: ROW + ISREF in `functions_used` (push-before-routing invariant); `ROW(NOW())` records BOTH names AND propagates `is_volatile` through the address-only walker's registry-passing delegation; transitive fanout on `on_function_registered` (chain `A1=NOW(), B1=A1+1, C1=B1+1` all dirty); `ROW(MyName)` cleanup regression (widened-storage-gate fix pin); `unregister_metadata` builtin-guard. (6) **H3 (HIGH) DOC-honesty correction** — hook docstrings now state plainly: substrate hooks ONLY dirty + transitive-fan; they do NOT re-extract deps. Contract §10.3 says "register / unregister dirties every formula referencing that canonical name (re-extract deps + reschedule)" — substrate satisfies the "dirty + reschedule" halves; "re-extract deps" lands at the 6.4 orchestrator level. **Tracked block-on-6.4-entry:** **H1** — `ql-exec::plan` carries two more hardcoded `matches!` whitelists (`is_aggregate_function`:406-505, `is_reference_aware_function`:566-571) that drive the binder's `arg_ctx` decision; UDFs with range args (every `BatchShape::ArrayBatch` UDF per the contract DTO) won't bind until these also derive from registry metadata. The substrate is "two-thirds of the UDF prerequisite"; H1 is the missing third. **H3** — re-extract gap; 6.4 closes via either (1) `fn_gen: u64` counter on `PlanCache` (mirror `name_gen` at `plan_cache.rs:69-74`; bump per register/unregister; cache misses trigger re-bind + re-extract on next eval) or (2) per-dependent `reextract_deps(node, &cached_plan, &workbook, &registry)` in the `WorkbookSession::register_function` orchestrator. **Filed for 6.4 (non-blocking):** M1 `FormulaDeps::is_empty/len()` lie (only check 2 of 6 fields); M3 `iter_metadata` HashMap-order (add `sorted_metadata()` view, matching the 6.1C H2 ordering discipline); M5 `FunctionRegistryError → EngineError` mapper + Appendix A `function_exists` / `function_not_found` rows; I1 `DepShape::LazyShape` for ISREF (today: hardcoded `name == "ISREF"` short-circuit at the walker); I2 metadata-update atomicity policy docs; L1 walker hot-path `to_ascii_uppercase()` allocation per call. **Cycle budget honored:** Cycle 1 = substrate code; cycle 2 = audit-fix; doc-sync separate. **Verification (focused re-verify of affected lanes):** `cargo build -p ql-exec -p ql-functions -p ql-bindings-node` clean; `cargo test -p ql-exec --lib` **742/0** (732 pre-substrate + 6 cycle-1 + 4 audit-fix); `cargo test -p ql-functions --lib` **1815/0** (1808 pre-substrate + 8 cycle-1; audit-fix rewrote one test, net unchanged); `cargo check --workspace` clean; clippy clean for edits (pre-existing warnings in ql-collab unchanged); `node crates/ql-bindings-node/tests/smoke_session.mjs` PASS. **NEXT (canonical decision-lock §2 item 6): 6.4 Python UDFs (the wedge function).** Block-on-entry: close H1 (plan.rs whitelists) + H3 (re-extract via fn_gen or per-dependent reextract) in the 6.4 entry-plan; ship M1/M3/M5/I1/I2 as substrate-completion sub-increments at 6.4 entry; L1 + cross-cutting effective-extent serializer fix on the 6.4 backlog list.
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:746:**[superseded note] ✅ 6.1A SHIPPED 2026-05-26** (docs-only, no code cycle): `docs/api/session-api.md` — the stable engine session contract (API6-01/02/03). Covers command surface (product commands ≠ collab op variants), versioned DTOs, `EngineError` taxonomy, operation-lifecycle + cancellation, sync/async + panic/validation boundary, event/diagnostic stream, function-metadata + graph-invalidation contract (the 6.4-0 prerequisite), per-binding obligations + golden-flow matrix. Bottom-up-extracted from the proven napi `CollabSession` surface + single-writer `WorkbookRuntime`; anchors verified at source (`calcgraph_session.rs:69-71` owning-session anticipation, `:149-164`/`:201-203` hardcoded whitelists = the metadata gap, `lib.rs:306-349` the `[kind]` error workaround). **✅ Codex-validated (gpt-5.5 xhigh, verdict REVISE → all 5 HIGH/5 MED/2 LOW/1 INFO resolved in `session-api.md` v2; review: `docs/api/codex-6-1a-review.md`).** Key locks added: single-writer `OpLog` mandatory → its Loro VV is the version token (resolves the deferred-collab token gap); cancellation scoped honestly (in-engine recalc = pre-start cancel only in v1; hard no-late-commit only for out-of-process UDF/SQL/AI; `Busy` lifecycle state); `batch(ops,options)` + opaque transaction handle (no RAII borrow across FFI); reserved bulk `write_range`/`publish_dataset`/`bind_range`/`refresh_source`/`materialize_query` for 6.4/6.5; `functions_used` reverse index + registration invalidation; malformed version token = fail-loud `invalid_version_token` (No-Fallbacks); error variant→code mapping appendix. **NEXT = 6.1B** (implement `WorkbookSession`; CODE phase → fresh session).
