  3300	/// **6.4-1 (2026-05-28; M5):** map `FunctionRegistryError` to the
  3301	/// binding-neutral `EngineError` taxonomy. Used by the (forthcoming, 6.4)
  3302	/// `WorkbookSession::register_function` / `unregister_function` /
  3303	/// `list_functions` trait methods to translate the registry-level error
  3304	/// into the contract §10.3 caller-visible codes
  3305	/// (`function_exists` / `function_not_found`). Mirrors the
  3306	/// `map_runtime_err` / `map_persistence_err` / `map_xlsx_err` / `map_csv_err`
  3307	/// pattern — one mapper per Appendix-A row family, exhaustive match, never
  3308	/// a silent default.
  3309	///
  3310	/// Both registry-level variants land in this mapper:
  3311	/// - `Conflict { name }` → `Conflict` / `function_exists`. The substrate's
  3312	///   `unregister_metadata` builtin-guard (6.4-0 audit-fix) ALSO returns
  3313	///   `Conflict` (with a different message) to signal that a built-in's
  3314	///   metadata can'\''t be removed — both surface here as the same caller-
  3315	///   visible code; the message disambiguates.
  3316	/// - `NotFound { name }` → `NotFound` / `function_not_found`. Matches the
  3317	///   contract §10.3 wording exactly.
  3318	///
  3319	/// No `_ => unmapped_*_error` arm because `FunctionRegistryError` is a
  3320	/// closed enum we own — adding a new variant without a mapping should
  3321	/// surface as a compile error at this match, not a silent runtime
  3322	/// catch-all.
  3323	// **6.4-2 (2026-05-28):** the `#[allow(dead_code)]` from 6.4-1 is REMOVED —
  3324	// `WorkbookSession::register_function` and `unregister_function` now wire
  3325	// this mapper into the engine→napi error surface (Appendix A
  3326	// `function_exists` / `function_not_found`).
  3327	fn map_function_registry_err(e: ql_functions::FunctionRegistryError) -> EngineError {
  3328	    use ql_functions::FunctionRegistryError as F;
  3329	    let display = e.to_string();
  3330	    match e {
  3331	        F::Conflict { .. } => EngineError::new(ErrorClass::Conflict, "function_exists", display),
  3332	        F::NotFound { .. } => EngineError::new(ErrorClass::NotFound, "function_not_found", display),
  3333	    }
  3334	}
