quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:549:✅ **5.7 V3.6 PHASE TERMINATION CLEAN** (V3.6.0.1 LOCK + V3.6.0.2 D1 + V3.6.0.X AUDIT-CLOSURE + V3.6.0.3 D2 + V3.6.0.X AUDIT-OF-D2 + V3.6.0.4 D3 + V3.6.0.X AUDIT-OF-D3 + V3.6.0.5 D4 + V3.6.0.X AUDIT-OF-D4 + V3.6.0.6 D5 + V3.6.0.X AUDIT-OF-D5 + V3.6.0.7 D6 SPIKE + V3.6.0.8.1 D6 LOCK + V3.6.0.8.2 ENGINE PART 1 + V3.6.0.8.3 ENGINE PART 2 napi + V3.6.0.8.4 AUDIT-OF-D6 + 5 HIGH CLOSURES + BENCH + V3.6.0.8.5 MOCHA + V3.6.0.10 D8 Op::RestoreSheet + V3.6.0.10 DOCS MEGAUDIT + V3.6.0.11 D9 typing-stroke watchdog SHIPPED 2026-05-23 → 05-26)** -- 9 D-decisions per V3.5.0.X Opus § F V3.6 ENTRY READINESS packet.  Status: D1-D6 + D8 + D9 SHIPPED; only D7 (#REF! substitution at V3.6.0.9) remains conditional pending user signal.  D6 perf contract delivered with 46× headroom (1.08 ms at 100 new cells vs 246 ms full snapshot).  D9 typing-stroke watchdog closes R-V3.5-7 false-negative.  V3.6 phase-termination megaudit unblocked at V3.6.0.11 ship.  D1 (Loro UndoManager `set_on_push` + `set_on_pop` callback wiring, HIGH PRIORITY): closes V3.5.0.X conservative `pure_local_frontier` gate properly via Loro 1.12.0's verified API (`OnPop = Box<dyn Fn(UndoOrRedo, CounterSpan, UndoItemMeta) + Send + Sync>` at registry/loro-internal-1.12.0/src/undo.rs:199); REMOVES `pure_local_frontier` field in V3.6.0.2.  D2 (session-wide RegisterFormat FormatTable cache): new `format_table_cache: HashMap<FormatId, Arc<str>>` field + new `CacheEffect::RegisterFormat` variant + new `FormatDefJson` napi struct + `WorkbookSnapshotJson.formats` additive field; unblocks D4 format-aware rendering.  D3 (per-cell op-index): new `cell_op_index: HashMap<(SheetId, RowId, ColId), Vec<usize>>` field; closes V3.5.0.6 R-V3.5-2 perf gap (invalidate_cell O(N) -> O(ops-for-this-cell)).  D4 (format-aware buildHtml rendering): engine-side `format_value` reuse via Phase 4.6 D-1 FormatTable; new `rendered: Option<String>` field on CellSnapshotJson; new `dateSystem: String` field on WorkbookSnapshotJson ("Excel1900" | "Excel1904"; String chosen over wrapper struct for simplicity; napi-rs auto-camelCases at JS boundary); workbook.locale() passthrough + per-snapshot parsed-format cache + Pending-skip per V3.6.0.X audit-of-D4 closures; CSP-safe.  D5 (IDE-facing `appendPutFormula` napi, NEW): thin wrapper over existing `Op::PutFormula`; unblocks end-to-end repaired-formula integration tests (closes V3.5.0.X A-HIGH-2 IDE-level verification gap).  D6 (incremental WorkbookSnapshot deltas): DEFER pending V3.6.0.7 mid-cycle profiling spike; ship only if cost > 50ms/call.  D7 (#REF! substitution): DEFER until user signal.  D8 (Op::RestoreSheet): DEFER until user signal.  D9 (sheet-tabs UX + mid-edit-render guard typing-stroke watchdog): DEFER sheet-tabs to V3.6+ multi-tab redesign per Opus § G; ship typing-stroke watchdog as V3.6.0.10 only if surfaced.  V3.6 sub-step rollout (actual + planned): V3.6.0.1 docs-only LOCK ✅; V3.6.0.2-0.6 priority ship (D1-D5) ✅; V3.6.0.7 profiling spike ✅ (verdict: D6 SHIPS); V3.6.0.8.1-8.5 D6 arc COMPLETE ✅ (D6 perf contract delivered with 46× headroom); V3.6.0.9 D7 #REF! conditional (PENDING user signal); V3.6.0.10 D8 Op::RestoreSheet ✅ SHIPPED + V3.6.0.10 docs megaudit ✅ SHIPPED; V3.6.0.11 D9 typing-stroke watchdog conditional (PENDING user signal); V3.6.0.X parallel Codex+Opus phase-termination megaudit + closures (PENDING at V3.6.0.11 ship; ~6-8 sessions).  Total estimated V3.6 wall time: 14-20 sessions.  **18 risks documented in plan as R-V3.6-1..18 + R-V3.6-NEW (the V3.6.0.7-spike-discovered rebuild_workbook dominant-cost risk, CLOSED-AT-V3.6.0.8.1 via option (a) cache rebuilt+repaired Workbook + clone-and-apply-delta)**.  All non-conditional risks closed; conditionals tied to D7/D9 surfacing.  Plan at `.plans/_active.md`.  ✅ **V3.6.0.2 D1 SHIPPED** at engine `89f5a5f9e0b`: REMOVED `pure_local_frontier` field + dispatch gate; ADDED `pending_undo_cells: Arc<Mutex<Option<Vec<(u16, u32, u32)>>>>` field + on_push closure encoding cells as LoroValue::List<List<I64>> into UndoItemMeta::value; undo/redo use top_undo_meta/top_redo_meta + pre-stage cells for synthetic inverse op's on_push; 2 V3.5.0.X regression tests REWRITTEN to verify partial-invalidate FIRES correctly (not full-rebuild fallback).  ✅ **V3.6.0.X AUDIT-CLOSURE SHIPPED** at engine `(THIS commit)`: Codex Lane A `docs/audits/2026-05-24-phase-5-7-v3-6-0-2-codex.md` (FAIL: 1 HIGH + 1 LOW + 2 INFO); Opus Lane B inline audit (PASS-WITH-CONVERGENT-FINDING).  Convergent HIGH (CODEX-V3-6-0-2-HIGH-1): grouped-undo + merge-interval-undo lose cells because Loro's `push_with_merge` discards subsequent meta when merging spans -- only the FIRST push's meta survives.  Codex empirically verified with `codex_tmp_grouped_undo_cache_probe` (4 stale cells remained post-undo); Opus independently confirmed by reading loro-internal-1.12.0/src/undo.rs:389-396.  Closure: new `inside_group: bool` + `undo_merge_interval_ms: i64` fields on CollabSession; start/end_undo_group + set_undo_merge_interval maintain these; append_op gates partial-invalidate behind `!inside_group && undo_merge_interval_ms == 0` (conservative full-rebuild fallback matches V3.5.0.6 semantics for grouped undo).  Clean fix (`set_top_undo_meta` to union cells) BLOCKED: API exists on loro_internal but not exposed on public `loro::UndoManager`; deferred to V3.6+ pending upstream contribution.  +2 ql-collab regression tests: grouped_undo_clears_cache_for_all_cells_in_the_group + merge_interval_undo_clears_cache_for_all_cells_in_window.  CODEX-LOW-1 (coverage expansion) DEFERRED to V3.6.0.3+ backlog.  Rule 4 arc terminus HELD at 6 throughout V3.6.0.2 + V3.6.0.X (new fields all Copy+Send+Sync trivially; 0 new triggers).  Cumulative V3.6 cycle through V3.6.0.X audit: +2 ql-collab tests (115 -> 117), IDE mocha unchanged at 346.  Audit transcripts: 33 (was 32; +1 V3.6.0.2 Codex Lane A).  Cumulative findings closed across Phase 5.7: 19+ HIGH + 50+ MEDIUM (was 18+ HIGH + 49+ MEDIUM).  ✅ **V3.6.0.3 D2 SHIPPED** at engine `ffa598a1c15` + IDE `b159c899359`: session-wide RegisterFormat FormatTable cache (new `format_table_cache: HashMap<FormatId, Arc<str>>` field on CollabSession + new `CacheEffect::RegisterFormat { id, string }` variant + walker integration; `apply_cache_effect` signature extended with 3rd param; all 3 callers updated; `force_clear_snapshot_cache` clears the cache; `rebuild_snapshot_cache` atomic-swaps; `invalidate_cell` uses throwaway local cache since RegisterFormat is session-wide) + new `FormatDefJson { id: FormatIdJson, string: String }` napi struct + `WorkbookSnapshotJson.formats: Vec<FormatDefJson>` additive field (populated from `Workbook.formats().iter()` -- authoritative; merges Builtin 0..=163 + Custom; avoids surfacing cross-peer cache-vs-Workbook divergence under concurrent RegisterFormat same-id-different-string).  IDE: `WorkbookSnapshotJson` interface gains required `formats: FormatDefJson[]` + new `FormatDefJson` interface; +4 mocha pinning shape; +1 stale V3.5.0.2 shape test updated; +10 V3.5.0.4b fixture additions for the now-required field.  +2 ql-collab regression tests: `register_format_op_populates_session_format_table_cache` + `register_format_cache_rebuilds_from_log_via_rebuild_snapshot_cache`.  Tests: ql-collab **119/119** (117 baseline + 2 new); IDE mocha **350/350** (346 baseline + 4 new).  Rule 4 arc terminus HELD at 6 (1 new ql-collab field + 1 new napi struct; positive Send+Sync via composition: `HashMap<K,V>: Send+Sync` iff both; `FormatId: Copy+Send+Sync`; `Arc<str>: Send+Sync`; `FormatDefJson` over `FormatIdJson` V3.5.0.5 walk + `String`; 0 new triggers).  Cumulative V3.6 cycle (through V3.6.0.3 D2): +4 ql-collab (115 -> 119); +4 IDE mocha (346 -> 350); audit transcripts still 33.  ✅ **V3.6.0.X AUDIT-OF-D2 SHIPPED** at engine `8480f247aea` + IDE `21fe6a73ec6` (2026-05-23).  Parallel Codex Lane A + Opus Lane B audit of V3.6.0.3 D2 surface; both PASS-WITH-FINDINGS.  Codex transcript: `docs/audits/2026-05-23-phase-5-7-v3-6-0-3-codex.md` (0 HIGH + 3 MED + 4 LOW + 6 INFO).  Opus transcript: `docs/audits/2026-05-23-phase-5-7-v3-6-0-3-opus.md` (1 HIGH + 3 MED + 4 LOW + 4 INFO).  3 convergent findings closed in-cycle: **CONVERGENT-HIGH-1** (Opus HIGH-1 ≡ Codex MED-3): cache walker LWW (`insert`) -> first-write-wins (`entry().or_insert`) mirroring `FormatTable::register_at`'s IdCollision rejection at the cache layer; closes the V3.6.0.1 plan body § D2 line 133 locked decision violation.  **CONVERGENT-MED-1** (Codex MED-1 ≡ Opus MED-2): `workbook_snapshot.formats` sorted by FormatId via the engine's derived Ord (Builtin variants first per enum order, then Custom lexicographically by `(peer, counter)`) before returning -- pre-closure was raw HashMap iter which varied across consecutive calls due to per-instance random hasher.  **CONVERGENT-MED-2** (Codex MED-2 ≡ Opus MED-1+MED-3): `collect_cache_effects` drops Builtin variant `Op::RegisterFormat` payloads at the cache walker (matches "ONLY Custom" docstring claim); Workbook-side `FormatTable::register_at` still accepts in-range Builtins as Phase 4.6 D-1 backward-compat (deferred V3.7+).  Codex INFO-1 REFUTED suspected undo-of-Op::RegisterFormat staleness bug empirically (Probe 1: non-cell-keyed ops trigger full-rebuild fallback via the V3.6.0.X audit-closure gate).  +5 ql-collab regression tests (Opus H.1 + H.2 + H.3 + H.5 + H.7).  Opus LOW-1 (CacheBuckets refactor) DEFERRED to V3.6.0.4 D3 ship.  Opus LOW-3 (Builtin 0..=163 docstring drift; ~20 actually preloaded) folded into 4-site docstring sweep.  Cumulative V3.6 cycle (through V3.6.0.X audit-of-D2): +9 ql-collab (115 -> 124); IDE mocha 350/350 unchanged (sort change is deterministic across existing shape tests).  Audit transcripts: 35 (was 33; +2 V3.6.0.X audit-of-D2 Codex + Opus).  Cumulative findings closed across Phase 5.7: 20+ HIGH + 53+ MEDIUM (was 19+ HIGH + 50+ MEDIUM).  Rule 4 arc terminus HELD at 6 (no new fields/variants/structs in audit-of-D2; behavior-only closures: `entry/or_insert` + `sort_by_key` + Builtin early-return).  ✅ **V3.6.0.4 D3 SHIPPED** at engine `119df9b3826` (2026-05-23).  Per-cell + per-sheet op-log index closes V3.5.0.6 R-V3.5-2 perf gap.  Engine surface: new `cell_op_index: HashMap<(u16,u32,u32), Vec<usize>>` + `sheet_op_index: HashMap<u16, Vec<usize>>` fields on CollabSession; new `CacheBuckets<'a>` struct bundling 5 mutable refs (closes Opus LOW-1 from V3.6.0.X audit-of-D2); new `OpLog::get(index)` accessor on ql-oplog (random-access lookup); `apply_cache_effect` signature refactored to `(&mut CacheBuckets<'_>, CacheEffect, op_log_index: usize)`; new `rebuild_op_indices_only()` helper called by undo+redo BEFORE the per-cell invalidate loop (necessary because Loro's UndoManager retract COMPACTS the visible op list and shifts positional indices -- design discovery during V3.6.0.4 implementation; documented as R-V3.6-10).  `invalidate_cell` rewritten to walk via `cell_op_index ∪ sheet_op_index` instead of full log walk: O(ops-for-this-cell) typical 1-3 + O(removes-for-this-sheet) typical 0-1 vs pre-D3 O(N).  `force_clear_snapshot_cache` clears the new indices; new `cell_op_index_iter` + `sheet_op_index_iter` accessors.  +6 ql-collab regression tests (130/130 pass; +6 over V3.6.0.X audit-of-D2 124 baseline).  Rule 4 arc terminus HELD at 6 (2 new HashMap fields + 1 struct with 5 ref fields; all positive Send+Sync via composition; 0 new triggers).  This session counted 3 plan-implement-audit cycles (V3.6.0.X audit-of-D2 + closures + V3.6.0.4 D3 ship), 1 over the CLAUDE.md ≤2 guideline; user-directed exception via AskUserQuestion.  ✅ **V3.6.0.X AUDIT-OF-D3 SHIPPED** at engine (this commit) (2026-05-23).  Parallel Codex Lane A + Opus Lane B audit of V3.6.0.4 D3 surface; both PASS-WITH-FINDINGS.  Codex transcript: `docs/audits/2026-05-23-phase-5-7-v3-6-0-4-codex.md` (0 HIGH + 2 MED + 4 LOW + 5 INFO).  Opus transcript: `docs/audits/2026-05-23-phase-5-7-v3-6-0-4-opus.md` (1 HIGH + 2 MED + 4 LOW + 3 INFO).  4 in-cycle closures: **CONVERGENT-HIGH-1** (Opus HIGH-1 / Codex LOW-2): `invalidate_cell` atomic-swap (build-into-fresh; defer `self.last_snapshot.remove(target_key)` until AFTER all fallible `OpLog::get` calls succeed).  Pre-closure the unconditional `remove()` at entry + fallible mid-walk Err produced a torn-write hazard.  **CONVERGENT-MED-2** (Codex MED-2 / Opus MED-1): `rebuild_op_indices_only` rewritten to use `apply_cache_effect` (canonical walker) with throwaway snapshot/format_cache buckets + local tombstones tracker; gives tombstone-aware index parity with `rebuild_snapshot_cache`.  Also added `cell_op_index.retain(|(sheet,_,_),_| *sheet != id)` to RemoveSheet handler (mirrors `snapshot.retain`; prunes ghost index entries for cells on tombstoned sheets).  **Codex MED-1**: `poll_remote_with_limit` partial-error rebuild -- track first drain error in the loop; if `merged > 0` before propagating, run `rebuild_snapshot_cache` to keep cache + indices consistent with the committed log state.  **Codex LOW-1**: `OpLog::get` docstring corrected from "O(1)" to "O(log N) BTree lookup" per Loro 1.12.0's internal `LengthFinder`-over-`generic_btree::BTree` implementation; invalidate_cell docstring updated to reflect the honest O(ops-for-this-cell * log N) bound.  ide-consumer-contract.md sweep: V3.6.0.4 D3 SHIPPED inline + R-V3.5-2 marked CLOSED.  +4 ql-collab regression tests (134/134 pass; +4 over V3.6.0.4 D3 130 baseline).  Codex INFO-3 + INFO-5 noted for V3.7+ (long-term stable-op-ID migration design; OpLog::append stores JSON-only payload + would need wire-format extension).  Rule 4 arc terminus HELD at 6 (no new fields/structs in audit-of-D3; behavior-only closures).  Cumulative V3.6 cycle: +19 ql-collab tests (115 -> 134); IDE mocha 350/350 unchanged; audit transcripts: 37 (was 35; +2 V3.6.0.4 Codex + Opus).  Cumulative findings closed across Phase 5.7: 21+ HIGH + 55+ MEDIUM (was 20+ HIGH + 53+ MEDIUM).  This session counted **5 plan-implement-audit cycles** (V3.6.0.X audit-of-D2 + closures + V3.6.0.4 D3 ship + V3.6.0.X audit-of-D3 + closures), 3 over CLAUDE.md ≤2 guideline; user-directed exception via AskUserQuestion + "Proceed next" directives.  ✅ **V3.6.0.5 D4 SHIPPED** at engine (this commit) + IDE (this commit) (2026-05-23).  Format-aware buildHtml rendering via engine-side `ql_functions::format::render`.  Engine napi: new `CellSnapshotJson.rendered: Option<String>` additive field (populated when cell has format + value: format::parse the format-string -> render(value, fmt, eval_context) where eval_context.date_system = workbook.date_system() + locale = EnUs + now_provider = System).  Silent fallback to `None` on: no format / no value / format-id lookup miss / format-string parse error / wire-decode error.  New `WorkbookSnapshotJson.dateSystem: String` additive field ("Excel1900" | "Excel1904"; mapped from `ql_types::DateSystem`).  IDE: `types.ts` interfaces extended (CellSnapshotJson.rendered?: string + WorkbookSnapshotJson.dateSystem union); QuantbookCellSnapshot.entries[*].rendered passthrough; `extractSheetSnapshot` conditional include (only when rendered defined -- preserves exact-shape tests); `cellGridHtml::renderRows` + client-side `renderRowsClient` use `e.rendered ?? formatCellValue(e.value)` (escapeHtml covers both paths; CSP-safe).  +4 mocha shape tests (354/354 pass; +4 over V3.6.0.X audit-of-D3 350 baseline).  ql-collab 134/134 unchanged (no engine collab-side changes).  Rule 4 arc terminus HELD at 6 (1 new String field + 1 new Option<String> field on existing napi structs; 0 new triggers).  **mocha-test scope limitation**: full format::render integration tests (Op::RegisterFormat + Op::SetCellFormat + Op::PutValue -> rendered output) are deferred to V3.6.0.X audit-of-D4 -- the IDE napi at V3.6.0.5 D4 has no appendSetCellFormat / appendRegisterFormat method, so end-to-end mocha can only pin SHAPE.  Engine-side Rust integration tests TBD at audit-of-D4 closure.  Cumulative V3.6 cycle: ql-collab 134/134 + mocha 350 -> 354; audit transcripts still 37.  This session counted **6 plan-implement-audit cycles** (V3.6.0.X audit-of-D2 + closures + V3.6.0.4 D3 ship + V3.6.0.X audit-of-D3 + closures + V3.6.0.5 D4 ship), 4 over CLAUDE.md ≤2 guideline; user-directed exception via repeated "Proceed next" + "Ship D4 fully this session" AskUserQuestion answer.  ✅ **V3.6.0.X AUDIT-OF-D4 SHIPPED** at engine (this commit) + IDE (this commit) (2026-05-24).  Most serious audit verdict in V3.6 cycle: Codex Lane A FAIL (1 HIGH + 2 MED + 3 LOW + 4 INFO) + Opus Lane B FAIL (3 HIGH + 3 MED + 4 LOW + 3 INFO).  Transcripts: `docs/audits/2026-05-24-phase-5-7-v3-6-0-5-codex.md` + `docs/audits/2026-05-24-phase-5-7-v3-6-0-5-opus.md`.  Convergent + in-cycle closures: **CONVERGENT-HIGH-1** (both lanes empirically probed): new `Op::SetDateSystem` wire variant + `DateSystemWire` enum (mirrors LocaleWire pattern) + replay handler + `from_qbook` seeds the op when loaded workbook's date_system != default.  Pre-closure Excel1904 workbooks rendered with Excel1900 epoch (1462-day off-by-one).  R-V3.6-11 documented.  **OPUS-HIGH-2** (Codex missed): new IDE `data-raw-value` attribute carries parseable raw representation for click-to-edit; `beginEdit` reads it first (falls back to `data-original-text` for backward compat).  Pre-closure `parseCellRawInput` NaN'd on currency/percent/thousands/date format-rendered strings, breaking every formatted-cell edit.  R-V3.6-12 documented.  **CONVERGENT-HIGH-3** (Opus HIGH-3 / Codex MED-1): short-circuit pre-render when `wire_value.is_pending()`; preserves IDE "(pending)" fallback.  Pre-closure pending+format displayed as formatted zero (Value::Blank routed as 0.0).  R-V3.6-13 documented.  **CONVERGENT-MED-1**: thread `workbook.locale()` through EvalContext (prevents silent forward-compat regression at V3.6.1+).  **CONVERGENT-MED-2**: per-snapshot parsed-format cache (HashMap<FormatId, FormatString>; reuses parse result across cells sharing FormatId).  **CONVERGENT-MED-3**: ide-consumer-contract.md sweep (R-V3.5-4 marked CLOSED; D4 "deferred" updated to SHIPPED).  **OPUS-LOW-2 + LOW-3**: dropped `.to_string()` on lookup result + TS docstring `date_system` -> `dateSystem`.  +2 ql-collab regression tests (Op::SetDateSystem replay + unknown-wire error).  Rule 4 arc terminus HELD at 6 (new DateSystemWire enum + Op::SetDateSystem variant; both Send+Sync via primitive composition; 0 new triggers).  Cumulative V3.6 cycle: ql-collab 134 -> 136; IDE mocha 354/354 unchanged; audit transcripts: 39 (was 37; +2 V3.6.0.5 Codex + Opus).  Cumulative findings closed across Phase 5.7: 24+ HIGH + 58+ MEDIUM (was 21+ HIGH + 55+ MEDIUM).  This session counted **8 plan-implement-audit cycles** (audit-of-D2 + closures + D3 + audit-of-D3 + closures + D4 + audit-of-D4 + closures), 6 over CLAUDE.md ≤2 guideline; user-directed exception throughout via "Proceed next" chain + AskUserQuestion "Close all in-cycle".  **V3.6.0.6 D5 IDE-facing appendPutFormula napi** (Opus § F.5, ~1 session) is the next recommended sub-step.  Baselines tracked: ql-collab **136/136** + IDE mocha **354/354** + ql-collab-ws 40/40 + engine workspace all 30 suites pass.  ✅ **V3.6.0.6 D5 SHIPPED** at engine (this commit) + IDE (this commit) (2026-05-24).  Engine napi: new `CollabSession::appendPutFormula(sheet: u16, row: f64, col: f64, text: String) -> Result<()>` mirroring `appendPutValue` validation discipline (validate_u32_index on row/col + sheet u16 at FFI boundary); wraps existing `Op::PutFormula { sheet, row, col, text }` (shipping since Phase 4.6.x); no new wire variant; no new CacheEffect (the cell-keyed cache walker already handles PutFormula via `CacheEffect::Cell`).  IDE: `types.ts` adds `CollabSessionInstance.appendPutFormula(...)` + `QuantbookCellSnapshot.entries[*].formula?: string`; `session.ts` adds `appendPutFormulaValidated(session, sheet, row, col, text)` typed wrapper (validates sheet/row/col BEFORE the FFI ToUint32-coercion boundary; matches `appendPutValueValidated` pattern; text not validated since wire accepts any string); `extractSheetSnapshot` passes through `cell.formula` (additive; conditional-key discipline like `rendered` preserves V3.5.0.4b shape-stability tests); `cellGridHtml::renderRows` server-side emits `data-raw-formula="${escapeHtml(e.formula)}"` when entry has formula text; client-side `renderRowsClient` mirrors; **`beginEdit` precedence chain updated to `data-raw-formula > data-raw-value > data-original-text`** (extends V3.6.0.X audit-of-D4 OPUS-HIGH-2 § G.2 -- cells with both formula AND value have two raw representations; formula is the more-authoritative source for editing since it's what the user typed).  +19 mocha tests (354 -> **373**): 6 appendPutFormulaValidated input validation (negative sheet, sheet>u16, fractional row, oversize col, non-string text, accepts valid); 4 engine napi (opCount, fractional row reject, negative row reject, out-of-u32 col reject); 3 workbookSnapshot surface (formula-only cell -> formula property; rename-chain repair end-to-end; round-trip via to_qbook/from_qbook); 2 extractSheetSnapshot (formula+value pass-through; formula-absent shape stability); 4 buildHtml emit (with-formula attribute, without-formula td scope check, HTML-escape XSS, beginEdit precedence chain).  **V3.5.0.X A-HIGH-2 IDE-level verification gap CLOSED end-to-end** (engine-side Rust regression already verified the repair; now IDE-driven mocha verifies the rename-chain repair surfaces through napi `workbookSnapshot`).  Tests: ql-collab **136/136** unchanged (no engine collab-side changes); ql-oplog **67/67** unchanged; ql-collab-ws **42/42** unchanged (30 lib + 10 transport + 2 doctests); engine workspace **99 test-result lines pass**; IDE mocha **373/373** (+19 V3.6.0.6 D5 over V3.6.0.X audit-of-D4 354 baseline).  Rule 4 arc terminus HELD at 6 (napi method only; no new structs/fields/variants; 0 new triggers).  This session counted **1 plan-implement-audit cycle** (V3.6.0.6 D5 ship), WITHIN the CLAUDE.md ≤2 cycle guideline -- recovery from the V3.6.0.5 D4 / audit-of-D4 / docs-audit session's 9+ cycle bloat.
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:675:   🚧 **V3.4 (undo + persistence + presence, 0.1-0.5 + 0.4a/b + 0.7 SHIPPED 2026-05-23)** -- 8 V3.4.0 sub-steps shipped; only 0.X audit remains.  Five locked D-decisions per V3.3.0.X Opus § V3.4 ENTRY READINESS: **D1 hybrid CellState cache** (unified `CellState{value, formula, ...}` for cell-keyed ops; non-cell ops stay on Workbook state); **D2 full-rebuild undo invalidation** (carries V3.3.0.X HIGH-1; partial-invalidate deferred to V3.5+); **D3 envelope-level persistence versioning** (V3.4.0.4a reuses existing v2 `workbook.toml.schema_version` from Phase 2A.8; no bump needed); **D4 boolean-flag race guard** (extends V3.3.0.4 `activeInput` pattern; R-V3.4-3 deferred at V3.4.0.5b implementation -- full HTML rebuild on every pollRemote merged tick handles regeneration); **D5 UUID-derived PeerId** -- **DEVIATED at V3.4.0.4b**: original lock specified persisted-per-workbook PeerId via envelope v3 / config file; implementation discovery showed two-windows-same-workspace collision; resolution is fresh-UUID-per-session via `crypto.randomUUID()` truncated to 64-bit BigInt, which is CRDT-correct + closes R-V3.3-5 fully (UUID 2^64 keyspace vs PID ~2^15 effective).  Cross-restart op-attribution continuity deferred to V3.4.1+ if user-facing feature surfaces.  Sub-steps shipped: 0.1 decision lock (engine `a87c31eed4f`); 0.2 hybrid CellState cache + 3 new ql-collab tests (engine `1ae59a1a1aa`); 0.3 undo/redo napi + Cmd-Z wiring + 13 mocha (engine `7d63ff53132` + IDE `673792af05f`); 0.4a engine .qbook napi (toQbook/fromQbook + `addSheet` REAL SEMANTIC GAP closure + 3 new napi-crate deps ql-io/ql-functions/ql-storage + persistence_error_to_napi + 5 mocha; engine `bef220d7d3c` + IDE `ec9b59db8a5`); 0.4b IDE Save As/Open + generateUuidPeerId + 4 mocha (engine `a1e2c673381` plan-only + IDE `fa7ec198cee`); 0.5a presence napi (5 wrappers + PresenceStateJson struct + 9 mocha; engine `5ce55f65739` + IDE `8ff2d81f1e4`); 0.5b IDE cell-grid presence integration (cell-grid-presence data block + .cell-peer-presence decoration + presenceUpdate envelope + R-V3.4-7 VOIDED + R-V3.4-3 DEFERRED + 16 mocha; engine `cd26a37b513` plan-only + IDE `1744cee11af`).  +47 cumulative V3.4-specific mocha tests (181 -> 228) + 3 new ql-collab tests (76 -> 79).  Rule 4 arc terminus held at 6 throughout (V3.4 surface adds one new Rust struct `PresenceStateJson` -- composition of u16/u32/bool primitives; trivially Send+Sync; 0 new triggers).  **0.6 mocha is EFFECTIVELY COMPLETE** via incremental per-sub-step coverage (47 V3.4-tests vs the plan's "~15 new" target).  **0.7 docs SHIPPED** at engine `fe10a245d07` (ide-consumer-contract.md § 4.1.z4 insertion; ~460 lines / file 837 -> 1280; covers full V3.4 napi surface + CellState cache + undo/redo + .qbook persistence + D5 DEVIATION + presence + 6 drift hazards + risk register R-V3.4-1..6 post-implementation reality + 12 out-of-scope items + steps 7-11 live smoke procedure extending V3.3.0.6).  Remaining: **0.X parallel Codex+Opus megaudit** (~4-6h cycle; sweeps V3.4.0.1-7 cumulatively).
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:712:**✅ 6.1A + 6.1B inc.1/1b + inc.2a/2b/2c-1/2c-2 SHIPPED 2026-05-26.** Contract: `docs/api/session-api.md` v2 (API6-01/02/03; Codex gpt-5.5 xhigh REVISE → all 13 findings resolved; review `docs/api/codex-6-1a-review.md`). Contract crate: `ql-session` (`38108a5c8ef`) — complete type-level `EngineSession` trait + DTOs + EngineError + operation/lifecycle + table ops. **Owning `WorkbookSession` SHIPPED** in `crates/ql-exec/src/session.rs` `impl EngineSession` (`83b1b33bac2` PlanCache → `7335a5a1bfa` core → `993492b6f9b` validate_formula/query_range/`CellValue::Blank` → `2b5e7a13f5b` structure+table ops → `9f7a1645dbd` tombstone-read-consistency audit fix) — REAL: lifecycle + `{epoch,op_count}` 24-byte version token + single-cell mutations + add/rename/**delete/restore/move** sheet (fail-loud) + set_name + **table ops** (create/rename/rename_column/resize/drop) + recalc (Busy/op-registry, CellDiagnostic events) + read (snapshot/cell/list_sheets/query_range/validate_formula; tombstoned sheet = uniformly NotFound) + cancel/operation_status/poll_events; error mapping via free fns (orphan rules forbid `From<RuntimeError> for EngineError`). 17 session tests + 653 ql-exec lib green, clippy clean. Remaining trait methods surfaced `Capability/not_implemented_in_v1_core` (No-Fallbacks). Doc fix: ql-oplog::OpLog DOES expose a Loro VV (`oplog_vv`) — earlier "no VV" claim corrected; `{epoch,op_count}` is the deliberate v1 token. NEXT = 6.1B inc.2c-3 (snapshot_delta) → batch/txn/undo/redo/persistence → functions/bulk → Node smoke migration → 6.1C audit. **(Superseded — inc.2c-3 through inc.2c-8 all SHIPPED 2026-05-27; current NEXT = persistence; see the inc.2c-8 entry below + `docs/api/workbook-session-impl-plan.md` §0.)**
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:714:**✅ 6.1B inc.2 AUDIT (F3–F10) + inc.2c-3 snapshot_delta SHIPPED 2026-05-27.** Parallel Codex (gpt-5.5 xhigh) + Opus audit of `WorkbookSession` (synthesis `docs/audits/2026-05-27-inc2-session-audit/SYNTHESIS.md`; 10 distinct findings, all verified at source). **Audit-fix `879f3601747`**: F3 `with_runtime` FaultGuard (panic→Faulted, the in-engine half of the §8 boundary); F4 read-path coord bounds (query_range/cell/validate_formula → BadArgument, closes a u32 overflow); F5 tombstone op-log fidelity (double-delete = true no-op; restore-of-live = Conflict); F6 `require_live_sheet` on rename_sheet + create_table; F7 query_range include-options fail-loud (Capability); F8 Appendix-A honest mapping; F9 deleted-sheets-formula-readable doc; F10 corrected misleading tables.rs atomicity comment (the BatchCommit fix is TRACKED — pre-existing, near-zero reachability). **inc.2c-3 `20427b1c4c7`**: `snapshot_delta` via design (a) — a session change-log keyed by a monotonic **`state_seq`** that REPLACES `oplog.len()` as the token counter (advances on every committed mutation AND every recompute-with-changes + Blank-clear, so distinct states never share a token; closes Codex HIGH F1+F2-token-half). `RecomputeResult` gained `changed_cells`. §4.3 rules + fail-loud `invalid_version_token`; epoch-bump for delta-inexpressible states (move/restore sheet, table ops). **ql-exec lib 667/0, clippy clean, workspace `cargo check` green.** NEXT = batch/txn → undo/redo → persistence → functions/bulk → Node smoke → 6.1C audit. **(Superseded — see the inc.2c-8 entry below for current NEXT = persistence.)**
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:720:**✅ 6.1B inc.2c-6 — F2 Blank-durability gap CLOSED (`Op::ClearValue`) SHIPPED 2026-05-27** (`d8d22a04248`). `set_value(Blank)` on a value-only cell previously appended NO op (`CellWireValue::from_value(Blank)==None`) → the clear was invisible to the op-log and lost on replay/save-load (a cell `5` then Blank-cleared replayed back to `5`). New additive `Op::ClearValue { sheet, row, col }` replays to `Workbook::put_at(.., Value::Blank)`; every value-clear path now logs it (`WorkbookRuntime::set_value`, `WorkbookSession::batch`, `WorkbookTransaction::commit`). `clear_formula` deliberately unchanged (preserves values — Excel convert-to-literal). ql-collab gains `CacheEffect::ClearValue` (mirrors ClearFormula); bindings `classify_delta_op` routes it cell-keyed. `OPLOG_SCHEMA_VERSION` NOT bumped (additive variant). Prerequisite for correct undo. Delegated-agent impl, reviewed at source + independently verified; ql-exec 692/0, ql-oplog/ql-collab green.
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:722:**✅ 6.1B inc.2c-7 — undo/redo SHIPPED 2026-05-27** (`4f8e9858d77`). `undo`/`redo`/`can_undo`/`can_redo` via a long-lived `loro::UndoManager` field (built in `from_workbook`, `set_merge_interval(0)` → 1 Loro commit = 1 undo unit; every command emits exactly one commit except `rename_table`/`rename_column` which are wrapped in a `grouped()` Loro undo group — the F10 PutFormula loop). `rematerialize` after a Loro undo/redo: replay the (compacted) op-log onto a CLONE of the construction-time **baseline workbook** → `rebuild_from_workbook` → `recompute_all` with the op-log DETACHED → `bump_epoch` (outstanding `snapshot_delta` token → EpochMismatch full rebuild). Empty stack → `consumed:false`. Builds on inc.2c-6: undo of a Blank-clear restores the prior value. **Parallel Codex+Opus audit:** both verified the two load-bearing claims at source (1-command-1-undo-unit; linear-replay rename fidelity needs no ql-collab repair passes); both flagged ONE real bug — a populated-`from_workbook` session + undo silently dropped pre-loaded content (replayed from an empty workbook) — **FIXED via the `baseline: Workbook` field** (Codex HIGH / Opus M1). F10 table-rename append-atomicity was left tracked at this point, then CLOSED in its own increment inc.2c-8 (`dca5695549e`) — NOT folded into persistence; 100-step undo cap documented. Synthesis `docs/audits/2026-05-27-inc2c67-undo-audit/SYNTHESIS.md`. **ql-exec lib 709/0, clippy clean, workspace build green.** (superseded NEXT — see inc.2c-8 below.)
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:730:**✅ 6.1B inc.2c-11 — csv `import`/`export` SHIPPED 2026-05-27.** `WorkbookSession::import("csv")` + `export("csv")` are live. **New pure-I/O leaf crate `ql-io-csv`** (deps: `csv = "=1.3.1"` + `ql-storage` + `ql-types` + `thiserror` — deliberately NOT `ql-exec`; CSV has no formulas → no recompute injection, unlike the inc.2c-10 xlsx path, so it stays a true leaf with no cycle risk). Public surface: `import_csv_bytes(bytes, CsvImportOptions) -> Result<CsvImportResult{workbook, report}, CsvError>` + `export_csv_bytes(workbook, sheet_id, CsvExportOptions) -> Result<Vec<u8>, CsvError>` + `CsvError` (`#[non_exhaustive]`: Io/Parse/ExceedsSheetLimits/SheetNotFound). RFC 4180 via BurntSushi's `csv` crate (quoting/embedded-newlines) rather than a hand-rolled splitter. **Import:** `has_headers(false)` (row 0 is data), leading UTF-8 BOM stripped, UTF-8-strict (non-UTF-8 → loud `csv_parse`), type inference (empty→Blank skipped; `TRUE`/`FALSE`→Boolean; finite f64→Number, `inf`/`nan`→text; leading `=`→**text**, injection-safe; Excel-like lossy numeric coercion `00123`→123 documented), engine-row/col-limit guarded BEFORE `put_at` (never panics) → **Option-1 adoption** (`*self = from_workbook`, registry preserved, epoch re-minted; **NO recompute** — no formulas). **Export (`&self`):** single LIVE sheet only (`sheet_display_order` minus `is_sheet_removed`; 0→empty bytes, 1→serialise, >1→loud `BadArgument` — refuse rather than silently drop sheets, since `&self` has no warn channel); verbatim/value-only (cells via `ql_types::Value` `Display`; no formula-trigger escaping; uses the conservative `Sheet::bounds` used-range like the xlsx exporter + `.qbook` saver). `unknown` import/export format → loud `BadArgument`. New `map_csv_err` fills Appendix A (Io/Parse→Persistence `csv_io`/`csv_parse`; ExceedsSheetLimits→BadArgument `csv_exceeds_limits`; SheetNotFound→Internal `csv_sheet_not_found`; foreign `#[non_exhaustive]` wildcard → loud `unmapped_csv_error`). **Parallel Codex(gpt-5.5 xhigh)+Opus audit, every finding verified at source:** Codex **HIGH** (export over conservative `Sheet::bounds`, which `Sheet::put` grows even on a `Blank` write → a blank-inflated workbook could emit a giant rectangle) **assessed consistent-with-siblings + documented + tracked**: the IDENTICAL `for row in 0..bounds.row_extent` pattern is in the xlsx exporter (`umya_export.rs:424`) AND the `.qbook` saver (`qbook_format.rs:1422`), both shipped through prior audits — a CSV-only divergent fix would be worse engineering; the correct fix is a uniform storage-level effective-non-blank-value-extent API adopted by all three serializers (TRACKED cross-cutting follow-up; the common round-trip path is unaffected — import skips blanks). Codex MEDIUM (export doesn't escape formula-triggers) → kept **faithful/verbatim** export (silent `'`-prefixing would corrupt data + break round-trip + violate No-Fallbacks; matches Excel/Sheets export), doc claim scoped to import + future opt-in sanitiser noted. Opus INFO (leading UTF-8 BOM not stripped → corrupts cell (0,0)) **FIXED** + test. Codex LOW (numeric lexical fidelity) kept Excel-consistent + pinned with a test. Both confirmed: limit guards correct/no-panic, import adoption atomic-on-failure, no-recompute safe, multi-sheet refusal correct, `ql-io-csv` a genuine leaf, `map_csv_err` exhaustive. Synthesis `docs/audits/2026-05-27-inc2c11-csv-audit/`. **ql-exec lib 728/0 + e2e 21/0, clippy clean; ql-io-csv 11/0; ql-io-xlsx green; workspace build green.** **(Superseded — inc.2c-12 below SHIPPED `export("xlsx")` + the xlsx-writer feature-gate; current NEXT = functions 6.4-0/6.4.)**
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:732:**✅ 6.1B inc.2c-12 — xlsx `export` + xlsx-writer feature-gate SHIPPED 2026-05-27.** `WorkbookSession::export("xlsx")` is live (whole-workbook — xlsx is multi-sheet, unlike the single-sheet csv export), AND the tracked inc.2c-10 follow-up (ql-exec pulling the xlsx WRITER's heavy umya-spreadsheet + image/rav1e/exr/tiff codec tree for import-only use) is CLOSED. **In-memory writer (no tempfile):** umya 2.2.0 exposes `writer::xlsx::write_writer<W: io::Write>`, so a new `ql_io_xlsx::export_xlsx_bytes(workbook, registry, XlsxExportOptions) -> Result<(Vec<u8>, XlsxExportReport), XlsxError>` serialises straight into a `Vec<u8>`; the path exporter (`export_xlsx_path`/`export_new_workbook`) now delegates to a shared `export_new_workbook_to_bytes` core + one `atomic_write_to_path`, and `post_process_zip(path,…)` became the bytes-in/bytes-out `post_process_bytes(Vec<u8>,…)` — output is byte-identical (umya's path `write` and `write_writer` both go through `make_buffer`, verified at the registry source). `export_xlsx_bytes` is `NewWorkbook`-only (UpdateOriginal → loud `XlsxError::Export`, no silent downgrade); Strict drop-feature check kept (no file to remove). **Feature-gate:** ql-io-xlsx `umya-spreadsheet` is now `optional`; `[features] default = ["write"]`, `write = ["dep:umya-spreadsheet"]` gates `mod write` + `export_xlsx_path` + `export_xlsx_bytes`; the READER (calamine/zip/quick-xml + `import_xlsx_*` + `XlsxRecomputer`) is always compiled. `ql-exec` depends `default-features = false` (reader only) + `[features] xlsx-write = ["ql-io-xlsx/write"]`; `export("xlsx")` is real behind `#[cfg(feature = "xlsx-write")]`, else honest `Capability/not_implemented_in_v1_core` (No-Fallbacks — the writer's codec tree is opt-in, keeping the default ql-exec build + WASM/bindings lean). A `ql-exec` `[dev-dependencies]` re-enables `write` so the inc.2c-10 import round-trip test fixture (which calls `export_xlsx_path`) still compiles; workspace `resolver = "2"` keeps that dev-dep `write` out of the normal lib build. `export` is `&self` (no event channel), so the export report's fidelity caveats are dropped under the default Permissive policy — the same `&self` no-warning-channel limitation as csv export (documented). `export("xlsx")` errors route through the existing `map_xlsx_err` (Appendix A unchanged). **Parallel Codex(gpt-5.5 xhigh)+Opus audit: CLEAN — 0 HIGH/MED/LOW** (both verified the `write_writer ≡ write` byte-equivalence at the umya registry source + the feature graph via read-only `cargo tree`: umya absent from default ql-exec normal deps, present under `--features xlsx-write`; 1 doc-precision INFO applied; 1 pre-existing HashMap-ordered fresh-rels INFO folded into the cross-cutting tracker). Synthesis `docs/audits/2026-05-27-inc2c12-xlsx-export-audit/`. **ql-exec lib 729/0 (default + `--features xlsx-write`), clippy clean; ql-io-xlsx 60+49/0 (default), `--no-default-features` builds clean; workspace build green.** **NEXT = functions (6.4-0 metadata substrate then 6.4) + reserved bulk → Node smoke migration (+ `.node` rebuild + B#1/S2-01 mocha) → 6.1C security audit → 6.4 Python UDFs. Plus tracked cross-cutting: a storage-level effective-non-blank-value extent API for all serializers (csv/xlsx/.qbook).** **(Superseded — inc.2d below SHIPPED the engine-side Node-smoke enabler; the prior "functions-first" NEXT was reconciled to the canonical decision-lock §2: IDE-side Node smoke + mocha → 6.1C → 6.4-0 → 6.4.)**
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:734:**✅ 6.1B inc.2d — owning `WorkbookSession` over napi (engine-side Node-smoke enabler) SHIPPED 2026-05-28.** The Node binding `ql-bindings-node` now exposes the product-neutral owning session over FFI as a new **`Session`** `#[napi]` class wrapping `Arc<parking_lot::Mutex<ql_exec::WorkbookSession>>` — `new`/`addSheet`/`setValue`/`setFormula`/`clear`/`recalcDirty`/`recalcAll`/`snapshot`/`cell`/`listSheets`. This is decision-lock §2 item 3 ("migrate the Node smoke path onto the owning session") + risk-mitigation #1 ("migrate the Node path early to catch missing commands"). It does NOT touch the existing `CollabSession` CRDT façade (collab = v1.5). New `engine_error_to_napi` (mirrors `collab_session_error_to_napi`; `EngineError::Display = "[code] message"`) + free-fn DTO mappers reusing the existing `#[napi(object)]` shapes (`CellValueJson`/`CellSnapshotJson`/`SheetSnapshotJson`/`WorkbookSnapshotJson`/`FormatIdJson`/`FormatDefJson`) + a new `SheetInfoJson`; all index args are `f64`+`validate_u16/u32_index` (no JS `ToUint32` silent coercion); a positive `const _ASSERT_BINDING_SESSION_SEND` compile-proof confirms `WorkbookSession: Send` (so `Arc<Mutex<…>>` is `Send+Sync` — the owning session IS FFI-shareable, no contract finding). Deps added: `ql-exec` (NO default features → does NOT pull the umya xlsx-writer/image-codec tree) + `ql-session`. A plain-Node `process.dlopen` smoke (`crates/ql-bindings-node/tests/smoke_session.mjs`) PASSES edit→recalc→snapshot (B1==11), clear-preserves-value, setValue(blank)-clears, unknown-kind→`[bad_argument]`. **Parallel Codex(gpt-5.5 xhigh)+Opus audit: SHIP — 0 HIGH/MED**; 1 LOW (clear docstring overstated "value+formula" → FIXED to convert-to-literal) + deferred items (snapshot `formats` ordering non-deterministic at the `WorkbookSession::snapshot` source → 6.1C; `WorkbookSnapshotJson` omits `schema_version` → 6.3; no `catch_unwind` under `panic=abort`, identical to CollabSession → known). Synthesis `docs/audits/2026-05-28-inc2d-session-napi-audit/`. **Build green: `cargo build -p ql-bindings-node` (default; `--features test-fixtures` checks), `cargo check --workspace`; inc.2d code clippy-clean.** **⚠️ Pre-existing clippy debt surfaced (NOT this increment): `cargo clippy -p ql-bindings-node` is RED at HEAD (it has `#![deny(clippy::all)]`) due to the `rust-1.95.0` clippy bump — 4 deny-errors in pre-existing CollabSession-path code (`lib.rs:416/502/564/2788`) + workspace-wide warn-level `doc_lazy_continuation`/`type_complexity` (ql-storage/ql-oplog/ql-collab); needs a focused hygiene pass.** **NEXT (canonical decision-lock §2): IDE-side Node smoke wiring + mocha (drive `Session` through `loader.ts`, rebuild the `.node`, add B#1/S2-01 cross-window tests) — cross-repo (`feat/visualise-v1`) → 6.1C security/design audit → 6.4-0 function-metadata substrate → 6.4 Python UDFs. Plus the tracked serializer effective-extent API.** **(Superseded — the IDE Node migration below SHIPPED; current NEXT = 6.1C.)**
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:738:**✅ 6.1C — Security/Design Audit SHIPPED 2026-05-28 (5-way parallel megaudit).** The mandatory audit before broader binding/service exposure (decision-lock §2 item 4) is complete — the Phase-6 exit-packet artifact lands at `docs/audits/2026-05-28-6-1c-megaudit/SYNTHESIS.md`. **Method:** 4 Codex (gpt-5.5 xhigh, `read-only`) lanes + 1 Opus agent + Opus synthesis (this 5-way pattern previously caught 22 HIGHs invisible per-batch at Phase 4.11+4.12 closure). Scope ≈9859 LoC: owning `WorkbookSession` (`session.rs` 5117) + `Session` napi class (`lib.rs:4276-4426` ~150) + the `ql-session` contract (~316) + the IDE TS consumer + shared `#[napi(object)]` DTOs. Lane briefs + orchestration committed at `c9297dff8ab` under `docs/phase6/6-1c-prep/`. **Verdict: SHIP-WITH-FIXES** — 3 HIGH (one fixed in audit-fix, two filed for 6.3 entry), 8 MED (two fixed in audit-fix, six filed for 6.3), 8 LOW + 6 INFO. **Foundation structurally sound:** Send/Sync compile-proven (audit rule 4); index validation exhaustive; error mapping consistent; lock discipline correct; lifecycle gates correct; `.qbook` open per-op `iter()` validation intact; F2/F10/undo all verified. **Audit-fix `6a14bd9075a`:** (1) **H2 deterministic ordering** — `snapshot.formats` + 5 `snapshot_delta` Vecs (`changed_cells`/`removed_cells`/`sheets_changed`/`sheets_removed`/`formats_added`) sorted by natural key, with `Ord`/`PartialOrd` added to `ql_session::FormatId` (additive trait, matches `ql_storage::FormatId`'s variant/field order so the wire-observable ordering is identical regardless of which side sorts); (2) **M8 `Session.close()`** bound over napi (5-line wrapper + a positive `[invalid_state]` smoke); (3) **M3 FaultGuard defense-in-depth** — lifted `FaultGuard` to module scope (eliminated the two inline duplicates in `with_runtime`/`with_runtime_no_oplog`) and wrapped `delete_sheet`/`restore_sheet`/`move_sheet`/`mark_volatiles_dirty` + `batch`'s Phase-2 op-log append so a panic mid-append/mutate seals →Faulted instead of leaving `state=Ready` with a torn op-log; (4) **L1 / seed input #5 closed** — `EngineSession::clear` trait doc tightened to "convert-to-literal; for delete-contents call `set_value(.., Blank)`" (verified at `cells.rs::set_value` Blank arm: emits `ClearValue + ClearFormula` atomically when a formula was present; the gap was docs-only, NO need for a separate `delete_cell` command); (5) **A-INFO/L-E6** — corrected the misleading `session.rs:332` docstring (Cargo default is `unwind`, NOT `abort`; the operational panic→host-abort is via napi-derive's no-`catch_unwind`-by-default behavior, which `#[napi(catch_unwind)]` would fix — tracked 6.3 M1); (6) **M6 partial** — `next_op_id` uses `checked_add` matching `next_txn_id`. **Tracked for 6.3-entry (block-on-6.3):** H1 (cross-repo IDE `parseQuantbookError` allowlist covers ~15 codes, engine `Session` emits ~40 — IDE-side commit on `feat/visualise-v1`), H3 (`snapshot_delta` under-reports spill changes — touches `WorkbookRuntime` return signature, too invasive for the audit-fix cycle; binding `snapshot_delta` over napi must wait for the engine fix). **Filed for 6.3:** M1 (`#[napi(catch_unwind)]` boundary), M2 (recalc cancel honesty — `run_recalc` allocates the op-id internally and never checks the registry, so even "pre-start cancel" is non-functional in v1), M5 (`schema_version` dropped at napi DTO boundary), M6 (events/ops bounded retention; needs event-ring infrastructure per contract §9), M7 (storage-level effective-non-blank-value extent cross-cutting). **Over-napi cut-line decision:** at 6.1C `Session` binds 11 methods (the existing 10 + `close`). `snapshotDelta`/`undo`/`redo`/`import`/`export`/`open`/`save`/`validateFormula`/`pollEvents`/`lifecycleState`/`operationStatus`/`cancel` all DEFER to 6.3; table/transaction/batch defer to 6.3; `register_function`/`unregister_function`/`list_functions` defer to 6.4 (function-metadata substrate prerequisite). Cycle-budget discipline (≤2 plan-implement-audit cycles per session) — megaudit cycle 1, audit-fix cycle 2, doc-sync separate. **Verification (focused re-verify of affected lanes):** `cargo build -p ql-exec -p ql-session -p ql-bindings-node` clean; `cargo test -p ql-exec --lib` 732/0 default + `--features xlsx-write` (+3 new H2 tests vs the 729 baseline); `cargo clippy -p ql-exec -p ql-session -p ql-bindings-node --all-targets` clean for edits; `node crates/ql-bindings-node/tests/smoke_session.mjs` PASS including the new post-close `[invalid_state]` + idempotent re-close assertions. **NEXT (canonical decision-lock §2 item 5): 6.4-0 function-metadata substrate** (replace the hardcoded `is_volatile_function` + `is_address_only_reference_fn` whitelists at `calcgraph_session.rs:149-164/:201-203` with first-class per-function metadata + `functions_used` reverse index → unblocks UDFs not bypassing the graph). Then 6.4 Python UDFs.
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:744:**✅ 6.4-0 — Function-metadata substrate SHIPPED 2026-05-28 (parallel 2-way audit).** Decision-lock §2 item 5; the prerequisite for 6.4 Python UDFs and for contract §10.3 registration-invalidation. Replaces the two hardcoded whitelists in `ql-exec::calcgraph_session` (`is_volatile_function` `:149-164`, `is_address_only_reference_fn` `:201-203`) with first-class `FunctionMetadata` stored on `FunctionRegistry`, and adds a `functions_used: HashMap<Arc<str>, HashSet<NodeId>>` reverse index on `CalcgraphSession` + two hooks `on_function_registered` / `on_function_unregistered`. **LAST CODE commits:** `63592126afe` (audit-fix; H2 production registry threading + 5 new substrate tests + 3 polish items) ← `ac20a432c63` (substrate; +1071/-117 across 8 files). **Substrate in 4 phases (each cleanly green):** (1) `ql-functions::FunctionRegistry` gains `metadata: HashMap<String, FunctionMetadata>` field + 5 public methods (`metadata` / `register_metadata` / `unregister_metadata` / `iter_metadata` / `metadata_count`) + a `FunctionRegistryError` enum (Conflict / NotFound); `default_registry()` runs a new `register_builtin_metadata` pass (Phase 1 explicit overrides match the prior whitelists byte-for-byte: NOW/TODAY/RAND/RANDBETWEEN/RANDARRAY → `Volatility::Volatile`; INDIRECT/OFFSET/INFO/CELL → `Volatility::Dynamic`; ROW/COLUMN/ROWS/COLUMNS/ISREF → `DepShape::AddressOnly`; Phase 2 defaults for every other dispatched builtin via `r.fns.keys()`); boot-time `assert!`-driven migration-shim invariant ("every dispatched fn has metadata"); `ql-functions` gains a one-way dep on `ql-session` (no cycle). (2) `FormulaDeps` gains `pub functions_used: Vec<Arc<str>>`; walker pushes at the TOP of the `ExprPlan::Function` arm BEFORE any routing decision, so ROW / ISREF / nested-fn paths all participate uniformly. (3) Walker signature `walk_plan_for_deps(plan, deps, registry)` + `walk_plan_for_address_only_deps` parallel; `is_volatile_function(registry, name)` reads `metadata.volatility ∈ {Volatile, Dynamic}` (migration-preserving); `is_address_only_reference_fn(registry, name)` reads `metadata.dep_shape == AddressOnly`; `rebuild_from_workbook(wb)` keeps its zero-arg public signature (constructs `default_registry()` internally) + new `rebuild_from_workbook_with_registry(wb, registry)` for production callers that own a session-scoped registry; 4 production call sites in `workbook_runtime/{cells, recompute, tables}.rs` thread `self.registry`; 53 test sites sed-batched. (4) `CalcgraphSession.functions_used` reverse-index field mirrors `name_to_formulas` pattern (populate at `extract_and_register_deps` after dedupe, cleanup at `remove_formula_deps`); storage gate widened from `!deps.is_empty() || deps.is_volatile` to also include `!deps.functions_used.is_empty() || !deps.names.is_empty() || !deps.tables.is_empty()` — closes a latent `ROW(MyName)` cleanup bug where the address-only walker's `names` push (without `named_ranges`) caused `name_to_formulas[MYNAME]` to leak on rebind; two new hooks return the dirtied-count, mirror `on_set_name`'s transitive BFS-fanout (Phase 3.10 H2 semantics) via `mark_dirty_from_cell_write`, bump new `HookCounts.function_registered` / `function_unregistered` counters; `functions_used_for(name)` read-only inspector. **Parallel Codex (gpt-5.5 xhigh) + Opus reviewer audit; verdict SHIP-WITH-FIXES** — 3 HIGH (1 fixed in audit-fix, 2 filed for 6.4 entry-plan), 5 MED (2 closed in audit-fix or by H3 disposition, 3 filed for 6.4), 4 LOW (all 4 closed in audit-fix), 5 INFO. Synthesis `docs/audits/2026-05-28-6-4-0-substrate-audit/SYNTHESIS.md`. **Audit-fix `63592126afe`:** (1) **H2 (HIGH)** — `WorkbookRuntime::recompute_all`'s cycle pre-pass at `workbook_runtime/recompute.rs:111` was building an ephemeral session via the zero-arg `rebuild_from_workbook(wb)`, silently falling back to `default_registry()` (benign today; silent divergence at 6.4 with UDFs); swapped to `_with_registry(self.workbook, self.registry)`. (2) **Codex A LOW** — `unregister_metadata` could remove builtin metadata (leaving dispatch present + metadata absent = silent walker regression); audit-fix guards via `if self.fns.contains_key(upper) → Conflict`. (3) **Opus L2** — `debug_assert!` migration-shim invariant upgraded to `assert!` (release builds now fail loud at boot rather than ship with silent unknown-fn fallback). (4) **Opus L3** — `HookCounts` gains `function_registered` / `function_unregistered` fields for parity. (5) **Opus M4 + Codex D LOW** — 5 new substrate tests pin: ROW + ISREF in `functions_used` (push-before-routing invariant); `ROW(NOW())` records BOTH names AND propagates `is_volatile` through the address-only walker's registry-passing delegation; transitive fanout on `on_function_registered` (chain `A1=NOW(), B1=A1+1, C1=B1+1` all dirty); `ROW(MyName)` cleanup regression (widened-storage-gate fix pin); `unregister_metadata` builtin-guard. (6) **H3 (HIGH) DOC-honesty correction** — hook docstrings now state plainly: substrate hooks ONLY dirty + transitive-fan; they do NOT re-extract deps. Contract §10.3 says "register / unregister dirties every formula referencing that canonical name (re-extract deps + reschedule)" — substrate satisfies the "dirty + reschedule" halves; "re-extract deps" lands at the 6.4 orchestrator level. **Tracked block-on-6.4-entry:** **H1** — `ql-exec::plan` carries two more hardcoded `matches!` whitelists (`is_aggregate_function`:406-505, `is_reference_aware_function`:566-571) that drive the binder's `arg_ctx` decision; UDFs with range args (every `BatchShape::ArrayBatch` UDF per the contract DTO) won't bind until these also derive from registry metadata. The substrate is "two-thirds of the UDF prerequisite"; H1 is the missing third. **H3** — re-extract gap; 6.4 closes via either (1) `fn_gen: u64` counter on `PlanCache` (mirror `name_gen` at `plan_cache.rs:69-74`; bump per register/unregister; cache misses trigger re-bind + re-extract on next eval) or (2) per-dependent `reextract_deps(node, &cached_plan, &workbook, &registry)` in the `WorkbookSession::register_function` orchestrator. **Filed for 6.4 (non-blocking):** M1 `FormulaDeps::is_empty/len()` lie (only check 2 of 6 fields); M3 `iter_metadata` HashMap-order (add `sorted_metadata()` view, matching the 6.1C H2 ordering discipline); M5 `FunctionRegistryError → EngineError` mapper + Appendix A `function_exists` / `function_not_found` rows; I1 `DepShape::LazyShape` for ISREF (today: hardcoded `name == "ISREF"` short-circuit at the walker); I2 metadata-update atomicity policy docs; L1 walker hot-path `to_ascii_uppercase()` allocation per call. **Cycle budget honored:** Cycle 1 = substrate code; cycle 2 = audit-fix; doc-sync separate. **Verification (focused re-verify of affected lanes):** `cargo build -p ql-exec -p ql-functions -p ql-bindings-node` clean; `cargo test -p ql-exec --lib` **742/0** (732 pre-substrate + 6 cycle-1 + 4 audit-fix); `cargo test -p ql-functions --lib` **1815/0** (1808 pre-substrate + 8 cycle-1; audit-fix rewrote one test, net unchanged); `cargo check --workspace` clean; clippy clean for edits (pre-existing warnings in ql-collab unchanged); `node crates/ql-bindings-node/tests/smoke_session.mjs` PASS. **NEXT (canonical decision-lock §2 item 6): 6.4 Python UDFs (the wedge function).** Block-on-entry: close H1 (plan.rs whitelists) + H3 (re-extract via fn_gen or per-dependent reextract) in the 6.4 entry-plan; ship M1/M3/M5/I1/I2 as substrate-completion sub-increments at 6.4 entry; L1 + cross-cutting effective-extent serializer fix on the 6.4 backlog list.
