quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:346:    Audit dispatched: Codex (gpt-5-codex via `codex exec`) reviewed Phase 3.1–3.9 commits independently. Findings: 4 HIGH (H1 range-deps-not-edges, H2 set_name not transitive, H3/H4 append-only-graph rebind staleness), 4 MEDIUM, 3 LOW, 6 test gaps. **Closed in audit commit:** H2 (BFS fanout fix + regression test `h2_set_name_propagates_dirty_transitively`), L1 (architecture doc rewrite), L2 (GAP-G-01 re-classified from performance-only to correctness), T4 (set_name regression test). **Deferred to Phase 4 with documented gaps:** H1 → GAP-G-03 (range-as-scheduler-edge), H3+H4 → GAP-G-01 (now correctness; needs delta-edge graph), M1 → GAP-R-08 (volatile-dependent recompute Excel-canon), M3 → GAP-S-06 (load bounds for formula-only cells). Full audit report: `docs/audits/2026-05-12-phase-3-megaudit.md`.  
quantbook-engine/docs/MASTER-PLAN.md:549:✅ **5.7 V3.6 PHASE TERMINATION CLEAN** (V3.6.0.1 LOCK + V3.6.0.2 D1 + V3.6.0.X AUDIT-CLOSURE + V3.6.0.3 D2 + V3.6.0.X AUDIT-OF-D2 + V3.6.0.4 D3 + V3.6.0.X AUDIT-OF-D3 + V3.6.0.5 D4 + V3.6.0.X AUDIT-OF-D4 + V3.6.0.6 D5 + V3.6.0.X AUDIT-OF-D5 + V3.6.0.7 D6 SPIKE + V3.6.0.8.1 D6 LOCK + V3.6.0.8.2 ENGINE PART 1 + V3.6.0.8.3 ENGINE PART 2 napi + V3.6.0.8.4 AUDIT-OF-D6 + 5 HIGH CLOSURES + BENCH + V3.6.0.8.5 MOCHA + V3.6.0.10 D8 Op::RestoreSheet + V3.6.0.10 DOCS MEGAUDIT + V3.6.0.11 D9 typing-stroke watchdog SHIPPED 2026-05-23 → 05-26)** -- 9 D-decisions per V3.5.0.X Opus § F V3.6 ENTRY READINESS packet.  Status: D1-D6 + D8 + D9 SHIPPED; only D7 (#REF! substitution at V3.6.0.9) remains conditional pending user signal.  D6 perf contract delivered with 46× headroom (1.08 ms at 100 new cells vs 246 ms full snapshot).  D9 typing-stroke watchdog closes R-V3.5-7 false-negative.  V3.6 phase-termination megaudit unblocked at V3.6.0.11 ship.  D1 (Loro UndoManager `set_on_push` + `set_on_pop` callback wiring, HIGH PRIORITY): closes V3.5.0.X conservative `pure_local_frontier` gate properly via Loro 1.12.0's verified API (`OnPop = Box<dyn Fn(UndoOrRedo, CounterSpan, UndoItemMeta) + Send + Sync>` at registry/loro-internal-1.12.0/src/undo.rs:199); REMOVES `pure_local_frontier` field in V3.6.0.2.  D2 (session-wide RegisterFormat FormatTable cache): new `format_table_cache: HashMap<FormatId, Arc<str>>` field + new `CacheEffect::RegisterFormat` variant + new `FormatDefJson` napi struct + `WorkbookSnapshotJson.formats` additive field; unblocks D4 format-aware rendering.  D3 (per-cell op-index): new `cell_op_index: HashMap<(SheetId, RowId, ColId), Vec<usize>>` field; closes V3.5.0.6 R-V3.5-2 perf gap (invalidate_cell O(N) -> O(ops-for-this-cell)).  D4 (format-aware buildHtml rendering): engine-side `format_value` reuse via Phase 4.6 D-1 FormatTable; new `rendered: Option<String>` field on CellSnapshotJson; new `dateSystem: String` field on WorkbookSnapshotJson ("Excel1900" | "Excel1904"; String chosen over wrapper struct for simplicity; napi-rs auto-camelCases at JS boundary); workbook.locale() passthrough + per-snapshot parsed-format cache + Pending-skip per V3.6.0.X audit-of-D4 closures; CSP-safe.  D5 (IDE-facing `appendPutFormula` napi, NEW): thin wrapper over existing `Op::PutFormula`; unblocks end-to-end repaired-formula integration tests (closes V3.5.0.X A-HIGH-2 IDE-level verification gap).  D6 (incremental WorkbookSnapshot deltas): DEFER pending V3.6.0.7 mid-cycle profiling spike; ship only if cost > 50ms/call.  D7 (#REF! substitution): DEFER until user signal.  D8 (Op::RestoreSheet): DEFER until user signal.  D9 (sheet-tabs UX + mid-edit-render guard typing-stroke watchdog): DEFER sheet-tabs to V3.6+ multi-tab redesign per Opus § G; ship typing-stroke watchdog as V3.6.0.10 only if surfaced.  V3.6 sub-step rollout (actual + planned): V3.6.0.1 docs-only LOCK ✅; V3.6.0.2-0.6 priority ship (D1-D5) ✅; V3.6.0.7 profiling spike ✅ (verdict: D6 SHIPS); V3.6.0.8.1-8.5 D6 arc COMPLETE ✅ (D6 perf contract delivered with 46× headroom); V3.6.0.9 D7 #REF! conditional (PENDING user signal); V3.6.0.10 D8 Op::RestoreSheet ✅ SHIPPED + V3.6.0.10 docs megaudit ✅ SHIPPED; V3.6.0.11 D9 typing-stroke watchdog conditional (PENDING user signal); V3.6.0.X parallel Codex+Opus phase-termination megaudit + closures (PENDING at V3.6.0.11 ship; ~6-8 sessions).  Total estimated V3.6 wall time: 14-20 sessions.  **18 risks documented in plan as R-V3.6-1..18 + R-V3.6-NEW (the V3.6.0.7-spike-discovered rebuild_workbook dominant-cost risk, CLOSED-AT-V3.6.0.8.1 via option (a) cache rebuilt+repaired Workbook + clone-and-apply-delta)**.  All non-conditional risks closed; conditionals tied to D7/D9 surfacing.  Plan at `.plans/_active.md`.  ✅ **V3.6.0.2 D1 SHIPPED** at engine `89f5a5f9e0b`: REMOVED `pure_local_frontier` field + dispatch gate; ADDED `pending_undo_cells: Arc<Mutex<Option<Vec<(u16, u32, u32)>>>>` field + on_push closure encoding cells as LoroValue::List<List<I64>> into UndoItemMeta::value; undo/redo use top_undo_meta/top_redo_meta + pre-stage cells for synthetic inverse op's on_push; 2 V3.5.0.X regression tests REWRITTEN to verify partial-invalidate FIRES correctly (not full-rebuild fallback).  ✅ **V3.6.0.X AUDIT-CLOSURE SHIPPED** at engine `(THIS commit)`: Codex Lane A `docs/audits/2026-05-24-phase-5-7-v3-6-0-2-codex.md` (FAIL: 1 HIGH + 1 LOW + 2 INFO); Opus Lane B inline audit (PASS-WITH-CONVERGENT-FINDING).  Convergent HIGH (CODEX-V3-6-0-2-HIGH-1): grouped-undo + merge-interval-undo lose cells because Loro's `push_with_merge` discards subsequent meta when merging spans -- only the FIRST push's meta survives.  Codex empirically verified with `codex_tmp_grouped_undo_cache_probe` (4 stale cells remained post-undo); Opus independently confirmed by reading loro-internal-1.12.0/src/undo.rs:389-396.  Closure: new `inside_group: bool` + `undo_merge_interval_ms: i64` fields on CollabSession; start/end_undo_group + set_undo_merge_interval maintain these; append_op gates partial-invalidate behind `!inside_group && undo_merge_interval_ms == 0` (conservative full-rebuild fallback matches V3.5.0.6 semantics for grouped undo).  Clean fix (`set_top_undo_meta` to union cells) BLOCKED: API exists on loro_internal but not exposed on public `loro::UndoManager`; deferred to V3.6+ pending upstream contribution.  +2 ql-collab regression tests: grouped_undo_clears_cache_for_all_cells_in_the_group + merge_interval_undo_clears_cache_for_all_cells_in_window.  CODEX-LOW-1 (coverage expansion) DEFERRED to V3.6.0.3+ backlog.  Rule 4 arc terminus HELD at 6 throughout V3.6.0.2 + V3.6.0.X (new fields all Copy+Send+Sync trivially; 0 new triggers).  Cumulative V3.6 cycle through V3.6.0.X audit: +2 ql-collab tests (115 -> 117), IDE mocha unchanged at 346.  Audit transcripts: 33 (was 32; +1 V3.6.0.2 Codex Lane A).  Cumulative findings closed across Phase 5.7: 19+ HIGH + 50+ MEDIUM (was 18+ HIGH + 49+ MEDIUM).  ✅ **V3.6.0.3 D2 SHIPPED** at engine `ffa598a1c15` + IDE `b159c899359`: session-wide RegisterFormat FormatTable cache (new `format_table_cache: HashMap<FormatId, Arc<str>>` field on CollabSession + new `CacheEffect::RegisterFormat { id, string }` variant + walker integration; `apply_cache_effect` signature extended with 3rd param; all 3 callers updated; `force_clear_snapshot_cache` clears the cache; `rebuild_snapshot_cache` atomic-swaps; `invalidate_cell` uses throwaway local cache since RegisterFormat is session-wide) + new `FormatDefJson { id: FormatIdJson, string: String }` napi struct + `WorkbookSnapshotJson.formats: Vec<FormatDefJson>` additive field (populated from `Workbook.formats().iter()` -- authoritative; merges Builtin 0..=163 + Custom; avoids surfacing cross-peer cache-vs-Workbook divergence under concurrent RegisterFormat same-id-different-string).  IDE: `WorkbookSnapshotJson` interface gains required `formats: FormatDefJson[]` + new `FormatDefJson` interface; +4 mocha pinning shape; +1 stale V3.5.0.2 shape test updated; +10 V3.5.0.4b fixture additions for the now-required field.  +2 ql-collab regression tests: `register_format_op_populates_session_format_table_cache` + `register_format_cache_rebuilds_from_log_via_rebuild_snapshot_cache`.  Tests: ql-collab **119/119** (117 baseline + 2 new); IDE mocha **350/350** (346 baseline + 4 new).  Rule 4 arc terminus HELD at 6 (1 new ql-collab field + 1 new napi struct; positive Send+Sync via composition: `HashMap<K,V>: Send+Sync` iff both; `FormatId: Copy+Send+Sync`; `Arc<str>: Send+Sync`; `FormatDefJson` over `FormatIdJson` V3.5.0.5 walk + `String`; 0 new triggers).  Cumulative V3.6 cycle (through V3.6.0.3 D2): +4 ql-collab (115 -> 119); +4 IDE mocha (346 -> 350); audit transcripts still 33.  ✅ **V3.6.0.X AUDIT-OF-D2 SHIPPED** at engine `8480f247aea` + IDE `21fe6a73ec6` (2026-05-23).  Parallel Codex Lane A + Opus Lane B audit of V3.6.0.3 D2 surface; both PASS-WITH-FINDINGS.  Codex transcript: `docs/audits/2026-05-23-phase-5-7-v3-6-0-3-codex.md` (0 HIGH + 3 MED + 4 LOW + 6 INFO).  Opus transcript: `docs/audits/2026-05-23-phase-5-7-v3-6-0-3-opus.md` (1 HIGH + 3 MED + 4 LOW + 4 INFO).  3 convergent findings closed in-cycle: **CONVERGENT-HIGH-1** (Opus HIGH-1 ≡ Codex MED-3): cache walker LWW (`insert`) -> first-write-wins (`entry().or_insert`) mirroring `FormatTable::register_at`'s IdCollision rejection at the cache layer; closes the V3.6.0.1 plan body § D2 line 133 locked decision violation.  **CONVERGENT-MED-1** (Codex MED-1 ≡ Opus MED-2): `workbook_snapshot.formats` sorted by FormatId via the engine's derived Ord (Builtin variants first per enum order, then Custom lexicographically by `(peer, counter)`) before returning -- pre-closure was raw HashMap iter which varied across consecutive calls due to per-instance random hasher.  **CONVERGENT-MED-2** (Codex MED-2 ≡ Opus MED-1+MED-3): `collect_cache_effects` drops Builtin variant `Op::RegisterFormat` payloads at the cache walker (matches "ONLY Custom" docstring claim); Workbook-side `FormatTable::register_at` still accepts in-range Builtins as Phase 4.6 D-1 backward-compat (deferred V3.7+).  Codex INFO-1 REFUTED suspected undo-of-Op::RegisterFormat staleness bug empirically (Probe 1: non-cell-keyed ops trigger full-rebuild fallback via the V3.6.0.X audit-closure gate).  +5 ql-collab regression tests (Opus H.1 + H.2 + H.3 + H.5 + H.7).  Opus LOW-1 (CacheBuckets refactor) DEFERRED to V3.6.0.4 D3 ship.  Opus LOW-3 (Builtin 0..=163 docstring drift; ~20 actually preloaded) folded into 4-site docstring sweep.  Cumulative V3.6 cycle (through V3.6.0.X audit-of-D2): +9 ql-collab (115 -> 124); IDE mocha 350/350 unchanged (sort change is deterministic across existing shape tests).  Audit transcripts: 35 (was 33; +2 V3.6.0.X audit-of-D2 Codex + Opus).  Cumulative findings closed across Phase 5.7: 20+ HIGH + 53+ MEDIUM (was 19+ HIGH + 50+ MEDIUM).  Rule 4 arc terminus HELD at 6 (no new fields/variants/structs in audit-of-D2; behavior-only closures: `entry/or_insert` + `sort_by_key` + Builtin early-return).  ✅ **V3.6.0.4 D3 SHIPPED** at engine `119df9b3826` (2026-05-23).  Per-cell + per-sheet op-log index closes V3.5.0.6 R-V3.5-2 perf gap.  Engine surface: new `cell_op_index: HashMap<(u16,u32,u32), Vec<usize>>` + `sheet_op_index: HashMap<u16, Vec<usize>>` fields on CollabSession; new `CacheBuckets<'a>` struct bundling 5 mutable refs (closes Opus LOW-1 from V3.6.0.X audit-of-D2); new `OpLog::get(index)` accessor on ql-oplog (random-access lookup); `apply_cache_effect` signature refactored to `(&mut CacheBuckets<'_>, CacheEffect, op_log_index: usize)`; new `rebuild_op_indices_only()` helper called by undo+redo BEFORE the per-cell invalidate loop (necessary because Loro's UndoManager retract COMPACTS the visible op list and shifts positional indices -- design discovery during V3.6.0.4 implementation; documented as R-V3.6-10).  `invalidate_cell` rewritten to walk via `cell_op_index ∪ sheet_op_index` instead of full log walk: O(ops-for-this-cell) typical 1-3 + O(removes-for-this-sheet) typical 0-1 vs pre-D3 O(N).  `force_clear_snapshot_cache` clears the new indices; new `cell_op_index_iter` + `sheet_op_index_iter` accessors.  +6 ql-collab regression tests (130/130 pass; +6 over V3.6.0.X audit-of-D2 124 baseline).  Rule 4 arc terminus HELD at 6 (2 new HashMap fields + 1 struct with 5 ref fields; all positive Send+Sync via composition; 0 new triggers).  This session counted 3 plan-implement-audit cycles (V3.6.0.X audit-of-D2 + closures + V3.6.0.4 D3 ship), 1 over the CLAUDE.md ≤2 guideline; user-directed exception via AskUserQuestion.  ✅ **V3.6.0.X AUDIT-OF-D3 SHIPPED** at engine (this commit) (2026-05-23).  Parallel Codex Lane A + Opus Lane B audit of V3.6.0.4 D3 surface; both PASS-WITH-FINDINGS.  Codex transcript: `docs/audits/2026-05-23-phase-5-7-v3-6-0-4-codex.md` (0 HIGH + 2 MED + 4 LOW + 5 INFO).  Opus transcript: `docs/audits/2026-05-23-phase-5-7-v3-6-0-4-opus.md` (1 HIGH + 2 MED + 4 LOW + 3 INFO).  4 in-cycle closures: **CONVERGENT-HIGH-1** (Opus HIGH-1 / Codex LOW-2): `invalidate_cell` atomic-swap (build-into-fresh; defer `self.last_snapshot.remove(target_key)` until AFTER all fallible `OpLog::get` calls succeed).  Pre-closure the unconditional `remove()` at entry + fallible mid-walk Err produced a torn-write hazard.  **CONVERGENT-MED-2** (Codex MED-2 / Opus MED-1): `rebuild_op_indices_only` rewritten to use `apply_cache_effect` (canonical walker) with throwaway snapshot/format_cache buckets + local tombstones tracker; gives tombstone-aware index parity with `rebuild_snapshot_cache`.  Also added `cell_op_index.retain(|(sheet,_,_),_| *sheet != id)` to RemoveSheet handler (mirrors `snapshot.retain`; prunes ghost index entries for cells on tombstoned sheets).  **Codex MED-1**: `poll_remote_with_limit` partial-error rebuild -- track first drain error in the loop; if `merged > 0` before propagating, run `rebuild_snapshot_cache` to keep cache + indices consistent with the committed log state.  **Codex LOW-1**: `OpLog::get` docstring corrected from "O(1)" to "O(log N) BTree lookup" per Loro 1.12.0's internal `LengthFinder`-over-`generic_btree::BTree` implementation; invalidate_cell docstring updated to reflect the honest O(ops-for-this-cell * log N) bound.  ide-consumer-contract.md sweep: V3.6.0.4 D3 SHIPPED inline + R-V3.5-2 marked CLOSED.  +4 ql-collab regression tests (134/134 pass; +4 over V3.6.0.4 D3 130 baseline).  Codex INFO-3 + INFO-5 noted for V3.7+ (long-term stable-op-ID migration design; OpLog::append stores JSON-only payload + would need wire-format extension).  Rule 4 arc terminus HELD at 6 (no new fields/structs in audit-of-D3; behavior-only closures).  Cumulative V3.6 cycle: +19 ql-collab tests (115 -> 134); IDE mocha 350/350 unchanged; audit transcripts: 37 (was 35; +2 V3.6.0.4 Codex + Opus).  Cumulative findings closed across Phase 5.7: 21+ HIGH + 55+ MEDIUM (was 20+ HIGH + 53+ MEDIUM).  This session counted **5 plan-implement-audit cycles** (V3.6.0.X audit-of-D2 + closures + V3.6.0.4 D3 ship + V3.6.0.X audit-of-D3 + closures), 3 over CLAUDE.md ≤2 guideline; user-directed exception via AskUserQuestion + "Proceed next" directives.  ✅ **V3.6.0.5 D4 SHIPPED** at engine (this commit) + IDE (this commit) (2026-05-23).  Format-aware buildHtml rendering via engine-side `ql_functions::format::render`.  Engine napi: new `CellSnapshotJson.rendered: Option<String>` additive field (populated when cell has format + value: format::parse the format-string -> render(value, fmt, eval_context) where eval_context.date_system = workbook.date_system() + locale = EnUs + now_provider = System).  Silent fallback to `None` on: no format / no value / format-id lookup miss / format-string parse error / wire-decode error.  New `WorkbookSnapshotJson.dateSystem: String` additive field ("Excel1900" | "Excel1904"; mapped from `ql_types::DateSystem`).  IDE: `types.ts` interfaces extended (CellSnapshotJson.rendered?: string + WorkbookSnapshotJson.dateSystem union); QuantbookCellSnapshot.entries[*].rendered passthrough; `extractSheetSnapshot` conditional include (only when rendered defined -- preserves exact-shape tests); `cellGridHtml::renderRows` + client-side `renderRowsClient` use `e.rendered ?? formatCellValue(e.value)` (escapeHtml covers both paths; CSP-safe).  +4 mocha shape tests (354/354 pass; +4 over V3.6.0.X audit-of-D3 350 baseline).  ql-collab 134/134 unchanged (no engine collab-side changes).  Rule 4 arc terminus HELD at 6 (1 new String field + 1 new Option<String> field on existing napi structs; 0 new triggers).  **mocha-test scope limitation**: full format::render integration tests (Op::RegisterFormat + Op::SetCellFormat + Op::PutValue -> rendered output) are deferred to V3.6.0.X audit-of-D4 -- the IDE napi at V3.6.0.5 D4 has no appendSetCellFormat / appendRegisterFormat method, so end-to-end mocha can only pin SHAPE.  Engine-side Rust integration tests TBD at audit-of-D4 closure.  Cumulative V3.6 cycle: ql-collab 134/134 + mocha 350 -> 354; audit transcripts still 37.  This session counted **6 plan-implement-audit cycles** (V3.6.0.X audit-of-D2 + closures + V3.6.0.4 D3 ship + V3.6.0.X audit-of-D3 + closures + V3.6.0.5 D4 ship), 4 over CLAUDE.md ≤2 guideline; user-directed exception via repeated "Proceed next" + "Ship D4 fully this session" AskUserQuestion answer.  ✅ **V3.6.0.X AUDIT-OF-D4 SHIPPED** at engine (this commit) + IDE (this commit) (2026-05-24).  Most serious audit verdict in V3.6 cycle: Codex Lane A FAIL (1 HIGH + 2 MED + 3 LOW + 4 INFO) + Opus Lane B FAIL (3 HIGH + 3 MED + 4 LOW + 3 INFO).  Transcripts: `docs/audits/2026-05-24-phase-5-7-v3-6-0-5-codex.md` + `docs/audits/2026-05-24-phase-5-7-v3-6-0-5-opus.md`.  Convergent + in-cycle closures: **CONVERGENT-HIGH-1** (both lanes empirically probed): new `Op::SetDateSystem` wire variant + `DateSystemWire` enum (mirrors LocaleWire pattern) + replay handler + `from_qbook` seeds the op when loaded workbook's date_system != default.  Pre-closure Excel1904 workbooks rendered with Excel1900 epoch (1462-day off-by-one).  R-V3.6-11 documented.  **OPUS-HIGH-2** (Codex missed): new IDE `data-raw-value` attribute carries parseable raw representation for click-to-edit; `beginEdit` reads it first (falls back to `data-original-text` for backward compat).  Pre-closure `parseCellRawInput` NaN'd on currency/percent/thousands/date format-rendered strings, breaking every formatted-cell edit.  R-V3.6-12 documented.  **CONVERGENT-HIGH-3** (Opus HIGH-3 / Codex MED-1): short-circuit pre-render when `wire_value.is_pending()`; preserves IDE "(pending)" fallback.  Pre-closure pending+format displayed as formatted zero (Value::Blank routed as 0.0).  R-V3.6-13 documented.  **CONVERGENT-MED-1**: thread `workbook.locale()` through EvalContext (prevents silent forward-compat regression at V3.6.1+).  **CONVERGENT-MED-2**: per-snapshot parsed-format cache (HashMap<FormatId, FormatString>; reuses parse result across cells sharing FormatId).  **CONVERGENT-MED-3**: ide-consumer-contract.md sweep (R-V3.5-4 marked CLOSED; D4 "deferred" updated to SHIPPED).  **OPUS-LOW-2 + LOW-3**: dropped `.to_string()` on lookup result + TS docstring `date_system` -> `dateSystem`.  +2 ql-collab regression tests (Op::SetDateSystem replay + unknown-wire error).  Rule 4 arc terminus HELD at 6 (new DateSystemWire enum + Op::SetDateSystem variant; both Send+Sync via primitive composition; 0 new triggers).  Cumulative V3.6 cycle: ql-collab 134 -> 136; IDE mocha 354/354 unchanged; audit transcripts: 39 (was 37; +2 V3.6.0.5 Codex + Opus).  Cumulative findings closed across Phase 5.7: 24+ HIGH + 58+ MEDIUM (was 21+ HIGH + 55+ MEDIUM).  This session counted **8 plan-implement-audit cycles** (audit-of-D2 + closures + D3 + audit-of-D3 + closures + D4 + audit-of-D4 + closures), 6 over CLAUDE.md ≤2 guideline; user-directed exception throughout via "Proceed next" chain + AskUserQuestion "Close all in-cycle".  **V3.6.0.6 D5 IDE-facing appendPutFormula napi** (Opus § F.5, ~1 session) is the next recommended sub-step.  Baselines tracked: ql-collab **136/136** + IDE mocha **354/354** + ql-collab-ws 40/40 + engine workspace all 30 suites pass.  ✅ **V3.6.0.6 D5 SHIPPED** at engine (this commit) + IDE (this commit) (2026-05-24).  Engine napi: new `CollabSession::appendPutFormula(sheet: u16, row: f64, col: f64, text: String) -> Result<()>` mirroring `appendPutValue` validation discipline (validate_u32_index on row/col + sheet u16 at FFI boundary); wraps existing `Op::PutFormula { sheet, row, col, text }` (shipping since Phase 4.6.x); no new wire variant; no new CacheEffect (the cell-keyed cache walker already handles PutFormula via `CacheEffect::Cell`).  IDE: `types.ts` adds `CollabSessionInstance.appendPutFormula(...)` + `QuantbookCellSnapshot.entries[*].formula?: string`; `session.ts` adds `appendPutFormulaValidated(session, sheet, row, col, text)` typed wrapper (validates sheet/row/col BEFORE the FFI ToUint32-coercion boundary; matches `appendPutValueValidated` pattern; text not