quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-18-phase-4-12-megaudit-consolidated.md:30:| C1 | Codex H-1 | NETWORKDAYS/WORKDAY out-of-range bounds | W5-D-PM12-1 |
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-17-w5-d-5-opus.md:83:The matrix entry (line 124) says `0 ≤ p ≤ 1 INCLUSIVE` which is technically right at the domain-check level but misleading at the result level. Either pin a test asserting `gamma_inv(p=1, α=1, β=1) = #NUM!` or update the matrix entry to `0 ≤ p < 1 effectively (p=1 → #NUM! via Inf-guard)`. Same shape applies to GAMMA.INV at `p = 0` with `α = 0.001` (well-defined → 0) vs `p = 0` with `α >> 1` (statrs returns 0; documented inclusive lower).
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-17-w5-d-5-opus.md:115:`beta_dist_arity_mismatch_returns_value` tests 0, 3, and 7 args (rejects 0/3 below 4, 7 above 6). `beta_dist_optional_bounds_scaling` uses 6 args. `beta_dist_a_equals_b_is_num_error` uses 6 args. No test exercises the 5-arg path (A specified, B defaults to 1.0). Same for BETA.INV — `beta_inv_optional_bounds_scaling` and `beta_inv_b_below_a` use 5 args; no test exercises the 4-arg path (A specified, B defaults). The variadic boundary handler at line 1600-1607 is technically untested for the "lower bound only" intermediate case.
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-17-w5-d-5-opus.md:123:`beta_dist_x_outside_bounds_is_num_error` tests `x = -0.5` (x < A) and `x = 1.5` (x > B). The boundary case `x = A` (passes the `<` check) should return CDF=0 / PDF depending on shape. `beta_dist_cdf_at_one_returns_one` covers x=B boundary for Beta(2,3). x=A boundary not covered. Minor gap; the bound check is `x < a || x > b` (strict) so x=A and x=B both pass, but only x=B has a numerical assertion pinned.
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-17-w5-d-5-opus.md:139:3. **Beta optional bounds transform**: `t = (x - a) / width`, `pdf / width` (Jacobian) at lines 1614-1622. Matches IronCalc beta.rs:96-97/114. Verified anchor: BETA.DIST(5,1,1,FALSE,0,10) = 0.1 (U(0,10) PDF = 1/10). BETA.DIST(5,1,1,TRUE,0,10) = 0.5 (CDF at midpoint).
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-17-w5-d-5-opus.md:143:5. **A == B rejected for BETA.DIST; B <= A rejected for BETA.INV**: BETA.DIST line 1611 uses `b == a` matching IronCalc (b < a indirectly rejected via x-bounds since x can't simultaneously be ≥a and ≤b when a > b). BETA.INV line 1672 uses `b <= a` matching IronCalc beta.rs:183 (`<=` not `<`).
