quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-19-phase-5-6-v1-codex.md:2877:    85	| ~~GAP-F-05~~ | ~~`ScalarFn` cannot carry range-vs-scalar argument metadata.~~ **CLOSED in Engine Phase 4.3 V2 (W5-53; refined W5-54).** Approach (a) — parallel `RangeAwareFn = fn(&[FnArg]) -> Value` table — chosen instead of full migration of the ~60 existing scalar entries. `FnArg` lives in `crates/ql-functions/src/range_aware_fns.rs`. **Final shape (W5-54 refactor):** `enum FnArg { Scalar(Value), Range { values: Vec<Value>, rows: usize, cols: usize } }` — `Range` is a struct variant carrying 2D shape, invariant `rows * cols == values.len()`. 1D consumers (SUMIF, COUNTIF) pattern-match `{ values, .. }` and ignore shape; 2D consumers (VLOOKUP, HLOOKUP, INDEX, MATCH) consume `rows`/`cols`. `FunctionRegistry` carries a second table `range_aware_fns: HashMap<&'static str, RangeAwareFn>` with `register_range_aware` / `lookup_range_aware`. Cross-table name collision panics at registration. Eval dispatch in `crates/ql-exec/src/scalar.rs::eval_scalar_with_cache` checks `lookup_range_aware` FIRST and constructs `Vec<FnArg>` from `ExprPlan` args (AggregateNameRef → `Range { values, rows, cols }` via `env.read_range_with_shape`, other plans → `Scalar` via recursive eval). SUMIF + COUNTIF shipped on this infra W5-53; SUMIFS / AVERAGEIF / SUMPRODUCT / VLOOKUP / HLOOKUP / MATCH / INDEX / CHOOSE + LARGE/SMALL/RANK/MEDIAN/MODE all live on it by W5-58. **W5-60 closure** added strict 2D shape validation in IFS family + SUMPRODUCT (`(rows, cols)` consensus, not flat length); `env.read_range_with_shape` distinguishes open-ended (clamp) from bounded (preserve+pad-with-Blank) ranges. 5 e2e tests in `workbook_runtime` + range-fn unit tests + 4 registry conflict/disjoint tests + extended `is_aggregate_function_lists_only_registered_aggregates` invariant test + W5-60 6 new 2D-shape regression tests. |
