quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-27-inc2c67-undo-audit/SYNTHESIS.md:14:- **Q3 recompute detachment** (no spurious ops/commits), **Q4 token/delta coherence** (epoch bump → EpochMismatch, change-log cleared), **Q5 F2 ClearValue** (replay guard identical to PutValue; `put_at(Blank)` truly clears; all producers covered), **Q6 lifecycle/No-Fallbacks** (gated Ready; empty stack → consumed:false; `group_end` always runs; no swallow) — all verified clean.
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-27-inc2c67-undo-audit/SYNTHESIS.md:27:| **LOW (L1)** | Silent 100-step undo cap (Loro's `set_max_undo_steps(100)` default, not overridden). | **DOCUMENTED** on the `undo_manager` field (bounded retention is intentional for v1, mirrors `ops`/`events`/`change_log` bounds; configurable depth = later increment). |
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-24-phase-5-7-v3-5-0-x-codex.md:42:`deleteSheet`/`Op::RemoveSheet` matches the tombstone-preserving ID-slot contract. The wire variant documents idempotency and older-binary forward-compat failure ([crates/ql-oplog/src/op.rs:133](../../crates/ql-oplog/src/op.rs#L133), [crates/ql-oplog/src/op.rs:167](../../crates/ql-oplog/src/op.rs#L167)). `Workbook::remove_sheet` is HashSet-backed and out-of-range tolerant ([crates/ql-storage/src/workbook.rs:749](../../crates/ql-storage/src/workbook.rs#L749)). `PutValue`, `PutFormula`, and `ClearFormula` validate cell bounds and then silently no-op on tombstoned sheets ([crates/ql-oplog/src/replay.rs:404](../../crates/ql-oplog/src/replay.rs#L404), [crates/ql-oplog/src/replay.rs:415](../../crates/ql-oplog/src/replay.rs#L415), [crates/ql-oplog/src/replay.rs:430](../../crates/ql-oplog/src/replay.rs#L430), [crates/ql-oplog/src/replay.rs:441](../../crates/ql-oplog/src/replay.rs#L441)). The napi layer allows already-tombstoned IDs because it checks existence by `sheet_count`, not tombstone state ([crates/ql-bindings-node/src/lib.rs:956](../../crates/ql-bindings-node/src/lib.rs#L956), [crates/ql-bindings-node/src/lib.rs:962](../../crates/ql-bindings-node/src/lib.rs#L962)).
