quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-22-phase-5-7-v2-2-codex.md:4581:quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-20-phase-5-2-d-1-step-4-codex.md:8254:quantbook-engine/docs/architecture/2026-05-14-structured-references-and-tables.md:160:6. **Table footprint fits within the Excel address grid** — NEW W5-125 (Phase 4.8.O.1 closure, Codex HIGH-1). `top_row + rows - 1` must be `≤ MAX_ROW` (1,048,575) and `top_col + cols - 1` must be `≤ MAX_COLUMN` (16,383). `TableMetadata::validate_footprint_bounds` (in `ql-storage`) is the shared check; called at FIVE entry points: producer `create_table` / `resize_table`, replay `apply_create_table` / `apply_resize_table`, and v6 `.qbook` loader. Pre-W5-125 the check was missing, so `for r in top_row..top_row + rows` either ran past the addressable grid (registering cells later `Sheet::put` would panic on) or u32-overflowed silently (skipping all downstream overlap / spill-anchor checks).
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-22-phase-5-7-v2-2-codex.md:4659:quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-20-phase-5-2-d-1-step-4-codex.md:10770:quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-16-phase-4.8.G.3-closing-megaudit-codex.md:2102:docs/architecture/2026-05-14-structured-references-and-tables.md:160:6. **Table footprint fits within the Excel address grid** — NEW W5-125 (Phase 4.8.O.1 closure, Codex HIGH-1). `top_row + rows - 1` must be `≤ MAX_ROW` (1,048,575) and `top_col + cols - 1` must be `≤ MAX_COLUMN` (16,383). `TableMetadata::validate_footprint_bounds` (in `ql-storage`) is the shared check; called at FIVE entry points: producer `create_table` / `resize_table`, replay `apply_create_table` / `apply_resize_table`, and v6 `.qbook` loader. Pre-W5-125 the check was missing, so `for r in top_row..top_row + rows` either ran past the addressable grid (registering cells later `Sheet::put` would panic on) or u32-overflowed silently (skipping all downstream overlap / spill-anchor checks).
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-22-phase-5-7-v2-2-codex.md:5343:quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-15-phase-4.9-closing-megaudit-codex.md:12351:I did not run the test suite because the sandbox is read-only. No findings for R1C1 axis bounds, `@Sheet1!A1` print order, locale unknown save paths, FR/DE separator symmetry, or calcgraph tag collision.
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-22-phase-5-7-v2-2-codex.md:5344:quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-15-phase-4.9-closing-megaudit-codex.md:12370:I did not run the test suite because the sandbox is read-only. No findings for R1C1 axis bounds, `@Sheet1!A1` print order, locale unknown save paths, FR/DE separator symmetry, or calcgraph tag collision.
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-22-phase-5-7-v2-2-codex.md:6249:quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-17-reference-tier-design-codex.md:123:**Detail:** Six tests per function is not enough for a new binder/eval/storage tier. The plan bundles cross-sheet, named range, and range variants into one slot, and does not require structured refs, implicit intersection, array constants, error propagation, formula text canonicalization, or whole-row/whole-column bounds.
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-22-phase-5-7-v2-2-codex.md:6250:quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-17-reference-tier-design-codex.md:125:**Recommendation:** Add a tier-level matrix: literal ranges, named ranges, cross-sheet refs, structured refs (`Sales[Qty]` and `[@Qty]`), `@` implicit intersection, array constants for ROWS/COLUMNS, max bounds, #REF propagation, formula text with leading `=`, non-formula `#N/A`, and recompute/dirty behavior for ISFORMULA/FORMULATEXT.
