quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-22-phase-5-7-v2-2-codex.md:9571:quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-18-phase-4-11-megaudit-opus-a.md:114:Sub-bug **also** in `crates/ql-io-xlsx/src/write/umya_export.rs::render_named_target`: returns `None` for `Constant(Error)` and `Constant(Blank)`, dropping silently with no log to `dropped_features` or `warnings`. The Strict claim "every unsupported feature triggers `XlsxError::UnsupportedFeature`" (`options.rs:60-62`) is violated even under Permissive — the user has no idea the names were lost.
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-22-phase-5-7-v2-2-codex.md:9595:quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-19-phase-5-2-d-1-step-1-codex.md:964:quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-19-phase-5-4-v1-codex.md:2693:quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-19-phase-5-6-v1-codex.md:1064:docs/audits/2026-05-17-w5-d-12-opus.md:104:- **Detail:** Both engine `scalar_fns::counta` and IronCalc `subtotal_counta` count errors (engine: `!matches!(v, Value::Blank).count()` includes Error; IronCalc: `String | Number | Boolean | Error => counta += 1`). Behavior matches. **However**, this is NOT pinned by any SUBTOTAL test — the `subtotal_counta_function_num_3` test only covers `[1, "skip", 2, blank, 3]` (no error). A future refactor of `scalar_fns::counta` to skip errors would silently break compatibility with IronCalc + Excel canon (Excel COUNTA does count errors) and the engine-wide aggregate convention. Probe-verified: `SUBTOTAL(3, [1, #DIV/0!, 3]) = ?`. **Not tested** in the new SUBTOTAL block (probe-confirmed = 3.0 — passes through to counta which counts the error).
