quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-22-phase-5-7-v2-2-codex.md:10633:quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-14-phase-4.6-closing-megaudit-codex.txt:4691:   106	        // behavior silently mapped missing-sheet to `Value::Blank`, which
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-22-phase-5-7-v2-2-codex.md:10941:quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-18-w5-d-14-codex.md:103:**Detail:** `id`, `headerRowCount`, `totalsRowCount`, and `tableColumn/@id` parse failures fall back to `0`/defaults. The parser does not validate `tableColumns/@count`, column count vs `ref` width, duplicate/zero column ids, duplicate table names, or table footprint bounds. `TableTable::insert` overwrites on canonical-name collision, so malformed duplicate tables silently lose one table.
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-22-phase-5-7-v2-2-codex.md:10963:quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-20-phase-5-2-d-1-step-7-consolidated.md:23:| M2 (Opus, Codex L1) | Opus (MEDIUM) / Codex (LOW) | MEDIUM | Version 0 silently accepted. No MIN_SUPPORTED gate. Asymmetric with qbook_format's pattern. | Added `pub const OPLOG_MIN_SUPPORTED_SCHEMA_VERSION: u32 = 1`. Loader now rejects `version < MIN \|\| version > MAX`. Error variant carries both bounds. New regression test `tier_d3_version_zero_rejected_as_unsupported`. | ✅ |
