quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-17-w5-d-1-opus.md:189:### MEDIUM-O-3 — `Value::Blank` arg behavior is untested in all four fns.
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-17-w5-d-1-opus.md:191:**Where:** `crates/ql-functions/src/distribution_fns.rs` test module (no `Value::Blank` use).
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-17-w5-d-1-opus.md:193:**Detail:** The module docstring claims `Blank → 0` (via `to_number_strict` semantics). None of the 35 tests exercise this path. Spreadsheet users **routinely** pass blank-cell references as `mean` / `sd` args without realizing they evaluate as 0:
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-17-w5-d-1-opus.md:195:- `NORM.DIST(0, Blank, Blank, TRUE)` would compute `Φ((0-0)/0)` → `sd=0` → `#NUM!` (correct).
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-17-w5-d-1-opus.md:196:- `NORM.DIST(1, Blank, 1, TRUE)` would compute `Φ(1) ≈ 0.8413` (silently treats missing mean as 0).
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-17-w5-d-1-opus.md:197:- `NORM.DIST(0, 0, 1, Blank)` — `cumulative=Blank` → `to_logical(Blank) → Ok(false)` → PDF path → 1/√(2π).
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-17-w5-d-1-opus.md:199:The third case is potentially surprising: `cumulative=Blank` defaults to `FALSE` (PDF), not user-expected CDF. If a user writes `=NORM.DIST(A1, 0, 1,)` with a trailing blank, they get PDF — but a parser might also reject the trailing comma as an arity error. Either way, **the contract should be tested**.
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-17-w5-d-1-opus.md:207:        norm_dist(&[Value::number(1.0), Value::Blank, Value::number(1.0), Value::Boolean(true)]),
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-17-w5-d-1-opus.md:215:        norm_dist(&[Value::number(1.0), Value::number(0.0), Value::Blank, Value::Boolean(true)]),
