quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-16-phase-4.10-wave-2-closing-megaudit-codex.md:1561:docs/compat/excel-matrix.md:79:| COUNTBLANK | ✅ | 6 | 4.10.B | W5-164: count blank cells in a single range. Per Excel canon (verified vs IronCalc `fn_countblank`): both `Value::Blank` AND empty strings (`""`) count as blank; errors are NOT blank (skipped). Single range arg required (scalar → `#VALUE!`; use COUNTIF for scalar shapes). |
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-16-phase-4.10-wave-2-closing-megaudit-codex.md:1562:docs/compat/excel-matrix.md:90:| AVERAGEA / MAXA / MINA | ✅ | 10 | 4.10.C | W5-165: `*A`-variant aggregates. Per Excel canon: Number → as-is; Boolean → 1/0; Text → 0 (including ""); Blank → SKIPPED. Errors propagate. AVERAGEA: empty / all-blank → #DIV/0!. MAXA / MINA: empty / all-blank → 0. DIVERGES from base AVERAGE / MAX / MIN which skip text + bool entirely. |
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-16-phase-4.10-wave-2-closing-megaudit-codex.md:1573:docs/compat/excel-matrix.md:177:| VALUE | ✅ | 7 | 4.10.E | W5-167: parse text as number, locale-aware decimal separator (EnUs `.`; De/Fr `,`). ContextAwareFn. Trim whitespace; reject empty / non-numeric → #VALUE!. Numbers pass through; Blank → 0. **Strict locale-confusion guard**: in De/Fr locale, `.` in the numeric string → #VALUE! (closes ambiguity for "1.5" vs "1,5"). Currency prefixes + thousands grouping NOT parsed in V1; bundle with Phase 4.5 polish wave. |
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-16-phase-4.10-wave-2-closing-megaudit-codex.md:1581:docs/compat/excel-matrix.md:234:| ISEVEN / ISODD | ✅ | 4 | 4.10.C | W5-165: truncate toward zero (matches Excel canon — `ISEVEN(-2.5)` truncates to -2 → even). Blank coerces to 0 → ISEVEN(blank) = TRUE. Text → #VALUE!. |
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-16-phase-4.10-wave-2-closing-megaudit-codex.md:1582:docs/compat/excel-matrix.md:235:| ISNONTEXT | ✅ | 1 | 4.10.C | W5-165: inverse of ISTEXT. Blank / Number / Boolean / Error → TRUE; only Text → FALSE. |
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-16-phase-4.10-wave-2-closing-megaudit-codex.md:1583:docs/compat/excel-matrix.md:236:| TYPE | ✅ | 1 | 4.10.C | W5-165: 1=Number (Blank also coerces to 1), 2=Text, 4=Boolean, 16=Error. Excel's 64=Array unreachable on this scalar path; flattening happens in eval dispatch. |
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-16-phase-4.10-wave-2-closing-megaudit-codex.md:1584:docs/compat/excel-matrix.md:237:| N | ✅ | 2 | 4.10.C | W5-165: Number → same; Blank → 0; Boolean → 1/0; **Text → 0 (NOT `#VALUE!` per Excel canon; verified vs IronCalc)**; Error → propagate. Date values (stored as Number) round-trip identically. |
