quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-24-phase-5-7-v3-6-0-5-codex.md:12:D4's basic formatted-rendering happy path works, and the IDE escaping path is sound. However, the date-system contract is not actually preserved for collab sessions loaded from `.qbook`: `workbookSnapshot().dateSystem` is effectively `Excel1900` unless a future op-log metadata op exists. That makes Excel1904 date-rendered cells display with the wrong epoch and can resave a loaded Excel1904 workbook as Excel1900.
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-24-phase-5-7-v3-6-0-5-codex.md:20:- `CellWireValue::Pending` is converted to `Value::Blank` at `crates/ql-oplog/src/wire.rs:111`; D4 then routes it through numeric/date formats and can display `"0.00"` instead of the IDE's previous `"(pending)"`.
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-24-phase-5-7-v3-6-0-5-codex.md:26:1. HIGH-1: `dateSystem` is effectively constant under op-log replay / `fromQbook`, so Excel1904 date rendering is wrong.
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-24-phase-5-7-v3-6-0-5-codex.md:60:   - `CellWireValue::Pending` decodes to `Value::Blank` at `crates/ql-oplog/src/wire.rs:111` through `crates/ql-oplog/src/wire.rs:125`.
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-24-phase-5-7-v3-6-0-5-codex.md:61:   - The formatter treats `Value::Blank` as `0.0` for number sections at `crates/ql-functions/src/format/render.rs:202` through `crates/ql-functions/src/format/render.rs:207` and date sections at `crates/ql-functions/src/format/render.rs:520` through `crates/ql-functions/src/format/render.rs:525`.
