quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-24-phase-5-7-v3-6-0-5-opus.md:12:Probes (8 total, replicated the napi `workbook_snapshot` rendering pipeline in pure Rust to bypass the napi-link-time test limitation; covered: happy-path percent format, Pending value rendering, Blank value rendering, Locale hardcoding, DateSystem replay path, format-string HTML-injection passthrough, unregistered-format replay error, Op::SetLocale persistence).
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-24-phase-5-7-v3-6-0-5-opus.md:18:**Verdict: FAIL.**  V3.6.0.5 D4 ships clean engine plumbing for format-aware rendering but the EvalContext construction silently drops two workbook-level inputs the rendering layer depends on -- `workbook.date_system()` is preserved BUT every replay path drops it before the napi sees it (no `Op::SetDateSystem`; `fromQbook` discards the loaded `Workbook`), and `workbook.locale()` is OVERRIDDEN to `EnUs` even when `Op::SetLocale` updated it via replay.  Additionally, the IDE edit-flow regression introduced by D4 (pre-rendered strings populate `data-original-text` which feeds the `<input>` on click-to-edit + the `Escape`-cancel restore path) breaks user editing for any format that introduces non-parseable characters (`$1,234.56`, `50.00%`, `0042` with leading zeros) -- `parseCellRawInput` does `Number(trimmed)` which produces NaN for currency/percent/grouped strings and errors out on Enter.  The Pending-with-format render (`Value::Blank` -> `0.00`) is a third UX regression -- pre-D4 pending cells displayed `"(pending)"`.
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-24-phase-5-7-v3-6-0-5-opus.md:22:The findings are concentrated in five areas: (1) **Op::SetDateSystem does not exist**; the workbook's `date_system` is set by the `.qbook` loader (`set_date_system`) but op-log replay never touches it, so the napi reads the default `Excel1900` regardless.  `fromQbook` then double-faults by discarding the loaded `Workbook` and constructing the session via `export_bytes -> from_snapshot`, so even the loader-side `set_date_system` is lost.  An Excel1904 workbook renders date format strings against Excel1900 (off by 1462 days).  Probed.  (2) **`Locale::EnUs` hardcoded** in the EvalContext while `workbook.locale()` is `EnUs` | `De` | `Fr` -- today the format render layer doesn't consult locale (month names hardcoded English in `render.rs:660-690`), so this is a DEFERRED-feature concern, but the V3.6.0.5 D4 docstring explicitly says "locale-aware deferred to V3.6.1+" implying it WILL matter and the hardcoding silently suppresses workbook locale once render.rs grows locale-conditionals.  Probed.  (3) **IDE `data-original-text` is the engine-pre-rendered string** -- a formatted cell's edit-mode `<input>` populates with the rendered display string, not the raw value; `parseCellRawInput` then NaN's on `$1,234.56` / `50.00%` / `0042`.  Pre-D4 the cell displayed the raw value and Enter committed correctly; post-D4 every format that introduces non-parseable characters breaks the edit path.  Probed by inspection (no compiled test for the mocha-level dispatcher in this audit lane).  (4) **`Pending` value + format -> `"0.00"`**: `CellWireValue::Pending.to_value()` returns `Value::Blank`; `route_section` treats Blank as `0.0`; a Number-format section renders `"0.00"`.  Pre-D4 the IDE explicitly mapped `pending` -> `"(pending)"` via `formatCellValue`; post-D4 the pre-rendered string takes precedence via `??` so a pending+formatted cell displays as `"0.00"`.  Probed.  (5) **No engine-side `FormatString` cache**: `format::parse` runs per-cell-per-snapshot.  For a workbook with 100k formatted cells, that's 100k `parse` invocations per `workbook_snapshot()` call.  The field docstring acknowledges this ("V3.7+ may cache parsed FormatString keyed by format id on CollabSession") but doesn't gate on profiling.
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-24-phase-5-7-v3-6-0-5-opus.md:179:`CellWireValue::Pending.to_value()` returns `Ok(Value::Blank)`.  `format::render(&Value::Blank, ...)` then routes through `routing_index_for_number(0.0, n_sections)` (line 59) -- Blank is treated as 0.0 for section routing AND for digit rendering.  A 1-section Number format like `"0.00"` produces `"0.00"`.
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-24-phase-5-7-v3-6-0-5-opus.md:187:**Severity HIGH** because: (a) silently changes the visible cell state; (b) breaks the IDE's explicit pre-D4 pending semantic; (c) the engine renderer's Blank-as-zero behavior is correct in isolation (it's Excel's behavior for cells with no value but a number format) but the IDE has a different semantic for `Pending` specifically (formula-not-yet-evaluated, not "blank").
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-19-phase-5-4-v2-v1-codex.md:3012: | GAP-O-04 | `set_value(Value::Blank)` emits no `PutValue` (CellWireValue lacks Blank variant). `clear_formula` has the same Blank-skip behavior on the preserved-value op. Documented limitation. | `ql-exec/src/workbook_runtime.rs::set_value` + `::clear_formula` comments | Engine | Engine Phase 5 (CRDT model) or earlier if forced |
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-19-phase-5-4-v2-v1-codex.md:3025: | GAP-S-06 | Phase 3.10 megaudit M3: qbook loader skips the value write for formula cells whose loaded value is `Value::Blank` (Pending), so `Sheet::bounds` doesn't grow to include the formula cell's position. Recompute later produces a real value, but plain load + render-without-recompute can miss formula-only-blank cells at the workbook fringe. | `ql-io/src/qbook_format.rs::load_workbook` formula branch | Engine | Engine Phase 4.5 (date/time + format) or earlier if the IDE forces render-without-recompute |
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-19-phase-5-4-v2-v1-codex.md:3033: | GAP-P-03 | NamedTarget::Constant(Value::Blank) wire-format ambiguity (conflates with formula-Pending) — cycle-3 audit M7 deferred | `ql-io/src/qbook_format.rs::NamedTargetWire::Constant` | Engine | Engine Phase 4 (when wire format gets a freeze pass) |
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-19-phase-5-4-v2-v1-codex.md:3053: | ~~GAP-F-05~~ | ~~`ScalarFn` cannot carry range-vs-scalar argument metadata.~~ **CLOSED in Engine Phase 4.3 V2 (W5-53; refined W5-54).** Approach (a) — parallel `RangeAwareFn = fn(&[FnArg]) -> Value` table — chosen instead of full migration of the ~60 existing scalar entries. `FnArg` lives in `crates/ql-functions/src/range_aware_fns.rs`. **Final shape (W5-54 refactor):** `enum FnArg { Scalar(Value), Range { values: Vec<Value>, rows: usize, cols: usize } }` — `Range` is a struct variant carrying 2D shape, invariant `rows * cols == values.len()`. 1D consumers (SUMIF, COUNTIF) pattern-match `{ values, .. }` and ignore shape; 2D consumers (VLOOKUP, HLOOKUP, INDEX, MATCH) consume `rows`/`cols`. `FunctionRegistry` carries a second table `range_aware_fns: HashMap<&'static str, RangeAwareFn>` with `register_range_aware` / `lookup_range_aware`. Cross-table name collision panics at registration. Eval dispatch in `crates/ql-exec/src/scalar.rs::eval_scalar_with_cache` checks `lookup_range_aware` FIRST and constructs `Vec<FnArg>` from `ExprPlan` args (AggregateNameRef → `Range { values, rows, cols }` via `env.read_range_with_shape`, other plans → `Scalar` via recursive eval). SUMIF + COUNTIF shipped on this infra W5-53; SUMIFS / AVERAGEIF / SUMPRODUCT / VLOOKUP / HLOOKUP / MATCH / INDEX / CHOOSE + LARGE/SMALL/RANK/MEDIAN/MODE all live on it by W5-58. **W5-60 closure** added strict 2D shape validation in IFS family + SUMPRODUCT (`(rows, cols)` consensus, not flat length); `env.read_range_with_shape` distinguishes open-ended (clamp) from bounded (preserve+pad-with-Blank) ranges. 5 e2e tests in `workbook_runtime` + range-fn unit tests + 4 registry conflict/disjoint tests + extended `is_aggregate_function_lists_only_registered_aggregates` invariant test + W5-60 6 new 2D-shape regression tests. |
