quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-22-phase-5-7-v3-2-codex.md:14:- Q1 exportSnapshot napi correctness: PASS. `OpLog::iter()` is index-based over `0..len` and therefore follows visible log order (`crates/ql-oplog/src/log.rs:107-137`). The sheet filter compares `u16` to `u16` (`crates/ql-bindings-node/src/lib.rs:505-517`). The final full-key sort by `(row, col)` makes output ordering deterministic despite `HashMap` iteration (`crates/ql-bindings-node/src/lib.rs:519-520`). JSON serialization failure is effectively defensive dead code for engine-produced finite shapes; non-finite floats would become JSON null before `to_string`, but the napi append path rejects them.
