quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-18-w5-d-14-self.md:138:**Subject:** `convert.rs` warns when a cell's row/col exceeds `MAX_ROW`/`MAX_COLUMN` but Quantbook's MAX values match Excel exactly (1048575 / 16383). The warnings are effectively dead code.
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-18-w5-d-14-self.md:142:**Detail:** Since `MAX_ROW = 1_048_575` matches Excel and calamine inherits Excel's limits, no real xlsx file can produce a cell beyond Quantbook's bounds. The bounds-check code path is unreachable in practice.
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-18-w5-d-14-self.md:144:**Recommendation:** Either (a) remove the bounds-check (the storage layer's panic on `put_at` is sufficient defense for the impossible case), or (b) keep the check but acknowledge in a comment that it's defense-in-depth for hand-constructed malformed xlsx.
