quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-16-phase-4.10-pre-review-codex.md:1305:./docs/compat/excel-matrix.md:67:| SUMIF | ⚠️ | 17 | 4.3 V2 | W5-53 + W5-61: supports number/text/bool/blank criteria + comparators `> < >= <= <> =`. **Wildcards `?` / `*` shipped W5-61** (escape with `~`); apply only to Eq/Ne text criteria, only against text cells (not coerced numbers). 2-arg + 3-arg forms; sum_range default to range. Error in sum_range cell propagates (Excel canon). **W5-60 KNOWN DIVERGENCE**: when `sum_range` size differs from `range`, Quantbook does a flat-index zip; Excel anchors the top-left of `sum_range` and uses `range`'s shape, ignoring `sum_range`'s declared extent. Behavior matches only when `sum_range.len() == range.len()`. Pin Phase 4.3 polish or 4.10. |
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-16-phase-4.10-pre-review-codex.md:1357:./docs/audits/2026-05-14-phase-4.7.G-sonnet-review.md:186:`COUNTA` is in `is_aggregate_function` (plan.rs line 279) and the aggregate expansion fires. `counta()` counts all non-blank values: `c = args.iter().filter(|v| !matches!(v, Value::Blank)).count()`. Three values: `Number(1)`, `Text("")`, `Error(NA)` — none are `Blank` → count = 3. (Note: `""` is a `Text("")`, which is NOT `Blank` in the Quantbook type system. Blank is a distinct variant.)
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-16-phase-4.10-pre-review-codex.md:1868:67:| SUMIF | ⚠️ | 17 | 4.3 V2 | W5-53 + W5-61: supports number/text/bool/blank criteria + comparators `> < >= <= <> =`. **Wildcards `?` / `*` shipped W5-61** (escape with `~`); apply only to Eq/Ne text criteria, only against text cells (not coerced numbers). 2-arg + 3-arg forms; sum_range default to range. Error in sum_range cell propagates (Excel canon). **W5-60 KNOWN DIVERGENCE**: when `sum_range` size differs from `range`, Quantbook does a flat-index zip; Excel anchors the top-left of `sum_range` and uses `range`'s shape, ignoring `sum_range`'s declared extent. Behavior matches only when `sum_range.len() == range.len()`. Pin Phase 4.3 polish or 4.10. |
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-16-phase-4.10-pre-review-codex.md:1891:163:| CONCAT | ✅ | 7 | 4.3 polish | W5-61: range-aware variant of CONCATENATE. Accepts ranges (flattens row-major) and scalars. Blanks become empty strings (no skip). Numbers / bools coerce to text representation. Errors propagate (first one returned). Variadic; ≥1 arg required. |
