quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-13-w5-49-50-51-megaudit-sonnet.md:114:- Blank coerces to 0.0 in the ATAN2 implementation (`NumericArg::Skip => 0.0`). This means `ATAN2(0, 0)` where both args are blank returns `#DIV/0!` — which matches the explicit zero-zero check. But `ATAN2(blank, 1)` returns `ATAN2(0, 1) = π/2`, not an error. Excel behavior here varies by version; this may be acceptable but is untested.
quantbook-engine/docs/audits/2026-05-18-phase-4-11-megaudit-opus-c.md:135:`update_original.rs:475-525` introduces a custom `iterate_simple_self_closing` parser for `[Content_Types].xml` `<Override>` / `<Default>` elements. The XML primitives (quick-xml) are already a dependency. The custom impl handles attribute-quote variants by `.find("\"")` and bounds boundaries with `.find("/>")`, with comments explicitly acknowledging "Conservative parser: doesn't handle nested elements or non-self-closing forms".
